        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_295 ;
    neo:h1 "ZEN FLESH, ZEN BONES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h2 "101 ZEN STORIES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h3 "35. Every-Minute Zen"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:id "f106db802e3cb7a0267b29b85e5db80b"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_name "1957_-_Paul_Reps_-_Zen_flesh_zen_bones-A_Collection_of_Zen_and_Pre_Zen_Writings_-_Scan_by_OceanofPDF_dot_com_-_local_converter.md"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_slug "zen-flesh-zen-bones"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:paragraph_number 1 ;
    neo:text "Zen students are with their masters at last ten years before they presume to teach others. Nan-in was visited by Tenno, who, having passed his apprenticeship, had become a teacher. The day happened to be rainy, so Tenno wore wooden clogs and carried an umbrella. After greeting him Nan- in remarked: 'I suppose you left your wooden clogs in the vestibule. I want to know if your umbrella is on the right or left side of the clogs.'"^^xsd:string .

ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1048 a neo:Document ;
    neo:MENTIONS ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1044,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_184,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_31 ;
    neo:h1 "ZEN FLESH, ZEN BONES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h2 "101 ZEN STORIES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h3 "35. Every-Minute Zen"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:id "8e2acc1b86d0260d5bc64ee7c157cd5d"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_name "1957_-_Paul_Reps_-_Zen_flesh_zen_bones-A_Collection_of_Zen_and_Pre_Zen_Writings_-_Scan_by_OceanofPDF_dot_com_-_local_converter.md"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_slug "zen-flesh-zen-bones"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:paragraph_number 2 ;
    neo:text "Tenno, confused, had no instant answer. He realized that he was unable to carry his Zen every minute. He became Nan-in's pupil, and he studied six more years to accomplish his every-minute Zen."^^xsd:string .

ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1049 a neo:Document ;
    neo:MENTIONS ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1050,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1051,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1052,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1053,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_90 ;
    neo:h1 "ZEN FLESH, ZEN BONES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h2 "101 ZEN STORIES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h3 "36. Flower Shower"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:id "d0592ee793cd06f964495893fc6337e9"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_name "1957_-_Paul_Reps_-_Zen_flesh_zen_bones-A_Collection_of_Zen_and_Pre_Zen_Writings_-_Scan_by_OceanofPDF_dot_com_-_local_converter.md"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_slug "zen-flesh-zen-bones"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:paragraph_number 1 ;
    neo:text "Subhuti was Buddha's disciple. He was able to understand the potency of emptiness, the viewpoint that nothing exists accept in its relationship of subjectivity and objectivity."^^xsd:string .

ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_105 a neo:Document ;
    neo:MENTIONS ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_106,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_107,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_108,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_109,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_110,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_111,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_112,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_22 ;
    neo:h1 "ZEN FLESH, ZEN BONES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h2 "101 ZEN STORIES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:id "aa7b198d205e4172e7e0c758351da809"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_name "1957_-_Paul_Reps_-_Zen_flesh_zen_bones-A_Collection_of_Zen_and_Pre_Zen_Writings_-_Scan_by_OceanofPDF_dot_com_-_local_converter.md"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_slug "zen-flesh-zen-bones"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:paragraph_number 2 ;
    neo:text "These stories were transcribed into English from a book called the Shaseki-shu (Collection of Stone and Sand), written late in the thirteenth century by the Japanese Zen teacher Muju (the 'non-dweller), and from anecdotes of Zen monks taken from various books published in Japan around the turn of the present century."^^xsd:string .

ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1054 a neo:Document ;
    neo:MENTIONS ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1050,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1055,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1056,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_400 ;
    neo:h1 "ZEN FLESH, ZEN BONES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h2 "101 ZEN STORIES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h3 "36. Flower Shower"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:id "4e6a054896e997cc96b95470f52d0ba9"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_name "1957_-_Paul_Reps_-_Zen_flesh_zen_bones-A_Collection_of_Zen_and_Pre_Zen_Writings_-_Scan_by_OceanofPDF_dot_com_-_local_converter.md"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_slug "zen-flesh-zen-bones"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:paragraph_number 2 ;
    neo:text "One day Subhuti, in a mood of sublime emptiness was sitting under a tree. Flowers began to fall about him."^^xsd:string .

ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1057 a neo:Document ;
    neo:MENTIONS ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1051,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1058,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1059,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_220 ;
    neo:h1 "ZEN FLESH, ZEN BONES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h2 "101 ZEN STORIES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h3 "36. Flower Shower"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:id "c02a045ed6f97b8fea6bc4c11e0a782d"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_name "1957_-_Paul_Reps_-_Zen_flesh_zen_bones-A_Collection_of_Zen_and_Pre_Zen_Writings_-_Scan_by_OceanofPDF_dot_com_-_local_converter.md"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_slug "zen-flesh-zen-bones"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:paragraph_number 3 ;
    neo:text "'We are praising you for your discourse on emptiness,' the gods whispered to him."^^xsd:string .

ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1060 a neo:Document ;
    neo:MENTIONS ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1050,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1051 ;
    neo:h1 "ZEN FLESH, ZEN BONES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h2 "101 ZEN STORIES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h3 "36. Flower Shower"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:id "e6d069a49d9e5057a96c2c137ab4c6c6"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_name "1957_-_Paul_Reps_-_Zen_flesh_zen_bones-A_Collection_of_Zen_and_Pre_Zen_Writings_-_Scan_by_OceanofPDF_dot_com_-_local_converter.md"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_slug "zen-flesh-zen-bones"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:paragraph_number 4 ;
    neo:text "'But I have not spoken of emptiness,' said Subhuti."^^xsd:string .

ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1061 a neo:Document ;
    neo:MENTIONS ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1050,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1051,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1058,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1062,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_233 ;
    neo:h1 "ZEN FLESH, ZEN BONES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h2 "101 ZEN STORIES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h3 "36. Flower Shower"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:id "ce8163274a8b9f0d915c9a21d87c216f"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_name "1957_-_Paul_Reps_-_Zen_flesh_zen_bones-A_Collection_of_Zen_and_Pre_Zen_Writings_-_Scan_by_OceanofPDF_dot_com_-_local_converter.md"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_slug "zen-flesh-zen-bones"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:paragraph_number 5 ;
    neo:text "'You have not spoken of emptiness, we have not heard emptiness,' responded the gods. This is the true emptiness.' And blossoms showered upon Subhuti as rain."^^xsd:string .

ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1063 a neo:Document ;
    neo:MENTIONS ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1064,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1065,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1066,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_22,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_297,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_31,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_7 ;
    neo:h1 "ZEN FLESH, ZEN BONES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h2 "101 ZEN STORIES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h3 "37. Publishing the Sutras"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:id "c516ec38b444dcef679ac9b92a4087a2"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_name "1957_-_Paul_Reps_-_Zen_flesh_zen_bones-A_Collection_of_Zen_and_Pre_Zen_Writings_-_Scan_by_OceanofPDF_dot_com_-_local_converter.md"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_slug "zen-flesh-zen-bones"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:paragraph_number 1 ;
    neo:text "Tetsugen, a devotee of Zen in Japan, decided to publish the sutras, which at that time were available only in Chinese. The books were to be printed with wood block in an edition of seven thousand copies, a tremendous undertaking."^^xsd:string .

ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1067 a neo:Document ;
    neo:MENTIONS ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1064,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1068,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1069,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1070,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1071,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1072,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1073 ;
    neo:h1 "ZEN FLESH, ZEN BONES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h2 "101 ZEN STORIES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h3 "37. Publishing the Sutras"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:id "44959e9ae89e3d5d114b0d3242c23afb"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_name "1957_-_Paul_Reps_-_Zen_flesh_zen_bones-A_Collection_of_Zen_and_Pre_Zen_Writings_-_Scan_by_OceanofPDF_dot_com_-_local_converter.md"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_slug "zen-flesh-zen-bones"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:paragraph_number 2 ;
    neo:text "Tetsugen began by traveling and collecting donations for this purpose. A few sympathizers would give him a hundred pieces of gold, but most of the time he received only small coins. He thanked each donor with equal gratitude. After ten yens Tetsugen had enough money to begin his task."^^xsd:string .

ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1074 a neo:Document ;
    neo:MENTIONS ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1064,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1075,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1076,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1077,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1078,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1079 ;
    neo:h1 "ZEN FLESH, ZEN BONES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h2 "101 ZEN STORIES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h3 "37. Publishing the Sutras"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:id "3b4b06a5b1627006a509c28cb42ef36f"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_name "1957_-_Paul_Reps_-_Zen_flesh_zen_bones-A_Collection_of_Zen_and_Pre_Zen_Writings_-_Scan_by_OceanofPDF_dot_com_-_local_converter.md"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_slug "zen-flesh-zen-bones"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:paragraph_number 3 ;
    neo:text "It happened that it that time the Uji River overflowed. Famine followed. Tetsugen took the funds he had collected for the book and spent them to save others from starvation. Then he began again his work of collecting."^^xsd:string .

ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1080 a neo:Document ;
    neo:MENTIONS ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1064,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1081,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1082,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_591 ;
    neo:h1 "ZEN FLESH, ZEN BONES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h2 "101 ZEN STORIES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h3 "37. Publishing the Sutras"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:id "c1bdd2076ff227f9bbdb1318b769b2f5"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_name "1957_-_Paul_Reps_-_Zen_flesh_zen_bones-A_Collection_of_Zen_and_Pre_Zen_Writings_-_Scan_by_OceanofPDF_dot_com_-_local_converter.md"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_slug "zen-flesh-zen-bones"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:paragraph_number 4 ;
    neo:text "Several years afterwards an epidemic spread over the country. Tetsugen gave away what he had collected, to help his people."^^xsd:string .

ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1083 a neo:Document ;
    neo:MENTIONS ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1084,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1085,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1086,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_241,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_297 ;
    neo:h1 "ZEN FLESH, ZEN BONES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h2 "101 ZEN STORIES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h3 "37. Publishing the Sutras"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:id "ec1482577cdf0585c827f46cd7fb752f"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_name "1957_-_Paul_Reps_-_Zen_flesh_zen_bones-A_Collection_of_Zen_and_Pre_Zen_Writings_-_Scan_by_OceanofPDF_dot_com_-_local_converter.md"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_slug "zen-flesh-zen-bones"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:paragraph_number 5 ;
    neo:text "For a third time he started his work, and after twenty years his wish was fulfilled. The printing blocks which produced the first edition of sutras can be seen today in the Obaku monastery in Kyoto."^^xsd:string .

ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1087 a neo:Document ;
    neo:MENTIONS ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1064,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1088,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1089,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1090,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_297,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_8 ;
    neo:h1 "ZEN FLESH, ZEN BONES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h2 "101 ZEN STORIES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h3 "37. Publishing the Sutras"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:id "25addce22d051a6f7309423f67fdc35e"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_name "1957_-_Paul_Reps_-_Zen_flesh_zen_bones-A_Collection_of_Zen_and_Pre_Zen_Writings_-_Scan_by_OceanofPDF_dot_com_-_local_converter.md"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_slug "zen-flesh-zen-bones"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:paragraph_number 6 ;
    neo:text "The Japanese tell their children that Tetsugen made three sets of sutras, and that the first two invisible sets surpass even the last."^^xsd:string .

ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1091 a neo:Document ;
    neo:MENTIONS ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1092,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1093,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1094,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_267,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_589 ;
    neo:h1 "ZEN FLESH, ZEN BONES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h2 "101 ZEN STORIES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h3 "38. Gisho's Work"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:id "f755b15db42a4c354a6984338747ac65"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_name "1957_-_Paul_Reps_-_Zen_flesh_zen_bones-A_Collection_of_Zen_and_Pre_Zen_Writings_-_Scan_by_OceanofPDF_dot_com_-_local_converter.md"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_slug "zen-flesh-zen-bones"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:paragraph_number 1 ;
    neo:text "Gisho was ordained as a nun when she was ten years old. She received training just as the little boys did. When she reached the age of sixteen she traveled from one Zen master to another, studying with them all."^^xsd:string .

ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1095 a neo:Document ;
    neo:MENTIONS ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1096,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1097,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1098,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_275 ;
    neo:h1 "ZEN FLESH, ZEN BONES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h2 "101 ZEN STORIES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h3 "38. Gisho's Work"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:id "8add0f0513c2989bc2c597749dc659e1"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_name "1957_-_Paul_Reps_-_Zen_flesh_zen_bones-A_Collection_of_Zen_and_Pre_Zen_Writings_-_Scan_by_OceanofPDF_dot_com_-_local_converter.md"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_slug "zen-flesh-zen-bones"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:paragraph_number 2 ;
    neo:text "She remained three years with Unzan, six years with Gukei, but was unable to obtain a clear vision. At last she went to me master Inzan."^^xsd:string .

ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1099 a neo:Document ;
    neo:MENTIONS ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1098,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1100,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1101,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_213 ;
    neo:h1 "ZEN FLESH, ZEN BONES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h2 "101 ZEN STORIES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h3 "38. Gisho's Work"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:id "5b48ed496f719b87ba2531080a94ecce"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_name "1957_-_Paul_Reps_-_Zen_flesh_zen_bones-A_Collection_of_Zen_and_Pre_Zen_Writings_-_Scan_by_OceanofPDF_dot_com_-_local_converter.md"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_slug "zen-flesh-zen-bones"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:paragraph_number 3 ;
    neo:text "Inzan showed her no distinction at all on account of her sex. He scolded her like a thunderstorm. He cuffed her to awaken her inner nature."^^xsd:string .

ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1102 a neo:Document ;
    neo:MENTIONS ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1092,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1098 ;
    neo:h1 "ZEN FLESH, ZEN BONES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h2 "101 ZEN STORIES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h3 "38. Gisho's Work"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:id "4ddf3ca8d82e77dc38c74faf71b9a809"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_name "1957_-_Paul_Reps_-_Zen_flesh_zen_bones-A_Collection_of_Zen_and_Pre_Zen_Writings_-_Scan_by_OceanofPDF_dot_com_-_local_converter.md"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_slug "zen-flesh-zen-bones"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:paragraph_number 4 ;
    neo:text "Gisho remained with Inzan thirteen years and then she found that which she was seeking!"^^xsd:string .

ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1103 a neo:Document ;
    neo:MENTIONS ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1098,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_329,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_462 ;
    neo:h1 "ZEN FLESH, ZEN BONES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h2 "101 ZEN STORIES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h3 "38. Gisho's Work"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:id "810f1b204b96a32a118223bab3818534"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_name "1957_-_Paul_Reps_-_Zen_flesh_zen_bones-A_Collection_of_Zen_and_Pre_Zen_Writings_-_Scan_by_OceanofPDF_dot_com_-_local_converter.md"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_slug "zen-flesh-zen-bones"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:paragraph_number 5 ;
    neo:text "In her honor, Inzan wrote a poem:"^^xsd:string .

ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1104 a neo:Document ;
    neo:MENTIONS ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_370,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_589 ;
    neo:h1 "ZEN FLESH, ZEN BONES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h2 "101 ZEN STORIES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h3 "38. Gisho's Work"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:id "cfc865b624b6f276dac3af61c56c4cd8"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_name "1957_-_Paul_Reps_-_Zen_flesh_zen_bones-A_Collection_of_Zen_and_Pre_Zen_Writings_-_Scan_by_OceanofPDF_dot_com_-_local_converter.md"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_slug "zen-flesh-zen-bones"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:paragraph_number 6 ;
    neo:text "This nun studied thirteen years under my guidance."^^xsd:string .

ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1105 a neo:Document ;
    neo:MENTIONS ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_205,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_275,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_755 ;
    neo:h1 "ZEN FLESH, ZEN BONES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h2 "101 ZEN STORIES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h3 "38. Gisho's Work"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:id "df079f079905aa494bc59852f6f2b76d"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_name "1957_-_Paul_Reps_-_Zen_flesh_zen_bones-A_Collection_of_Zen_and_Pre_Zen_Writings_-_Scan_by_OceanofPDF_dot_com_-_local_converter.md"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_slug "zen-flesh-zen-bones"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:paragraph_number 7 ;
    neo:text "In the evening she considered the deepest koans,"^^xsd:string .

ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1106 a neo:Document ;
    neo:MENTIONS ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_275,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_755,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_805 ;
    neo:h1 "ZEN FLESH, ZEN BONES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h2 "101 ZEN STORIES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h3 "38. Gisho's Work"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:id "1666d29b05670251ce500d4a8e0f9e4b"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_name "1957_-_Paul_Reps_-_Zen_flesh_zen_bones-A_Collection_of_Zen_and_Pre_Zen_Writings_-_Scan_by_OceanofPDF_dot_com_-_local_converter.md"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_slug "zen-flesh-zen-bones"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:paragraph_number 8 ;
    neo:text "In the morning she was wrapped in other koans."^^xsd:string .

ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1107 a neo:Document ;
    neo:MENTIONS ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1108 ;
    neo:h1 "ZEN FLESH, ZEN BONES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h2 "101 ZEN STORIES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h3 "38. Gisho's Work"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:id "ac613325a9935fb47cbefde31c2ee090"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_name "1957_-_Paul_Reps_-_Zen_flesh_zen_bones-A_Collection_of_Zen_and_Pre_Zen_Writings_-_Scan_by_OceanofPDF_dot_com_-_local_converter.md"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_slug "zen-flesh-zen-bones"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:paragraph_number 9 ;
    neo:text "The Chinese nun Tetsuma surpassed all before her,"^^xsd:string .

ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1110 a neo:Document ;
    neo:MENTIONS ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1092,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1111,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1112 ;
    neo:h1 "ZEN FLESH, ZEN BONES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h2 "101 ZEN STORIES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h3 "38. Gisho's Work"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:id "ec1d04b3d5e5629de68d0f9b23b01cb5"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_name "1957_-_Paul_Reps_-_Zen_flesh_zen_bones-A_Collection_of_Zen_and_Pre_Zen_Writings_-_Scan_by_OceanofPDF_dot_com_-_local_converter.md"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_slug "zen-flesh-zen-bones"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:paragraph_number 10 ;
    neo:text "And since Mujaku none has been so genuine as this Gisho!"^^xsd:string .

ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1113 a neo:Document ;
    neo:MENTIONS ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1114,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_329 ;
    neo:h1 "ZEN FLESH, ZEN BONES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h2 "101 ZEN STORIES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h3 "38. Gisho's Work"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:id "fbd352fcfb9d5b68f546abbd0d22f0f6"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_name "1957_-_Paul_Reps_-_Zen_flesh_zen_bones-A_Collection_of_Zen_and_Pre_Zen_Writings_-_Scan_by_OceanofPDF_dot_com_-_local_converter.md"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_slug "zen-flesh-zen-bones"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:paragraph_number 11 ;
    neo:text "Yet there are many more gates for her to pass through."^^xsd:string .

ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1115 a neo:Document ;
    neo:MENTIONS ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1116,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_275,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_370 ;
    neo:h1 "ZEN FLESH, ZEN BONES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h2 "101 ZEN STORIES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h3 "38. Gisho's Work"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:id "d223c01a6e0193f93205363ec9f30130"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_name "1957_-_Paul_Reps_-_Zen_flesh_zen_bones-A_Collection_of_Zen_and_Pre_Zen_Writings_-_Scan_by_OceanofPDF_dot_com_-_local_converter.md"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_slug "zen-flesh-zen-bones"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:paragraph_number 12 ;
    neo:text "She should receive still more blows from my iron fist."^^xsd:string .

ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1117 a neo:Document ;
    neo:MENTIONS ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1092,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1118,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1119,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1120,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_885 ;
    neo:h1 "ZEN FLESH, ZEN BONES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h2 "101 ZEN STORIES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h3 "38. Gisho's Work"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:id "18f0dad2e0d334a5150b07032baf45a0"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_name "1957_-_Paul_Reps_-_Zen_flesh_zen_bones-A_Collection_of_Zen_and_Pre_Zen_Writings_-_Scan_by_OceanofPDF_dot_com_-_local_converter.md"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_slug "zen-flesh-zen-bones"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:paragraph_number 13 ;
    neo:text "After Gisho was enlightened she went to the province of Banshu, started her own Zen temple and taught two hundred other nuns until she passed away one year in the month of August."^^xsd:string .

ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1121 a neo:Document ;
    neo:MENTIONS ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1122,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1123,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1124,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_251 ;
    neo:h1 "ZEN FLESH, ZEN BONES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h2 "101 ZEN STORIES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h3 "39. Sleeping in the Dayime"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:id "d8cab22104ae573d8110b7c1dacbb8f7"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_name "1957_-_Paul_Reps_-_Zen_flesh_zen_bones-A_Collection_of_Zen_and_Pre_Zen_Writings_-_Scan_by_OceanofPDF_dot_com_-_local_converter.md"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_slug "zen-flesh-zen-bones"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:paragraph_number 1 ;
    neo:text "The master Soya Shaku passed from this world when he was sixty-one years of age. Fulfilling his life's work, he left a great teaching, far richer than that of most Zen masters. His pupils used to sleep in the daytime during midsummer, and while he overlooked this he himself never wasted a minute."^^xsd:string .

ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1125 a neo:Document ;
    neo:MENTIONS ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1126,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1127,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_178 ;
    neo:h1 "ZEN FLESH, ZEN BONES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h2 "101 ZEN STORIES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h3 "39. Sleeping in the Dayime"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:id "65d865ca2474aba6c2fdee8dc01f5661"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_name "1957_-_Paul_Reps_-_Zen_flesh_zen_bones-A_Collection_of_Zen_and_Pre_Zen_Writings_-_Scan_by_OceanofPDF_dot_com_-_local_converter.md"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_slug "zen-flesh-zen-bones"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:paragraph_number 2 ;
    neo:text "When he was but twelve year old he was already studying Tendai philosophical speculation. One summer day the air had been so sultry that Little Soyen stretched his legs and went to sleep while his teacher was away."^^xsd:string .

ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1128 a neo:Document ;
    neo:MENTIONS ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1129,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1130,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_355 ;
    neo:h1 "ZEN FLESH, ZEN BONES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h2 "101 ZEN STORIES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h3 "39. Sleeping in the Dayime"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:id "eb1d43fbb47df8e9221da9fb1d168147"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_name "1957_-_Paul_Reps_-_Zen_flesh_zen_bones-A_Collection_of_Zen_and_Pre_Zen_Writings_-_Scan_by_OceanofPDF_dot_com_-_local_converter.md"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_slug "zen-flesh-zen-bones"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:paragraph_number 3 ;
    neo:text "Three hours passed when, suddenly waking he hard his master enter, but it was too late. There he lay, sprawled across the doorway."^^xsd:string .

ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_113 a neo:Document ;
    neo:MENTIONS ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_114,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_115,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_116,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_117,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_118 ;
    neo:h1 "ZEN FLESH, ZEN BONES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h2 "101 ZEN STORIES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:id "5d70a0b06b3d8f1b2c734714e4aab1df"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_name "1957_-_Paul_Reps_-_Zen_flesh_zen_bones-A_Collection_of_Zen_and_Pre_Zen_Writings_-_Scan_by_OceanofPDF_dot_com_-_local_converter.md"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_slug "zen-flesh-zen-bones"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:paragraph_number 3 ;
    neo:text "For Orientals, more interested in being than in business the self- discovered man has been the most worthy of respect."^^xsd:string .

ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1131 a neo:Document ;
    neo:MENTIONS ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1132,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1133,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_178 ;
    neo:h1 "ZEN FLESH, ZEN BONES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h2 "101 ZEN STORIES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h3 "39. Sleeping in the Dayime"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:id "475a94bf259ee70b827150f452be2f11"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_name "1957_-_Paul_Reps_-_Zen_flesh_zen_bones-A_Collection_of_Zen_and_Pre_Zen_Writings_-_Scan_by_OceanofPDF_dot_com_-_local_converter.md"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_slug "zen-flesh-zen-bones"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:paragraph_number 4 ;
    neo:text "'I beg your pardon, I beg your pardon,' his teacher whispered, stepping carefully over Soyen's body as if it were that of some distinguished guest. After this, Soyen never slept again in the afternoon."^^xsd:string .

ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1134 a neo:Document ;
    neo:MENTIONS ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1135,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1136,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1137,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1138,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1139,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1140,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_526,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_802 ;
    neo:h1 "ZEN FLESH, ZEN BONES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h2 "101 ZEN STORIES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h3 "40. In Dreamland"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:id "b97485d66b20a3567c9456ccb1d33ce4"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_name "1957_-_Paul_Reps_-_Zen_flesh_zen_bones-A_Collection_of_Zen_and_Pre_Zen_Writings_-_Scan_by_OceanofPDF_dot_com_-_local_converter.md"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_slug "zen-flesh-zen-bones"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:paragraph_number 1 ;
    neo:text "'Our schoolmaster used to take a nap every afternoon,' related a disciple of Soyen Shaku. 'We children asked him why he did it and he told us: 'I go to dreamland to meet the old sages just as Confucius did.' When Confucius slept, he would dream of ancient sages and later tell his followers about them."^^xsd:string .

ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1141 a neo:Document ;
    neo:MENTIONS ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1033,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1135,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1136,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1138,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1142 ;
    neo:h1 "ZEN FLESH, ZEN BONES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h2 "101 ZEN STORIES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h3 "40. In Dreamland"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:id "b235407a1ca924941e79fa105a87b809"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_name "1957_-_Paul_Reps_-_Zen_flesh_zen_bones-A_Collection_of_Zen_and_Pre_Zen_Writings_-_Scan_by_OceanofPDF_dot_com_-_local_converter.md"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_slug "zen-flesh-zen-bones"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:paragraph_number 2 ;
    neo:text "'It was extremely hot one day so some of us took a nap. Our schoolmaster scolded us. \"We went to dreamland to meet the ancient sages the same as Confucius did,\" we explained. \"What was the message from those sages?\" our schoolmaster demanded. One of us replied: \"We went to dreamland and met the sages and asked than if our schoolmaster came there every afternoon, but they said they had never seen any such fellow.\""^^xsd:string .

ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1143 a neo:Document ;
    neo:MENTIONS ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_31,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_680 ;
    neo:h1 "ZEN FLESH, ZEN BONES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h2 "101 ZEN STORIES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h3 "41. Joshu's Zen"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:id "9c8d6fae7a6ed2e3825b2aeadb1ad2c2"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_name "1957_-_Paul_Reps_-_Zen_flesh_zen_bones-A_Collection_of_Zen_and_Pre_Zen_Writings_-_Scan_by_OceanofPDF_dot_com_-_local_converter.md"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_slug "zen-flesh-zen-bones"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:paragraph_number 1 ;
    neo:text "Joshu began the study of Zen when he was sixty years old and continued until he was eighty, when he realized Zen."^^xsd:string .

ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1144 a neo:Document ;
    neo:MENTIONS ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1145,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_355 ;
    neo:h1 "ZEN FLESH, ZEN BONES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h2 "101 ZEN STORIES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h3 "41. Joshu's Zen"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:id "0790862a724cb585ecad02e81f55be81"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_name "1957_-_Paul_Reps_-_Zen_flesh_zen_bones-A_Collection_of_Zen_and_Pre_Zen_Writings_-_Scan_by_OceanofPDF_dot_com_-_local_converter.md"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_slug "zen-flesh-zen-bones"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:paragraph_number 2 ;
    neo:text "He taught from the age of eighty until he was one hundred and twenty. A student once asked him: 'If I haven't anything in my mind, what shall I do?'"^^xsd:string .

ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1146 a neo:Document ;
    neo:MENTIONS ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_680 ;
    neo:h1 "ZEN FLESH, ZEN BONES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h2 "101 ZEN STORIES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h3 "41. Joshu's Zen"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:id "182db90df1b6d9815ae33351b10ac7ea"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_name "1957_-_Paul_Reps_-_Zen_flesh_zen_bones-A_Collection_of_Zen_and_Pre_Zen_Writings_-_Scan_by_OceanofPDF_dot_com_-_local_converter.md"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_slug "zen-flesh-zen-bones"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:paragraph_number 3 ;
    neo:text "Joshu replied: 'Throw it out.'"^^xsd:string .

ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1148 a neo:Document ;
    neo:MENTIONS ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1149 ;
    neo:h1 "ZEN FLESH, ZEN BONES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h2 "101 ZEN STORIES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h3 "41. Joshu's Zen"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:id "33c0b9af59c31e13f0aa88939ef00d5e"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_name "1957_-_Paul_Reps_-_Zen_flesh_zen_bones-A_Collection_of_Zen_and_Pre_Zen_Writings_-_Scan_by_OceanofPDF_dot_com_-_local_converter.md"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_slug "zen-flesh-zen-bones"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:paragraph_number 4 ;
    neo:text "'But if I haven't anything how on I throw it out?' continued the questioner."^^xsd:string .

ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1150 a neo:Document ;
    neo:MENTIONS ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_680 ;
    neo:h1 "ZEN FLESH, ZEN BONES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h2 "101 ZEN STORIES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h3 "41. Joshu's Zen"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:id "22523608e0df808c606fc74ba2fe153a"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_name "1957_-_Paul_Reps_-_Zen_flesh_zen_bones-A_Collection_of_Zen_and_Pre_Zen_Writings_-_Scan_by_OceanofPDF_dot_com_-_local_converter.md"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_slug "zen-flesh-zen-bones"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:paragraph_number 5 ;
    neo:text "'Well,' said Joshu, 'then carry it out.'"^^xsd:string .

ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1151 a neo:Document ;
    neo:MENTIONS ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1152,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_178,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_780 ;
    neo:h1 "ZEN FLESH, ZEN BONES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h2 "101 ZEN STORIES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h3 "42. The Dead Man's Answer"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:id "edfef85c58c2f7c8e698eb6bcbef29ac"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_name "1957_-_Paul_Reps_-_Zen_flesh_zen_bones-A_Collection_of_Zen_and_Pre_Zen_Writings_-_Scan_by_OceanofPDF_dot_com_-_local_converter.md"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_slug "zen-flesh-zen-bones"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:paragraph_number 1 ;
    neo:text "When Mamiya, who later became a well-known preacher, went to a teacher for personal guidance, he was asked to explain the sound of one hand."^^xsd:string .

ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1153 a neo:Document ;
    neo:MENTIONS ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1152,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_174,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_178,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_252,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_587,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_778 ;
    neo:h1 "ZEN FLESH, ZEN BONES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h2 "101 ZEN STORIES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h3 "42. The Dead Man's Answer"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:id "d4489268253b8b28777bcbf672881ed4"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_name "1957_-_Paul_Reps_-_Zen_flesh_zen_bones-A_Collection_of_Zen_and_Pre_Zen_Writings_-_Scan_by_OceanofPDF_dot_com_-_local_converter.md"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_slug "zen-flesh-zen-bones"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:paragraph_number 2 ;
    neo:text "Mamiya concentrated upon what the sound of one hand might be. 'You are not working hard enough,' his teacher told him. 'You are too attached to food, wealth, things, and that sound. It would he better if you died. That would solve the problem.'"^^xsd:string .

ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1154 a neo:Document ;
    neo:MENTIONS ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1152,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_178,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_778 ;
    neo:h1 "ZEN FLESH, ZEN BONES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h2 "101 ZEN STORIES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h3 "42. The Dead Man's Answer"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:id "e1d195213ea034264188b7640557dce8"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_name "1957_-_Paul_Reps_-_Zen_flesh_zen_bones-A_Collection_of_Zen_and_Pre_Zen_Writings_-_Scan_by_OceanofPDF_dot_com_-_local_converter.md"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_slug "zen-flesh-zen-bones"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:paragraph_number 3 ;
    neo:text "The next time Mamiya appeared before his teacher he was again asked what he had to show regarding the sound of one hand. Mamiya at once fell over as if he were dead."^^xsd:string .

ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1155 a neo:Document ;
    neo:MENTIONS ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1156,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_312 ;
    neo:h1 "ZEN FLESH, ZEN BONES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h2 "101 ZEN STORIES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h3 "42. The Dead Man's Answer"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:id "2c5ce437b3fc9a81befa97bd30519879"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_name "1957_-_Paul_Reps_-_Zen_flesh_zen_bones-A_Collection_of_Zen_and_Pre_Zen_Writings_-_Scan_by_OceanofPDF_dot_com_-_local_converter.md"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_slug "zen-flesh-zen-bones"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:paragraph_number 4 ;
    neo:text "'You are dead all right' observed the teacher. 'But how about that sound?'"^^xsd:string .

ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1157 a neo:Document ;
    neo:MENTIONS ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1152,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_178 ;
    neo:h1 "ZEN FLESH, ZEN BONES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h2 "101 ZEN STORIES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h3 "42. The Dead Man's Answer"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:id "895d07665fcd3363db8060cb380b776b"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_name "1957_-_Paul_Reps_-_Zen_flesh_zen_bones-A_Collection_of_Zen_and_Pre_Zen_Writings_-_Scan_by_OceanofPDF_dot_com_-_local_converter.md"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_slug "zen-flesh-zen-bones"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:paragraph_number 5 ;
    neo:text "'I haven't solved that yet,' replied Mamiya, looking up. 'Dead men do not speak,' said the teacher.' Get out!'"^^xsd:string .

ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1158 a neo:Document ;
    neo:MENTIONS ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1159,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1160,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_171,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_31 ;
    neo:h1 "ZEN FLESH, ZEN BONES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h2 "101 ZEN STORIES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h3 "43. Zen in a Beggar's Life"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:id "ef0d2258902353daff28c3e37ea3b6ae"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_name "1957_-_Paul_Reps_-_Zen_flesh_zen_bones-A_Collection_of_Zen_and_Pre_Zen_Writings_-_Scan_by_OceanofPDF_dot_com_-_local_converter.md"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_slug "zen-flesh-zen-bones"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:paragraph_number 1 ;
    neo:text "Tosui was a well-known Zen teacher of his time. He had lived in several temples and taught in various provinces."^^xsd:string .

ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1161 a neo:Document ;
    neo:MENTIONS ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1159,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1162,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_305 ;
    neo:h1 "ZEN FLESH, ZEN BONES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h2 "101 ZEN STORIES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h3 "43. Zen in a Beggar's Life"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:id "0b53fbc60f7cc402cfb995f5c378c7ee"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_name "1957_-_Paul_Reps_-_Zen_flesh_zen_bones-A_Collection_of_Zen_and_Pre_Zen_Writings_-_Scan_by_OceanofPDF_dot_com_-_local_converter.md"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_slug "zen-flesh-zen-bones"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:paragraph_number 2 ;
    neo:text "The last temple he visited accumulated so many adherents that Tosui told them he was going to quit the lecture business entirely. He advised them to disperse and to go wherever they desired. After that no one could find any trace of him."^^xsd:string .

ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1163 a neo:Document ;
    neo:MENTIONS ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1159,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1164,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1165,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_241,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_463 ;
    neo:h1 "ZEN FLESH, ZEN BONES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h2 "101 ZEN STORIES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h3 "43. Zen in a Beggar's Life"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:id "12ce8a247693384b8ddabe072f75c61e"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_name "1957_-_Paul_Reps_-_Zen_flesh_zen_bones-A_Collection_of_Zen_and_Pre_Zen_Writings_-_Scan_by_OceanofPDF_dot_com_-_local_converter.md"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_slug "zen-flesh-zen-bones"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:paragraph_number 3 ;
    neo:text "Three years later one of his disciple discovered him living with some beggars under a bridge in Kyoto. He at once implored Tosui to teach him."^^xsd:string .

ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1166 a neo:Document ;
    neo:MENTIONS ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1159 ;
    neo:h1 "ZEN FLESH, ZEN BONES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h2 "101 ZEN STORIES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h3 "43. Zen in a Beggar's Life"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:id "72e44f1a4aa6bc6f2809f9b6ab495027"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_name "1957_-_Paul_Reps_-_Zen_flesh_zen_bones-A_Collection_of_Zen_and_Pre_Zen_Writings_-_Scan_by_OceanofPDF_dot_com_-_local_converter.md"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_slug "zen-flesh-zen-bones"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:paragraph_number 4 ;
    neo:text "'If you can do as I do for even a couple of days, I might,' Tosui replied."^^xsd:string .

ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1167 a neo:Document ;
    neo:MENTIONS ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1159,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1168,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1169,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1170,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1171,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_872 ;
    neo:h1 "ZEN FLESH, ZEN BONES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h2 "101 ZEN STORIES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h3 "43. Zen in a Beggar's Life"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:id "7f5d088e8d4c00448d115234e7675754"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_name "1957_-_Paul_Reps_-_Zen_flesh_zen_bones-A_Collection_of_Zen_and_Pre_Zen_Writings_-_Scan_by_OceanofPDF_dot_com_-_local_converter.md"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_slug "zen-flesh-zen-bones"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:paragraph_number 5 ;
    neo:text "So the former disciple dressed as a beggar and spent a day with Tosui. The following day one of the beggars died. Tosui and his pupil carried the body off at midnight and buried it on a mountainside. After that they returned to their shelter under the bridge."^^xsd:string .

ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1172 a neo:Document ;
    neo:MENTIONS ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1159,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1173,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1174,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_587 ;
    neo:h1 "ZEN FLESH, ZEN BONES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h2 "101 ZEN STORIES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h3 "43. Zen in a Beggar's Life"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:id "0922a5ac8682c498b5e791ab65376fa3"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_name "1957_-_Paul_Reps_-_Zen_flesh_zen_bones-A_Collection_of_Zen_and_Pre_Zen_Writings_-_Scan_by_OceanofPDF_dot_com_-_local_converter.md"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_slug "zen-flesh-zen-bones"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:paragraph_number 6 ;
    neo:text "Tosui slept soundly the remainder of the night, but the disciple could not sleep. When morning came Tosui said: 'We do not have to beg food today. Our dead friend has left some over there.' But the disciple was unable to eat a single bite of it."^^xsd:string .

ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1175 a neo:Document ;
    neo:MENTIONS ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1159 ;
    neo:h1 "ZEN FLESH, ZEN BONES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h2 "101 ZEN STORIES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h3 "43. Zen in a Beggar's Life"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:id "7e5d894853bd62c72ae0791604a6cf8d"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_name "1957_-_Paul_Reps_-_Zen_flesh_zen_bones-A_Collection_of_Zen_and_Pre_Zen_Writings_-_Scan_by_OceanofPDF_dot_com_-_local_converter.md"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_slug "zen-flesh-zen-bones"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:paragraph_number 7 ;
    neo:text "'I have said you could not do as I.' concluded Tosui. 'Get out of here and do not bother me again.'"^^xsd:string .

ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1176 a neo:Document ;
    neo:MENTIONS ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1177,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1178,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1179,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_225,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_297,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_411 ;
    neo:h1 "ZEN FLESH, ZEN BONES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h2 "101 ZEN STORIES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h3 "44. The Thief Who Became a Disciple"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:id "5dd16c3d2d26cb893d724870c8f1ab17"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_name "1957_-_Paul_Reps_-_Zen_flesh_zen_bones-A_Collection_of_Zen_and_Pre_Zen_Writings_-_Scan_by_OceanofPDF_dot_com_-_local_converter.md"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_slug "zen-flesh-zen-bones"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:paragraph_number 1 ;
    neo:text "One evening as Shichiri Kojun was reciting sutras a thief with a sharp sword entered, demanding either his money or his life, Shichiri told him: 'Do not disturb me. You an find the money in that drawer.' Then he resumed his recitation."^^xsd:string .

ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1180 a neo:Document ;
    neo:MENTIONS ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1181,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_355 ;
    neo:h1 "ZEN FLESH, ZEN BONES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h2 "101 ZEN STORIES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h3 "44. The Thief Who Became a Disciple"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:id "ec26cec18bf4b9bc8e85c6f79394e76a"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_name "1957_-_Paul_Reps_-_Zen_flesh_zen_bones-A_Collection_of_Zen_and_Pre_Zen_Writings_-_Scan_by_OceanofPDF_dot_com_-_local_converter.md"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_slug "zen-flesh-zen-bones"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:paragraph_number 2 ;
    neo:text "A little while afterwards he stopped and called: 'Don't take it all. I need some to pay taxes with tomorrow.'"^^xsd:string .

ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1182 a neo:Document ;
    neo:MENTIONS ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1183,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1184,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1185,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1186,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_225 ;
    neo:h1 "ZEN FLESH, ZEN BONES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h2 "101 ZEN STORIES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h3 "44. The Thief Who Became a Disciple"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:id "31bfe6bf8ad2a485273e79e5d4406820"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_name "1957_-_Paul_Reps_-_Zen_flesh_zen_bones-A_Collection_of_Zen_and_Pre_Zen_Writings_-_Scan_by_OceanofPDF_dot_com_-_local_converter.md"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_slug "zen-flesh-zen-bones"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:paragraph_number 3 ;
    neo:text "The intruder gathered up most of the money and started to leave. 'Thank a person when you receive a gift,' Shichiri added."^^xsd:string .

ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1187 a neo:Document ;
    neo:MENTIONS ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_220,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_235 ;
    neo:h1 "ZEN FLESH, ZEN BONES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h2 "101 ZEN STORIES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h3 "44. The Thief Who Became a Disciple"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:id "85d08d162fce3209b98852ca3fe099a7"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_name "1957_-_Paul_Reps_-_Zen_flesh_zen_bones-A_Collection_of_Zen_and_Pre_Zen_Writings_-_Scan_by_OceanofPDF_dot_com_-_local_converter.md"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_slug "zen-flesh-zen-bones"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:paragraph_number 4 ;
    neo:text "The man thanked him and made off."^^xsd:string .

ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1188 a neo:Document ;
    neo:MENTIONS ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1184,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1189,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_225,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_976 ;
    neo:h1 "ZEN FLESH, ZEN BONES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h2 "101 ZEN STORIES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h3 "44. The Thief Who Became a Disciple"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:id "8340812c33959247525988dc41614229"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_name "1957_-_Paul_Reps_-_Zen_flesh_zen_bones-A_Collection_of_Zen_and_Pre_Zen_Writings_-_Scan_by_OceanofPDF_dot_com_-_local_converter.md"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_slug "zen-flesh-zen-bones"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:paragraph_number 5 ;
    neo:text "A few days afterwards the fellow was caught and confessed, among others, the offence against Shichiri. When Shichiri was called as a witness he said: 'This man is no thief, at least as far as I am concerned. I gave him the money and he thanked me for it.'"^^xsd:string .

ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_119 a neo:Document ;
    neo:MENTIONS ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_120,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_121,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_90 ;
    neo:h1 "ZEN FLESH, ZEN BONES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h2 "101 ZEN STORIES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:id "7379b3fff72b39b9bcf95a5167f3566b"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_name "1957_-_Paul_Reps_-_Zen_flesh_zen_bones-A_Collection_of_Zen_and_Pre_Zen_Writings_-_Scan_by_OceanofPDF_dot_com_-_local_converter.md"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_slug "zen-flesh-zen-bones"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:paragraph_number 4 ;
    neo:text "Such a man proposes to open his consciousness just as the Buddha did."^^xsd:string .

ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1190 a neo:Document ;
    neo:MENTIONS ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1184,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1191,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_355 ;
    neo:h1 "ZEN FLESH, ZEN BONES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h2 "101 ZEN STORIES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h3 "44. The Thief Who Became a Disciple"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:id "64b3b9f53bca08f012ace792b2fab776"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_name "1957_-_Paul_Reps_-_Zen_flesh_zen_bones-A_Collection_of_Zen_and_Pre_Zen_Writings_-_Scan_by_OceanofPDF_dot_com_-_local_converter.md"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_slug "zen-flesh-zen-bones"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:paragraph_number 6 ;
    neo:text "After he had finished his prison term, the men went to Shichiri and became his disciple."^^xsd:string .

ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1192 a neo:Document ;
    neo:MENTIONS ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_22,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_294,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_872 ;
    neo:h1 "ZEN FLESH, ZEN BONES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h2 "101 ZEN STORIES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h3 "45. Right and Wrong"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:id "0f5debe35b8314b0531cddb140d4c119"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_name "1957_-_Paul_Reps_-_Zen_flesh_zen_bones-A_Collection_of_Zen_and_Pre_Zen_Writings_-_Scan_by_OceanofPDF_dot_com_-_local_converter.md"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_slug "zen-flesh-zen-bones"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:paragraph_number 1 ;
    neo:text "When Bankei held his seclusion weeks of meditation, pupils from many parts of Japan came to attend. During one of the gatherings a pupil was caught stealing. The matter was reported to Bankei with the request that the culprit be expelled."^^xsd:string .

ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1193 a neo:Document ;
    neo:MENTIONS ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1194,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_294 ;
    neo:h1 "ZEN FLESH, ZEN BONES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h2 "101 ZEN STORIES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h3 "45. Right and Wrong"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:id "e9f6a8dfbcfc922c1f176f2a87544c15"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_name "1957_-_Paul_Reps_-_Zen_flesh_zen_bones-A_Collection_of_Zen_and_Pre_Zen_Writings_-_Scan_by_OceanofPDF_dot_com_-_local_converter.md"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_slug "zen-flesh-zen-bones"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:paragraph_number 2 ;
    neo:text "Bankei ignored the case."^^xsd:string .

ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1195 a neo:Document ;
    neo:MENTIONS ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1196,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1197,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1198,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_294,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_725 ;
    neo:h1 "ZEN FLESH, ZEN BONES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h2 "101 ZEN STORIES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h3 "45. Right and Wrong"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:id "0269e75e2a5978eedfed52e0542b10e2"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_name "1957_-_Paul_Reps_-_Zen_flesh_zen_bones-A_Collection_of_Zen_and_Pre_Zen_Writings_-_Scan_by_OceanofPDF_dot_com_-_local_converter.md"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_slug "zen-flesh-zen-bones"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:paragraph_number 3 ;
    neo:text "Later the pupil was caught in a similar act, and again Bankei disregarded the matter. This angered the other pupils, who drew up a petition asking for the dismissal of the thief, stating that otherwise they would leave in a body."^^xsd:string .

ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1199 a neo:Document ;
    neo:MENTIONS ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1200,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1201,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1202,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_294 ;
    neo:h1 "ZEN FLESH, ZEN BONES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h2 "101 ZEN STORIES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h3 "45. Right and Wrong"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:id "8430043579c4a79466b8624750588a1e"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_name "1957_-_Paul_Reps_-_Zen_flesh_zen_bones-A_Collection_of_Zen_and_Pre_Zen_Writings_-_Scan_by_OceanofPDF_dot_com_-_local_converter.md"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_slug "zen-flesh-zen-bones"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:paragraph_number 4 ;
    neo:text "When Bankei had read the petition he called everyone before him. 'You are wise brothers,' he told them. 'You know what is right and what is not right. You may go somewhere else to study if you wish, but this poor brother does not even know right from wrong. Who will teach him if I do not? I am going to keep him here even if all the rest of you leave.'"^^xsd:string .

ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1203 a neo:Document ;
    neo:MENTIONS ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1204,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1205,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1206,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1207,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_550 ;
    neo:h1 "ZEN FLESH, ZEN BONES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h2 "101 ZEN STORIES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h3 "45. Right and Wrong"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:id "1f9c95a4e88e82d32dcf706f48b26bcf"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_name "1957_-_Paul_Reps_-_Zen_flesh_zen_bones-A_Collection_of_Zen_and_Pre_Zen_Writings_-_Scan_by_OceanofPDF_dot_com_-_local_converter.md"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_slug "zen-flesh-zen-bones"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:paragraph_number 5 ;
    neo:text "A torrent of tears cleansed the face of the brother who had stolen. All the desire to steal had vanished."^^xsd:string .

ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1208 a neo:Document ;
    neo:MENTIONS ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1209,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1210,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1211,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_31,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_40 ;
    neo:h1 "ZEN FLESH, ZEN BONES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h2 "101 ZEN STORIES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h3 "46. How Grass and Trees Become Enlightened"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:id "c60553dd515a1eb8eeab3d4ab2cec729"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_name "1957_-_Paul_Reps_-_Zen_flesh_zen_bones-A_Collection_of_Zen_and_Pre_Zen_Writings_-_Scan_by_OceanofPDF_dot_com_-_local_converter.md"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_slug "zen-flesh-zen-bones"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:paragraph_number 1 ;
    neo:text "During the Kamkura period, Shinkan studied Tendai six years and then studied Zen seven years; then he went to China and contemplated Zen for thirteen years more."^^xsd:string .

ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1212 a neo:Document ;
    neo:MENTIONS ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1209,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1213,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_22 ;
    neo:h1 "ZEN FLESH, ZEN BONES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h2 "101 ZEN STORIES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h3 "46. How Grass and Trees Become Enlightened"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:id "6b770ee4496353c04ee5d5d0e72ad5f1"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_name "1957_-_Paul_Reps_-_Zen_flesh_zen_bones-A_Collection_of_Zen_and_Pre_Zen_Writings_-_Scan_by_OceanofPDF_dot_com_-_local_converter.md"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_slug "zen-flesh-zen-bones"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:paragraph_number 2 ;
    neo:text "When he returned to Japan many desired to interview him and asked obscure questions. But when Shinkan received visitors, which was infrequently, he seldom answered their questions."^^xsd:string .

ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1214 a neo:Document ;
    neo:MENTIONS ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1209,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1215,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1216,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1217,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_503 ;
    neo:h1 "ZEN FLESH, ZEN BONES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h2 "101 ZEN STORIES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h3 "46. How Grass and Trees Become Enlightened"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:id "6f8b9a7e6b86acb1612857912dd240eb"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_name "1957_-_Paul_Reps_-_Zen_flesh_zen_bones-A_Collection_of_Zen_and_Pre_Zen_Writings_-_Scan_by_OceanofPDF_dot_com_-_local_converter.md"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_slug "zen-flesh-zen-bones"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:paragraph_number 3 ;
    neo:text "One day a fifty-year-old student of enlightenment said to Shinkan: 'I have studied the Tendai school of thought since I was a little boy, but one thing in it I cannot understand. Tendai claims that even the grass and trees will become enlightened. To me this seems very strange.'"^^xsd:string .

ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1218 a neo:Document ;
    neo:MENTIONS ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1209,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1219,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1220,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_503 ;
    neo:h1 "ZEN FLESH, ZEN BONES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h2 "101 ZEN STORIES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h3 "46. How Grass and Trees Become Enlightened"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:id "131e224d4d4ea861db1439a0bf7a5763"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_name "1957_-_Paul_Reps_-_Zen_flesh_zen_bones-A_Collection_of_Zen_and_Pre_Zen_Writings_-_Scan_by_OceanofPDF_dot_com_-_local_converter.md"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_slug "zen-flesh-zen-bones"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:paragraph_number 4 ;
    neo:text "'Of what use is it to discuss how grass and trees become enlightened?' asked Shinkan. The question is how you yourself can become so. Did you ever consider that!'"^^xsd:string .

ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_122 a neo:Document ;
    neo:MENTIONS ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_123,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_124 ;
    neo:h1 "ZEN FLESH, ZEN BONES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h2 "101 ZEN STORIES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:id "cfc3f19831b056f6bce87a481b63a785"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_name "1957_-_Paul_Reps_-_Zen_flesh_zen_bones-A_Collection_of_Zen_and_Pre_Zen_Writings_-_Scan_by_OceanofPDF_dot_com_-_local_converter.md"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_slug "zen-flesh-zen-bones"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:paragraph_number 5 ;
    neo:text "These are stories about such self-discoveries."^^xsd:string .

ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1221 a neo:Document ;
    neo:MENTIONS ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1209,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1222 ;
    neo:h1 "ZEN FLESH, ZEN BONES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h2 "101 ZEN STORIES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h3 "46. How Grass and Trees Become Enlightened"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:id "7804dd49b178cd1d91dbb43d942db14e"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_name "1957_-_Paul_Reps_-_Zen_flesh_zen_bones-A_Collection_of_Zen_and_Pre_Zen_Writings_-_Scan_by_OceanofPDF_dot_com_-_local_converter.md"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_slug "zen-flesh-zen-bones"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:paragraph_number 5 ;
    neo:text "'I never thought of it in that way,' marveled the old man. Then go home and think it over,' finished Shinkan."^^xsd:string .

ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1223 a neo:Document ;
    neo:MENTIONS ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1224,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1225,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1226 ;
    neo:h1 "ZEN FLESH, ZEN BONES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h2 "101 ZEN STORIES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h3 "46. The Stingy Artist"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:id "655f0000a3898e01b2a730246d716e93"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_name "1957_-_Paul_Reps_-_Zen_flesh_zen_bones-A_Collection_of_Zen_and_Pre_Zen_Writings_-_Scan_by_OceanofPDF_dot_com_-_local_converter.md"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_slug "zen-flesh-zen-bones"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:paragraph_number 1 ;
    neo:text "Gessen was an artist monk. Before he would start a drawing or painting he always insisted upon being paid in advance and his fees were high. He was known as the 'Stingy Artist'."^^xsd:string .

ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1227 a neo:Document ;
    neo:MENTIONS ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1224,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1228,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1229 ;
    neo:h1 "ZEN FLESH, ZEN BONES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h2 "101 ZEN STORIES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h3 "46. The Stingy Artist"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:id "39c433ab5cd9a09751b5b88be491e25b"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_name "1957_-_Paul_Reps_-_Zen_flesh_zen_bones-A_Collection_of_Zen_and_Pre_Zen_Writings_-_Scan_by_OceanofPDF_dot_com_-_local_converter.md"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_slug "zen-flesh-zen-bones"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:paragraph_number 2 ;
    neo:text "A geisha once gave him a commission for a painting. 'How much can you pay?' inquired Gessen. 'Whatever you charge,' replied the girl, 'but I want you to do the work in front of me.'"^^xsd:string .

ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1230 a neo:Document ;
    neo:MENTIONS ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1224,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1228,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1231 ;
    neo:h1 "ZEN FLESH, ZEN BONES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h2 "101 ZEN STORIES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h3 "46. The Stingy Artist"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:id "a6d7e5e10eef37cac4819de46329b5cc"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_name "1957_-_Paul_Reps_-_Zen_flesh_zen_bones-A_Collection_of_Zen_and_Pre_Zen_Writings_-_Scan_by_OceanofPDF_dot_com_-_local_converter.md"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_slug "zen-flesh-zen-bones"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:paragraph_number 3 ;
    neo:text "So on a certain day Gessen was called by the geisha. She was holding a feast for her patron."^^xsd:string .

ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1232 a neo:Document ;
    neo:MENTIONS ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1224,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1228,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1229,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1231,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1233,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_225 ;
    neo:h1 "ZEN FLESH, ZEN BONES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h2 "101 ZEN STORIES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h3 "46. The Stingy Artist"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:id "abd7eba19f9e5071de760ec2db9440f9"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_name "1957_-_Paul_Reps_-_Zen_flesh_zen_bones-A_Collection_of_Zen_and_Pre_Zen_Writings_-_Scan_by_OceanofPDF_dot_com_-_local_converter.md"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_slug "zen-flesh-zen-bones"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:paragraph_number 4 ;
    neo:text "Gessen with fine brushwork did the painting. When it was completed he asked the highest sum of his time. He received his pay. Then the geisha turned to her patron, saying: 'All this artist wants is money. His paintings are fine but his mind is dirty: money has caused it to become muddy. Drawn by such a filthy mind his work is not fit to exhibit. It is just about good enough for one of my petticoats.'"^^xsd:string .

ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1234 a neo:Document ;
    neo:MENTIONS ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1224,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1235,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1236,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1237,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_275 ;
    neo:h1 "ZEN FLESH, ZEN BONES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h2 "101 ZEN STORIES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h3 "46. The Stingy Artist"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:id "47ff94542cca2fafed6cb3eb69e73162"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_name "1957_-_Paul_Reps_-_Zen_flesh_zen_bones-A_Collection_of_Zen_and_Pre_Zen_Writings_-_Scan_by_OceanofPDF_dot_com_-_local_converter.md"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_slug "zen-flesh-zen-bones"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:paragraph_number 5 ;
    neo:text "Removing her skirt, she then asked Gessen to do another picture on the back of her petticoat."^^xsd:string .

ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1238 a neo:Document ;
    neo:MENTIONS ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1224,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1239 ;
    neo:h1 "ZEN FLESH, ZEN BONES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h2 "101 ZEN STORIES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h3 "46. The Stingy Artist"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:id "4d96419cd6382dc220b59692582a5504"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_name "1957_-_Paul_Reps_-_Zen_flesh_zen_bones-A_Collection_of_Zen_and_Pre_Zen_Writings_-_Scan_by_OceanofPDF_dot_com_-_local_converter.md"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_slug "zen-flesh-zen-bones"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:paragraph_number 6 ;
    neo:text "'How much will you pay?' asked Gessen."^^xsd:string .

ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1240 a neo:Document ;
    neo:MENTIONS ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_346 ;
    neo:h1 "ZEN FLESH, ZEN BONES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h2 "101 ZEN STORIES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h3 "46. The Stingy Artist"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:id "835f65bfec119a3c5b4e527c9cca090c"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_name "1957_-_Paul_Reps_-_Zen_flesh_zen_bones-A_Collection_of_Zen_and_Pre_Zen_Writings_-_Scan_by_OceanofPDF_dot_com_-_local_converter.md"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_slug "zen-flesh-zen-bones"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:paragraph_number 7 ;
    neo:text "'Oh, any amount,' answered the girl."^^xsd:string .

ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1241 a neo:Document ;
    neo:MENTIONS ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1224,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1237,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1242,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1243 ;
    neo:h1 "ZEN FLESH, ZEN BONES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h2 "101 ZEN STORIES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h3 "46. The Stingy Artist"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:id "f38f648395864d574c878e117a59d460"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_name "1957_-_Paul_Reps_-_Zen_flesh_zen_bones-A_Collection_of_Zen_and_Pre_Zen_Writings_-_Scan_by_OceanofPDF_dot_com_-_local_converter.md"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_slug "zen-flesh-zen-bones"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:paragraph_number 8 ;
    neo:text "Gessen named a fancy price, painted the picture in the manner requested and went away."^^xsd:string .

ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1244 a neo:Document ;
    neo:MENTIONS ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1224,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_225 ;
    neo:h1 "ZEN FLESH, ZEN BONES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h2 "101 ZEN STORIES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h3 "46. The Stingy Artist"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:id "ce216d9715401bbea0611ce274926346"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_name "1957_-_Paul_Reps_-_Zen_flesh_zen_bones-A_Collection_of_Zen_and_Pre_Zen_Writings_-_Scan_by_OceanofPDF_dot_com_-_local_converter.md"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_slug "zen-flesh-zen-bones"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:paragraph_number 9 ;
    neo:text "It was learned later that Gessen had these reasons for desiring money."^^xsd:string .

ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1245 a neo:Document ;
    neo:MENTIONS ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1076,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1224,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1246,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1247,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1248,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1249,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1250 ;
    neo:h1 "ZEN FLESH, ZEN BONES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h2 "101 ZEN STORIES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h3 "46. The Stingy Artist"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:id "8ffd477f15e744ae34a5d832ae90eca4"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_name "1957_-_Paul_Reps_-_Zen_flesh_zen_bones-A_Collection_of_Zen_and_Pre_Zen_Writings_-_Scan_by_OceanofPDF_dot_com_-_local_converter.md"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_slug "zen-flesh-zen-bones"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:paragraph_number 10 ;
    neo:text "A ravaging famine often visited his province. The rich would not help the poor, so Gessen had a secret warehouse, unknown to anyone, which he kept filled with grain prepared for these emergencies."^^xsd:string .

ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_125 a neo:Document ;
    neo:MENTIONS ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_109,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_123,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_126,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_127,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_128 ;
    neo:h1 "ZEN FLESH, ZEN BONES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h2 "101 ZEN STORIES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:id "3df50ea4ef2c0905853dda83ee1f159b"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_name "1957_-_Paul_Reps_-_Zen_flesh_zen_bones-A_Collection_of_Zen_and_Pre_Zen_Writings_-_Scan_by_OceanofPDF_dot_com_-_local_converter.md"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_slug "zen-flesh-zen-bones"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:paragraph_number 6 ;
    neo:text "The following is adapted from the preface to the first edition of these stories in English."^^xsd:string .

ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1251 a neo:Document ;
    neo:MENTIONS ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1252,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1253,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1254,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1255,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1256,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1257,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_355 ;
    neo:h1 "ZEN FLESH, ZEN BONES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h2 "101 ZEN STORIES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h3 "46. The Stingy Artist"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:id "52bd37f597a99b78307de4ff4b2581d5"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_name "1957_-_Paul_Reps_-_Zen_flesh_zen_bones-A_Collection_of_Zen_and_Pre_Zen_Writings_-_Scan_by_OceanofPDF_dot_com_-_local_converter.md"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_slug "zen-flesh-zen-bones"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:paragraph_number 11 ;
    neo:text "From his village to the National Shrine the road was in very poor condition and many travelers suffered while traversing it. He desired to build a better road."^^xsd:string .

ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1258 a neo:Document ;
    neo:MENTIONS ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1224,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_178,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_391 ;
    neo:h1 "ZEN FLESH, ZEN BONES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h2 "101 ZEN STORIES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h3 "46. The Stingy Artist"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:id "9467f346524fd228e01c734fa178d9bb"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_name "1957_-_Paul_Reps_-_Zen_flesh_zen_bones-A_Collection_of_Zen_and_Pre_Zen_Writings_-_Scan_by_OceanofPDF_dot_com_-_local_converter.md"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_slug "zen-flesh-zen-bones"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:paragraph_number 12 ;
    neo:text "His teacher had passed away without realizing his wish build a temple and Gessen wished to complete this temple for him."^^xsd:string .

ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1259 a neo:Document ;
    neo:MENTIONS ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1224,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1260,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1261,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1262,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1263 ;
    neo:h1 "ZEN FLESH, ZEN BONES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h2 "101 ZEN STORIES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h3 "46. The Stingy Artist"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:id "4f636a99d6a27a1f01dbac8c1bc180e5"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_name "1957_-_Paul_Reps_-_Zen_flesh_zen_bones-A_Collection_of_Zen_and_Pre_Zen_Writings_-_Scan_by_OceanofPDF_dot_com_-_local_converter.md"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_slug "zen-flesh-zen-bones"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:paragraph_number 13 ;
    neo:text "After Gessen had accomplished his three wishes he threw away his brushes and artist's materials and retiring to the mountains never painted again."^^xsd:string .

ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1264 a neo:Document ;
    neo:MENTIONS ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1265,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1266,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1267,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1268 ;
    neo:h1 "ZEN FLESH, ZEN BONES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h2 "101 ZEN STORIES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h3 "47. Accurate Proportion"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:id "3a21825dec78eaf4f5da7be34952ee0b"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_name "1957_-_Paul_Reps_-_Zen_flesh_zen_bones-A_Collection_of_Zen_and_Pre_Zen_Writings_-_Scan_by_OceanofPDF_dot_com_-_local_converter.md"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_slug "zen-flesh-zen-bones"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:paragraph_number 1 ;
    neo:text "Sen no Rikyu, a tea-master, wished to hang a flower basket on a column. He asked a carpenter to help him, directing the man to place it a little higher or lower, to the right or left, until he had found exactly the right spot. That's the place,' said Sen no Rikyu finally."^^xsd:string .

ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1269 a neo:Document ;
    neo:MENTIONS ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1270,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1271,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1272,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_76 ;
    neo:h1 "ZEN FLESH, ZEN BONES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h2 "101 ZEN STORIES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h3 "47. Accurate Proportion"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:id "b8b67aa5e5b30196f0ff880a5f3865b1"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_name "1957_-_Paul_Reps_-_Zen_flesh_zen_bones-A_Collection_of_Zen_and_Pre_Zen_Writings_-_Scan_by_OceanofPDF_dot_com_-_local_converter.md"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_slug "zen-flesh-zen-bones"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:paragraph_number 2 ;
    neo:text "The carpenter, to test the master, marked the spot and then pretended he had forgotten. Was this the place? 'Was this the place, perhaps?' the carpenter kept asking, pointing to various places on the column."^^xsd:string .

ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1273 a neo:Document ;
    neo:MENTIONS ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1266,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1274,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1275,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1276 ;
    neo:h1 "ZEN FLESH, ZEN BONES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h2 "101 ZEN STORIES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h3 "47. Accurate Proportion"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:id "143130ffc9234d11338c85cb6af2b53e"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_name "1957_-_Paul_Reps_-_Zen_flesh_zen_bones-A_Collection_of_Zen_and_Pre_Zen_Writings_-_Scan_by_OceanofPDF_dot_com_-_local_converter.md"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_slug "zen-flesh-zen-bones"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:paragraph_number 3 ;
    neo:text "But so accurate was the tea-master's sense of proportion that it was not until the carpenter reached the identical spot again that its location was approved."^^xsd:string .

ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1277 a neo:Document ;
    neo:MENTIONS ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1278,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1279,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_503,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_589,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_90 ;
    neo:h1 "ZEN FLESH, ZEN BONES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h2 "101 ZEN STORIES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h3 "48. Black-Nosed Buddha"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:id "c3ea75129f302dddb57b945ad0c70620"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_name "1957_-_Paul_Reps_-_Zen_flesh_zen_bones-A_Collection_of_Zen_and_Pre_Zen_Writings_-_Scan_by_OceanofPDF_dot_com_-_local_converter.md"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_slug "zen-flesh-zen-bones"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:paragraph_number 1 ;
    neo:text "A nun who was searching for enlightenment made a statue of Buddha and covered it with gold leaf. Wherever she went she carried this golden Buddha with her."^^xsd:string .

ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1280 a neo:Document ;
    neo:MENTIONS ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1281,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1282,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1283,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1284,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_227,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_849 ;
    neo:h1 "ZEN FLESH, ZEN BONES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h2 "101 ZEN STORIES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h3 "48. Black-Nosed Buddha"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:id "d2ebbb414f47a212c98b906cd60c974d"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_name "1957_-_Paul_Reps_-_Zen_flesh_zen_bones-A_Collection_of_Zen_and_Pre_Zen_Writings_-_Scan_by_OceanofPDF_dot_com_-_local_converter.md"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_slug "zen-flesh-zen-bones"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:paragraph_number 2 ;
    neo:text "Years passed and, still carrying her Buddha, the nun came to live in a small temple in a country where there were many Buddha's, each one with its own particular shrine."^^xsd:string .

ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1285 a neo:Document ;
    neo:MENTIONS ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1286,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1287,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1288,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1289,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1290,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_807,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_849 ;
    neo:h1 "ZEN FLESH, ZEN BONES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h2 "101 ZEN STORIES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h3 "48. Black-Nosed Buddha"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:id "355aab257d551962a8c089829d758c11"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_name "1957_-_Paul_Reps_-_Zen_flesh_zen_bones-A_Collection_of_Zen_and_Pre_Zen_Writings_-_Scan_by_OceanofPDF_dot_com_-_local_converter.md"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_slug "zen-flesh-zen-bones"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:paragraph_number 3 ;
    neo:text "The nun wished to burn incense before her golden Buddha. Not liking the idea of the perfume straying to the others, she devised a funnel through which the smoke would ascend only to her statue. This blackened the nose of the Golden Buddha making it especially ugly."^^xsd:string .

ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_129 a neo:Document ;
    neo:MENTIONS ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_130,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_22,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_30,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_31,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_39,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_40 ;
    neo:h1 "ZEN FLESH, ZEN BONES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h2 "101 ZEN STORIES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:id "1762bbb3bab007d2bf3ab141bd2c5c14"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_name "1957_-_Paul_Reps_-_Zen_flesh_zen_bones-A_Collection_of_Zen_and_Pre_Zen_Writings_-_Scan_by_OceanofPDF_dot_com_-_local_converter.md"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_slug "zen-flesh-zen-bones"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:paragraph_number 7 ;
    neo:text "Zen might be called the inner art and design of the Orient. It was rooted in China by Bodhidharma, who came from India in the sixth century, and was carried eastward into Japan by the twelfth century. It has been described as: 'A special teaching without scriptures, beyond words and letters, pointing to the mind essence of man seeing directly into one's nature, attaining enlightenment.'"^^xsd:string .

ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1291 a neo:Document ;
    neo:MENTIONS ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1292,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1293 ;
    neo:h1 "ZEN FLESH, ZEN BONES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h2 "101 ZEN STORIES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h3 "50. Ryonen's Clear Realization"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:id "e042f899f6e8acc7118a21a03f619a5c"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_name "1957_-_Paul_Reps_-_Zen_flesh_zen_bones-A_Collection_of_Zen_and_Pre_Zen_Writings_-_Scan_by_OceanofPDF_dot_com_-_local_converter.md"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_slug "zen-flesh-zen-bones"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:paragraph_number 1 ;
    neo:text "The Buddhist nun known as Ryonen was born in 1797. She was a granddaughter of the famous Japanese warrior Shingen."^^xsd:string .

ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1294 a neo:Document ;
    neo:MENTIONS ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1295,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1296,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1297,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1298,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1299,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_275 ;
    neo:h1 "ZEN FLESH, ZEN BONES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h2 "101 ZEN STORIES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h3 "50. Ryonen's Clear Realization"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:id "0598fc63d7edd4f50c38504e30008dee"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_name "1957_-_Paul_Reps_-_Zen_flesh_zen_bones-A_Collection_of_Zen_and_Pre_Zen_Writings_-_Scan_by_OceanofPDF_dot_com_-_local_converter.md"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_slug "zen-flesh-zen-bones"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:paragraph_number 2 ;
    neo:text "Her poetical genius and alluring beauty were such that at seventeen she was serving the empress as one of the ladies of the court. Even at such a youthful age fame awaited her."^^xsd:string .

ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1300 a neo:Document ;
    neo:MENTIONS ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1292,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1301,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1302,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_31 ;
    neo:h1 "ZEN FLESH, ZEN BONES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h2 "101 ZEN STORIES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h3 "50. Ryonen's Clear Realization"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:id "7a205bb89285333492fad2bc22b8b39f"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_name "1957_-_Paul_Reps_-_Zen_flesh_zen_bones-A_Collection_of_Zen_and_Pre_Zen_Writings_-_Scan_by_OceanofPDF_dot_com_-_local_converter.md"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_slug "zen-flesh-zen-bones"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:paragraph_number 3 ;
    neo:text "The beloved emperor died suddenly and Ryonen's hopeful dreams vanished. She became acutely aware of the impermanency of life in this world. I was then that she desired to study Zen."^^xsd:string .

ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1303 a neo:Document ;
    neo:MENTIONS ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1292,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1304 ;
    neo:h1 "ZEN FLESH, ZEN BONES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h2 "101 ZEN STORIES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h3 "50. Ryonen's Clear Realization"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:id "68d5afff37a622fc6b710ae7c211646c"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_name "1957_-_Paul_Reps_-_Zen_flesh_zen_bones-A_Collection_of_Zen_and_Pre_Zen_Writings_-_Scan_by_OceanofPDF_dot_com_-_local_converter.md"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_slug "zen-flesh-zen-bones"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:paragraph_number 4 ;
    neo:text "Her relatives disagreed, however, and practically forced her into marriage. With a promise that she might become a nun after she had borne three children. Ryonen assented. Before she was twenty-five she had accomplished this condition."^^xsd:string .

ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1305 a neo:Document ;
    neo:MENTIONS ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1292,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1304,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1306,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1307,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1308,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_201 ;
    neo:h1 "ZEN FLESH, ZEN BONES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h2 "101 ZEN STORIES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h3 "50. Ryonen's Clear Realization"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:id "000d39cd8ca9bb4a29c3b774e558f98b"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_name "1957_-_Paul_Reps_-_Zen_flesh_zen_bones-A_Collection_of_Zen_and_Pre_Zen_Writings_-_Scan_by_OceanofPDF_dot_com_-_local_converter.md"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_slug "zen-flesh-zen-bones"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:paragraph_number 5 ;
    neo:text "Then her husband and relatives could no longer dissuade her from her desire. She shaved her had took the name of Ryonen which means to realize clearly, and stated on her pilgrimage. She came to the city of Edo and asked Tetsugyu to accept her as a disciple. At one glance the master rejected her because she was too beautiful."^^xsd:string .

ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1309 a neo:Document ;
    neo:MENTIONS ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1292,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1310,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1311,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1312 ;
    neo:h1 "ZEN FLESH, ZEN BONES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h2 "101 ZEN STORIES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h3 "50. Ryonen's Clear Realization"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:id "48b0a21348b81f1fee4abb63b78852ee"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_name "1957_-_Paul_Reps_-_Zen_flesh_zen_bones-A_Collection_of_Zen_and_Pre_Zen_Writings_-_Scan_by_OceanofPDF_dot_com_-_local_converter.md"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_slug "zen-flesh-zen-bones"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:paragraph_number 6 ;
    neo:text "Ryonen then went to another master, Hakuo. Hakuo refused her for the same reason, saying that her beauty would only make trouble. Ryonen obtained a hot iron and placed it against her face. In a few moments her beauty had vanished forever."^^xsd:string .

ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_131 a neo:Document ;
    neo:MENTIONS ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_132,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_133,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_134,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_135,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_136,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_137,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_31,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_40,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_90 ;
    neo:h1 "ZEN FLESH, ZEN BONES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h2 "101 ZEN STORIES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:id "2e05daf1ae85b84f9cb1fa0fa63a894f"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_name "1957_-_Paul_Reps_-_Zen_flesh_zen_bones-A_Collection_of_Zen_and_Pre_Zen_Writings_-_Scan_by_OceanofPDF_dot_com_-_local_converter.md"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_slug "zen-flesh-zen-bones"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:paragraph_number 8 ;
    neo:text "Zen was known as Ch'an in China. The Ch'an-Zen masters, instead of being followers of the Buddha, aspire to be his friends and to place themselves in the same responsive relationship with the universe, as did Buddha and Jesus. Zen is not a sect but an experience."^^xsd:string .

ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1313 a neo:Document ;
    neo:MENTIONS ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1310,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_329 ;
    neo:h1 "ZEN FLESH, ZEN BONES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h2 "101 ZEN STORIES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h3 "50. Ryonen's Clear Realization"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:id "33b2ea67c002151b82fa0af93b888fdf"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_name "1957_-_Paul_Reps_-_Zen_flesh_zen_bones-A_Collection_of_Zen_and_Pre_Zen_Writings_-_Scan_by_OceanofPDF_dot_com_-_local_converter.md"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_slug "zen-flesh-zen-bones"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:paragraph_number 7 ;
    neo:text "Hakuo then accepted her as a disciple."^^xsd:string .

ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1314 a neo:Document ;
    neo:MENTIONS ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1292,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1315,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_462 ;
    neo:h1 "ZEN FLESH, ZEN BONES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h2 "101 ZEN STORIES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h3 "50. Ryonen's Clear Realization"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:id "6121517621e9f9355749cedae00141f6"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_name "1957_-_Paul_Reps_-_Zen_flesh_zen_bones-A_Collection_of_Zen_and_Pre_Zen_Writings_-_Scan_by_OceanofPDF_dot_com_-_local_converter.md"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_slug "zen-flesh-zen-bones"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:paragraph_number 8 ;
    neo:text "Commemorating this occasion. Ryonen wrote a poem on the back of a little mirror:"^^xsd:string .

ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1316 a neo:Document ;
    neo:MENTIONS ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1295,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1317,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_370,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_807 ;
    neo:h1 "ZEN FLESH, ZEN BONES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h2 "101 ZEN STORIES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h3 "50. Ryonen's Clear Realization"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:id "9f78f0ae2a844935c62727746e7578c7"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_name "1957_-_Paul_Reps_-_Zen_flesh_zen_bones-A_Collection_of_Zen_and_Pre_Zen_Writings_-_Scan_by_OceanofPDF_dot_com_-_local_converter.md"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_slug "zen-flesh-zen-bones"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:paragraph_number 9 ;
    neo:text "In the service of my Empress I burned incense to perfume my exquisite clothes,"^^xsd:string .

ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1318 a neo:Document ;
    neo:MENTIONS ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1319,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_370,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_885 ;
    neo:h1 "ZEN FLESH, ZEN BONES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h2 "101 ZEN STORIES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h3 "50. Ryonen's Clear Realization"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:id "499f9fec68eb08f9daeed4cf0edac60f"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_name "1957_-_Paul_Reps_-_Zen_flesh_zen_bones-A_Collection_of_Zen_and_Pre_Zen_Writings_-_Scan_by_OceanofPDF_dot_com_-_local_converter.md"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_slug "zen-flesh-zen-bones"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:paragraph_number 10 ;
    neo:text "Now as a homeless mendicant I burn my face to enter a Zen temple."^^xsd:string .

ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1320 a neo:Document ;
    neo:MENTIONS ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1292,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_462 ;
    neo:h1 "ZEN FLESH, ZEN BONES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h2 "101 ZEN STORIES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h3 "50. Ryonen's Clear Realization"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:id "aba226c1a0d8b1e0d708b2631b832f09"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_name "1957_-_Paul_Reps_-_Zen_flesh_zen_bones-A_Collection_of_Zen_and_Pre_Zen_Writings_-_Scan_by_OceanofPDF_dot_com_-_local_converter.md"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_slug "zen-flesh-zen-bones"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:paragraph_number 11 ;
    neo:text "When Ryonen was about to pass from this world she wrote another poem:"^^xsd:string .

ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1321 a neo:Document ;
    neo:MENTIONS ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1322,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1323,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1324 ;
    neo:h1 "ZEN FLESH, ZEN BONES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h2 "101 ZEN STORIES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h3 "50. Ryonen's Clear Realization"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:id "0b577f754b4447c09a971becbcc3b1ea"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_name "1957_-_Paul_Reps_-_Zen_flesh_zen_bones-A_Collection_of_Zen_and_Pre_Zen_Writings_-_Scan_by_OceanofPDF_dot_com_-_local_converter.md"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_slug "zen-flesh-zen-bones"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:paragraph_number 12 ;
    neo:text "Sixty-six times have these eyes beheld the changing scene of autumn."^^xsd:string .

ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1325 a neo:Document ;
    neo:MENTIONS ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1326,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_370 ;
    neo:h1 "ZEN FLESH, ZEN BONES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h2 "101 ZEN STORIES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h3 "50. Ryonen's Clear Realization"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:id "b386387ec3a2683c2be9753c3cf8442f"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_name "1957_-_Paul_Reps_-_Zen_flesh_zen_bones-A_Collection_of_Zen_and_Pre_Zen_Writings_-_Scan_by_OceanofPDF_dot_com_-_local_converter.md"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_slug "zen-flesh-zen-bones"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:paragraph_number 13 ;
    neo:text "I have had enough about moonlight,"^^xsd:string .

ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1327 a neo:Document ;
    neo:MENTIONS ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1328,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1329,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_788,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_928 ;
    neo:h1 "ZEN FLESH, ZEN BONES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h2 "101 ZEN STORIES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h3 "50. Ryonen's Clear Realization"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:id "7da00efee9ad09fad0a631f4662155d6"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_name "1957_-_Paul_Reps_-_Zen_flesh_zen_bones-A_Collection_of_Zen_and_Pre_Zen_Writings_-_Scan_by_OceanofPDF_dot_com_-_local_converter.md"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_slug "zen-flesh-zen-bones"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:paragraph_number 14 ;
    neo:text "Ask no more. Only listen to the voice of pines and cedars when no wind stirs."^^xsd:string .

ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1330 a neo:Document ;
    neo:MENTIONS ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1331,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1332,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1333,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1334,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1335,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1336,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1337,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_294 ;
    neo:h1 "ZEN FLESH, ZEN BONES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h2 "101 ZEN STORIES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h3 "51. Sour Miso"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:id "abf341cfc5594dcf869555728d67b963"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_name "1957_-_Paul_Reps_-_Zen_flesh_zen_bones-A_Collection_of_Zen_and_Pre_Zen_Writings_-_Scan_by_OceanofPDF_dot_com_-_local_converter.md"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_slug "zen-flesh-zen-bones"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:paragraph_number 1 ;
    neo:text "The cook monk Dairyo, at Bankei's monastery, decided that he would take good care of his old teacher's health and give him only fresh miso, a paste of soy beans mixed with wheat and yeast that often ferments. Bankei, noticing that he was being served better miso than his pupils, asked: 'Who is the cook today?'"^^xsd:string .

ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1338 a neo:Document ;
    neo:MENTIONS ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1331,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1339,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1340,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1341,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_294,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_771 ;
    neo:h1 "ZEN FLESH, ZEN BONES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h2 "101 ZEN STORIES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h3 "51. Sour Miso"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:id "4cba01c773ef995b9b3d367b7707b1a0"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_name "1957_-_Paul_Reps_-_Zen_flesh_zen_bones-A_Collection_of_Zen_and_Pre_Zen_Writings_-_Scan_by_OceanofPDF_dot_com_-_local_converter.md"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_slug "zen-flesh-zen-bones"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:paragraph_number 2 ;
    neo:text "Dairyo was sent before him. Bankei learned that according to his age and position he should eat only fresh miso. So he said to the cook: Then you think I shouldn't eat at all.' With this he entered his room and locked the door."^^xsd:string .

ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1342 a neo:Document ;
    neo:MENTIONS ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1331,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_294 ;
    neo:h1 "ZEN FLESH, ZEN BONES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h2 "101 ZEN STORIES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h3 "51. Sour Miso"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:id "319723f8e2b602bfb23dc317a2c43ce1"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_name "1957_-_Paul_Reps_-_Zen_flesh_zen_bones-A_Collection_of_Zen_and_Pre_Zen_Writings_-_Scan_by_OceanofPDF_dot_com_-_local_converter.md"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_slug "zen-flesh-zen-bones"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:paragraph_number 3 ;
    neo:text "Dairyo, sitting outside the door, asked his teacher's pardon. Bankei would not answer. For seven days Dairyo sit outside and Bankei within."^^xsd:string .

ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1343 a neo:Document ;
    neo:MENTIONS ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1015,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_294 ;
    neo:h1 "ZEN FLESH, ZEN BONES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h2 "101 ZEN STORIES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h3 "51. Sour Miso"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:id "d01b3f671f3a093839a79a050ed99316"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_name "1957_-_Paul_Reps_-_Zen_flesh_zen_bones-A_Collection_of_Zen_and_Pre_Zen_Writings_-_Scan_by_OceanofPDF_dot_com_-_local_converter.md"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_slug "zen-flesh-zen-bones"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:paragraph_number 4 ;
    neo:text "Finally in desperation an adherent called loudly to Bankei: 'You may be all right old teacher, but this young disciple here has to eat. He cannot go without food forever!'"^^xsd:string .

ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1344 a neo:Document ;
    neo:MENTIONS ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1331,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_294 ;
    neo:h1 "ZEN FLESH, ZEN BONES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h2 "101 ZEN STORIES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h3 "51. Sour Miso"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:id "52b8e88f47b5e9e48f1f0aa576361f82"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_name "1957_-_Paul_Reps_-_Zen_flesh_zen_bones-A_Collection_of_Zen_and_Pre_Zen_Writings_-_Scan_by_OceanofPDF_dot_com_-_local_converter.md"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_slug "zen-flesh-zen-bones"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:paragraph_number 5 ;
    neo:text "At that Bankei opened the door. He was smiling. He told Dairyo: 'I insist on eating the same food as the least of my followers. When you become the teacher I do not want you to forget this.'"^^xsd:string .

ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1345 a neo:Document ;
    neo:MENTIONS ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1211,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_31,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_480,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_630,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_633 ;
    neo:h1 "ZEN FLESH, ZEN BONES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h2 "101 ZEN STORIES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h3 "52. Your Light may go out"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:id "636dad85c30cb43aee5c527b5733c302"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_name "1957_-_Paul_Reps_-_Zen_flesh_zen_bones-A_Collection_of_Zen_and_Pre_Zen_Writings_-_Scan_by_OceanofPDF_dot_com_-_local_converter.md"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_slug "zen-flesh-zen-bones"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:paragraph_number 1 ;
    neo:text "A student of Tendai a philosophical school of Buddhism, came to the Zen abode of Gasan as a pupil. When he was departing a few years later, Gasan warned him: 'Studying the truth speculatively is useful as a way of collecting preaching material. But remember that unless you meditate constantly your light of truth may go out.'"^^xsd:string .

ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1346 a neo:Document ;
    neo:MENTIONS ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1347,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1348,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1349,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1350,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1351,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_201 ;
    neo:h1 "ZEN FLESH, ZEN BONES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h2 "101 ZEN STORIES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h3 "53. The Giver Should be Thankful"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:id "490859d28a3b75dcca957c41994c5795"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_name "1957_-_Paul_Reps_-_Zen_flesh_zen_bones-A_Collection_of_Zen_and_Pre_Zen_Writings_-_Scan_by_OceanofPDF_dot_com_-_local_converter.md"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_slug "zen-flesh-zen-bones"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:paragraph_number 1 ;
    neo:text "While Seisetsu was the master of Engaku in Kamakura he required larger quarters, since those in which he was teaching were overcrowded. Umezu Seibei, a merchant of Edo, decided to donate five hundred pieces of gold called ryo toward the construction of a more commodious school. This money he brought to the teacher."^^xsd:string .

ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1352 a neo:Document ;
    neo:MENTIONS ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1347 ;
    neo:h1 "ZEN FLESH, ZEN BONES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h2 "101 ZEN STORIES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h3 "53. The Giver Should be Thankful"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:id "b3b6c684177f8e2647a10d74ed86f0ec"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_name "1957_-_Paul_Reps_-_Zen_flesh_zen_bones-A_Collection_of_Zen_and_Pre_Zen_Writings_-_Scan_by_OceanofPDF_dot_com_-_local_converter.md"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_slug "zen-flesh-zen-bones"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:paragraph_number 2 ;
    neo:text "Seisetsu said: 'All right. I will take it.'"^^xsd:string .

ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1354 a neo:Document ;
    neo:MENTIONS ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1347,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1355,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1356,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1357,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1358 ;
    neo:h1 "ZEN FLESH, ZEN BONES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h2 "101 ZEN STORIES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h3 "53. The Giver Should be Thankful"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:id "35745b01239deff4de5d06b47de8b84d"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_name "1957_-_Paul_Reps_-_Zen_flesh_zen_bones-A_Collection_of_Zen_and_Pre_Zen_Writings_-_Scan_by_OceanofPDF_dot_com_-_local_converter.md"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_slug "zen-flesh-zen-bones"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:paragraph_number 3 ;
    neo:text "Umezu gave Seisetsu the sack of gold, but he was dissatisfied with the attitude of the teacher. One might live a whole year on three ryo, and the merchant had not even been thanked for five hundred."^^xsd:string .

ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1361 a neo:Document ;
    neo:MENTIONS ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1355,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1362,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_522 ;
    neo:h1 "ZEN FLESH, ZEN BONES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h2 "101 ZEN STORIES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h3 "53. The Giver Should be Thankful"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:id "58a7be683c412f83f9ccf0a71f8b3f84"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_name "1957_-_Paul_Reps_-_Zen_flesh_zen_bones-A_Collection_of_Zen_and_Pre_Zen_Writings_-_Scan_by_OceanofPDF_dot_com_-_local_converter.md"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_slug "zen-flesh-zen-bones"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:paragraph_number 4 ;
    neo:text "'In that sack are five hundred ryo,' hinted Umezu."^^xsd:string .

ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1363 a neo:Document ;
    neo:MENTIONS ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1347 ;
    neo:h1 "ZEN FLESH, ZEN BONES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h2 "101 ZEN STORIES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h3 "53. The Giver Should be Thankful"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:id "a2e9e83831a5f8a2bd022253eebfb7f7"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_name "1957_-_Paul_Reps_-_Zen_flesh_zen_bones-A_Collection_of_Zen_and_Pre_Zen_Writings_-_Scan_by_OceanofPDF_dot_com_-_local_converter.md"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_slug "zen-flesh-zen-bones"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:paragraph_number 5 ;
    neo:text "\"You told me that before,' replied Seisetsu."^^xsd:string .

ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1364 a neo:Document ;
    neo:MENTIONS ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1355,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1359,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1362,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1365,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_225 ;
    neo:h1 "ZEN FLESH, ZEN BONES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h2 "101 ZEN STORIES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h3 "53. The Giver Should be Thankful"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:id "e13a12f071a6f6c74d95d94a0681e4b8"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_name "1957_-_Paul_Reps_-_Zen_flesh_zen_bones-A_Collection_of_Zen_and_Pre_Zen_Writings_-_Scan_by_OceanofPDF_dot_com_-_local_converter.md"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_slug "zen-flesh-zen-bones"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:paragraph_number 6 ;
    neo:text "'Even if I am a wealthy merchant, five hundred ryo is a lot of money,' said Umezu."^^xsd:string .

ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1366 a neo:Document ;
    neo:MENTIONS ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1347 ;
    neo:h1 "ZEN FLESH, ZEN BONES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h2 "101 ZEN STORIES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h3 "53. The Giver Should be Thankful"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:id "3e23f4976d2b0c092fa1c282c7edcf3a"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_name "1957_-_Paul_Reps_-_Zen_flesh_zen_bones-A_Collection_of_Zen_and_Pre_Zen_Writings_-_Scan_by_OceanofPDF_dot_com_-_local_converter.md"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_slug "zen-flesh-zen-bones"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:paragraph_number 7 ;
    neo:text "'Do you want me to thank you for it?' asked Seisetsu."^^xsd:string .

ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1367 a neo:Document ;
    neo:MENTIONS ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1355 ;
    neo:h1 "ZEN FLESH, ZEN BONES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h2 "101 ZEN STORIES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h3 "53. The Giver Should be Thankful"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:id "c4fc8954f0f6d943fa0444f9a9a94b11"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_name "1957_-_Paul_Reps_-_Zen_flesh_zen_bones-A_Collection_of_Zen_and_Pre_Zen_Writings_-_Scan_by_OceanofPDF_dot_com_-_local_converter.md"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_slug "zen-flesh-zen-bones"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:paragraph_number 8 ;
    neo:text "\"You ought to,' replied Umezu."^^xsd:string .

ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1368 a neo:Document ;
    neo:MENTIONS ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1347,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1369 ;
    neo:h1 "ZEN FLESH, ZEN BONES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h2 "101 ZEN STORIES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h3 "53. The Giver Should be Thankful"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:id "9dafcfbf9b9d1c94b7930b3eacd26151"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_name "1957_-_Paul_Reps_-_Zen_flesh_zen_bones-A_Collection_of_Zen_and_Pre_Zen_Writings_-_Scan_by_OceanofPDF_dot_com_-_local_converter.md"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_slug "zen-flesh-zen-bones"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:paragraph_number 9 ;
    neo:text "'Why should I?' inquired Seisetsu. 'The giver should be thankful.'"^^xsd:string .

ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1370 a neo:Document ;
    neo:MENTIONS ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1371,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1372,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1373,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1374,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1375,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1376,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_242,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_31 ;
    neo:h1 "ZEN FLESH, ZEN BONES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h2 "101 ZEN STORIES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h3 "54. Last Will and Testament"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:id "3cbac8edf7f82add0614e755a934359d"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_name "1957_-_Paul_Reps_-_Zen_flesh_zen_bones-A_Collection_of_Zen_and_Pre_Zen_Writings_-_Scan_by_OceanofPDF_dot_com_-_local_converter.md"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_slug "zen-flesh-zen-bones"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:paragraph_number 1 ;
    neo:text "Ikkyu, a famous Zen teacher of the Ashikaga era, was the son of the emperor. When he was very young, his mother left the palace and went to study Zen in a temple. In this way Prince Ikkyu also became a student. When his mother passed on, she left with him a letter. It read:"^^xsd:string .

ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1377 a neo:Document ;
    neo:MENTIONS ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1371 ;
    neo:h1 "ZEN FLESH, ZEN BONES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h2 "101 ZEN STORIES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h3 "54. Last Will and Testament"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:id "bc65131a952effe4234c0abe936b7114"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_name "1957_-_Paul_Reps_-_Zen_flesh_zen_bones-A_Collection_of_Zen_and_Pre_Zen_Writings_-_Scan_by_OceanofPDF_dot_com_-_local_converter.md"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_slug "zen-flesh-zen-bones"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:paragraph_number 2 ;
    neo:text "To Ikkyu:"^^xsd:string .

ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1378 a neo:Document ;
    neo:MENTIONS ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1379,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1380,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1381,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_261,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_370,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_633 ;
    neo:h1 "ZEN FLESH, ZEN BONES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h2 "101 ZEN STORIES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h3 "54. Last Will and Testament"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:id "ec07d4e5d5ba91a5774a19ecd3be0e52"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_name "1957_-_Paul_Reps_-_Zen_flesh_zen_bones-A_Collection_of_Zen_and_Pre_Zen_Writings_-_Scan_by_OceanofPDF_dot_com_-_local_converter.md"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_slug "zen-flesh-zen-bones"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:paragraph_number 3 ;
    neo:text "I have finished my work in this life and am now returning Into Eternity. I wish you to become a good student and to realize your Buddha-nature. You will know if I am in hell and whether I am always with you or not."^^xsd:string .

ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_138 a neo:Document ;
    neo:MENTIONS ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_130,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_139,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_140,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_141,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_142,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_143,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_144,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_145,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_146,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_147,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_22,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_31 ;
    neo:h1 "ZEN FLESH, ZEN BONES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h2 "101 ZEN STORIES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:id "c90acb0fd9e3001711a985fa5eb74907"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_name "1957_-_Paul_Reps_-_Zen_flesh_zen_bones-A_Collection_of_Zen_and_Pre_Zen_Writings_-_Scan_by_OceanofPDF_dot_com_-_local_converter.md"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_slug "zen-flesh-zen-bones"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:paragraph_number 9 ;
    neo:text "The Zen habit of self-searching through meditation to realize one's true nature, with disregard of formalism, with insistence on self-discipline and simplicity of living, ultimately won the support of the nobility and ruling classes in Japan and the profound respect of all levels of philosophical thought in the Orient."^^xsd:string .

ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1382 a neo:Document ;
    neo:MENTIONS ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1383,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1384,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1385,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1386,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1387,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_165,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_39,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_697,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_90 ;
    neo:h1 "ZEN FLESH, ZEN BONES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h2 "101 ZEN STORIES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h3 "54. Last Will and Testament"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:id "913fe8272c2b2e6884a40199d21bfa3b"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_name "1957_-_Paul_Reps_-_Zen_flesh_zen_bones-A_Collection_of_Zen_and_Pre_Zen_Writings_-_Scan_by_OceanofPDF_dot_com_-_local_converter.md"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_slug "zen-flesh-zen-bones"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:paragraph_number 4 ;
    neo:text "If you become a man who realizes that the Buddha and his follower Bodhidharma are your own servants, you may leave off studying and work for humanity. The Buddha preached for forty-nine years and in all that time found it not necessary to speak one word. You ought to know why. But if you don't and yet wish to, avoid thinking fruitlessly."^^xsd:string .

ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1388 a neo:Document ;
    neo:MENTIONS ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1389 ;
    neo:h1 "ZEN FLESH, ZEN BONES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h2 "101 ZEN STORIES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h3 "54. Last Will and Testament"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:id "6d1da427b4b0ce769441d4d813b42c5a"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_name "1957_-_Paul_Reps_-_Zen_flesh_zen_bones-A_Collection_of_Zen_and_Pre_Zen_Writings_-_Scan_by_OceanofPDF_dot_com_-_local_converter.md"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_slug "zen-flesh-zen-bones"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:paragraph_number 5 ;
    neo:text "Your Mother,"^^xsd:string .

ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1390 a neo:Document ;
    neo:MENTIONS ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1391,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1392,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1393 ;
    neo:h1 "ZEN FLESH, ZEN BONES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h2 "101 ZEN STORIES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h3 "54. Last Will and Testament"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:id "e2e5b76ff1f568529f9e4c0416e627d4"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_name "1957_-_Paul_Reps_-_Zen_flesh_zen_bones-A_Collection_of_Zen_and_Pre_Zen_Writings_-_Scan_by_OceanofPDF_dot_com_-_local_converter.md"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_slug "zen-flesh-zen-bones"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:paragraph_number 6 ;
    neo:text "Not born, not dead."^^xsd:string .

ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1394 a neo:Document ;
    neo:MENTIONS ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1395,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1396 ;
    neo:h1 "ZEN FLESH, ZEN BONES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h2 "101 ZEN STORIES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h3 "54. Last Will and Testament"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:id "bb103438cfabbb869877867832098bd5"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_name "1957_-_Paul_Reps_-_Zen_flesh_zen_bones-A_Collection_of_Zen_and_Pre_Zen_Writings_-_Scan_by_OceanofPDF_dot_com_-_local_converter.md"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_slug "zen-flesh-zen-bones"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:paragraph_number 7 ;
    neo:text "September first."^^xsd:string .

ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1397 a neo:Document ;
    neo:MENTIONS ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1398,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1399,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1400,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1401,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1402,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1403,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1404,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1405,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_480,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_90 ;
    neo:h1 "ZEN FLESH, ZEN BONES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h2 "101 ZEN STORIES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h3 "54. Last Will and Testament"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:id "a068ba1788294262fc306f3e4e165042"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_name "1957_-_Paul_Reps_-_Zen_flesh_zen_bones-A_Collection_of_Zen_and_Pre_Zen_Writings_-_Scan_by_OceanofPDF_dot_com_-_local_converter.md"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_slug "zen-flesh-zen-bones"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:paragraph_number 8 ;
    neo:text "PS. The teaching of Buddha was mainly for the purpose of enlightening others. If you are dependent a any of its methods, you are naught but an ignorant insect. There are 80,000, books on Buddhism and if you should read all of them and still not see your own nature, you will not understand even this letter. This is my will and testament."^^xsd:string .

ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1406 a neo:Document ;
    neo:MENTIONS ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1265,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1407,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1408,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_22,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_735 ;
    neo:h1 "ZEN FLESH, ZEN BONES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h2 "101 ZEN STORIES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h3 "55. The Tea-Master and the Assassin"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:id "2e5e4c31ea4c23a6d6c64ec803e9a0ab"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_name "1957_-_Paul_Reps_-_Zen_flesh_zen_bones-A_Collection_of_Zen_and_Pre_Zen_Writings_-_Scan_by_OceanofPDF_dot_com_-_local_converter.md"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_slug "zen-flesh-zen-bones"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:paragraph_number 1 ;
    neo:text "Taiko, a warrior who lived in Japan before the Tokugawa era, studied Cha- no-yu, tea etiquette, with Sen no Rikyu, a teacher of that aesthetical expression of calmness and contentment."^^xsd:string .

ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1409 a neo:Document ;
    neo:MENTIONS ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1265,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1407,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1410,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1411,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1412,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_188 ;
    neo:h1 "ZEN FLESH, ZEN BONES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h2 "101 ZEN STORIES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h3 "55. The Tea-Master and the Assassin"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:id "bc43f922cd7e5b67a23b37961c507497"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_name "1957_-_Paul_Reps_-_Zen_flesh_zen_bones-A_Collection_of_Zen_and_Pre_Zen_Writings_-_Scan_by_OceanofPDF_dot_com_-_local_converter.md"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_slug "zen-flesh-zen-bones"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:paragraph_number 2 ;
    neo:text "Taiko's attendant warrior Kato interpreted his superior's enthusiasm for tea etiquette as negligence of state affairs, m he decided to kill Sen no Rikyu. He pretended to make a social call upon the tea-master and was invited to drink tea."^^xsd:string .

ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1413 a neo:Document ;
    neo:MENTIONS ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1178,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1408,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1410,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1414,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1415,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_76,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_771 ;
    neo:h1 "ZEN FLESH, ZEN BONES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h2 "101 ZEN STORIES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h3 "55. The Tea-Master and the Assassin"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:id "c1c08a7f7ed3c26b37d6f67c204623e7"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_name "1957_-_Paul_Reps_-_Zen_flesh_zen_bones-A_Collection_of_Zen_and_Pre_Zen_Writings_-_Scan_by_OceanofPDF_dot_com_-_local_converter.md"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_slug "zen-flesh-zen-bones"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:paragraph_number 3 ;
    neo:text "The master, who was well skilled in his art, saw at a glance the warrior's intention, so he invited Kato to leave his sword outside before entering the room for the ceremony, explaining that Cha-no-yu represents peacefulness itself."^^xsd:string .

ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1416 a neo:Document ;
    neo:MENTIONS ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1178,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1408,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1410,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1417,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1418 ;
    neo:h1 "ZEN FLESH, ZEN BONES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h2 "101 ZEN STORIES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h3 "55. The Tea-Master and the Assassin"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:id "a6fea0eba69f505cbbe7f9571789c380"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_name "1957_-_Paul_Reps_-_Zen_flesh_zen_bones-A_Collection_of_Zen_and_Pre_Zen_Writings_-_Scan_by_OceanofPDF_dot_com_-_local_converter.md"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_slug "zen-flesh-zen-bones"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:paragraph_number 4 ;
    neo:text "Kato would wt Isten to this 'I am a warrior,' he said. I always have my sword with me. Cha-no-yu or no Cha-no-yu. I have my sword.'"^^xsd:string .

ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1419 a neo:Document ;
    neo:MENTIONS ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1178,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1265,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_188 ;
    neo:h1 "ZEN FLESH, ZEN BONES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h2 "101 ZEN STORIES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h3 "55. The Tea-Master and the Assassin"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:id "dc6f324179762570231f02e102d0acf0"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_name "1957_-_Paul_Reps_-_Zen_flesh_zen_bones-A_Collection_of_Zen_and_Pre_Zen_Writings_-_Scan_by_OceanofPDF_dot_com_-_local_converter.md"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_slug "zen-flesh-zen-bones"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:paragraph_number 5 ;
    neo:text "'Very well. Bring your sword in and have some tea,' consented Sen no Rikyu."^^xsd:string .

ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1420 a neo:Document ;
    neo:MENTIONS ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1265,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1288,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1418,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1421,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1422,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1423,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1424,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_771 ;
    neo:h1 "ZEN FLESH, ZEN BONES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h2 "101 ZEN STORIES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h3 "55. The Tea-Master and the Assassin"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:id "2767a046acec891d750d8235b99288d4"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_name "1957_-_Paul_Reps_-_Zen_flesh_zen_bones-A_Collection_of_Zen_and_Pre_Zen_Writings_-_Scan_by_OceanofPDF_dot_com_-_local_converter.md"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_slug "zen-flesh-zen-bones"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:paragraph_number 6 ;
    neo:text "The kettle was boiling on the charcoal fire. Suddenly Sen no Rikyu tipped it over. Hissing steam arose filling the room with smoke and ashes. The startled warrior ran outside."^^xsd:string .

ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1425 a neo:Document ;
    neo:MENTIONS ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1178,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1274,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1424,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_188 ;
    neo:h1 "ZEN FLESH, ZEN BONES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h2 "101 ZEN STORIES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h3 "55. The Tea-Master and the Assassin"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:id "9dd3b2da84dca2a7300ebb1bad3b782d"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_name "1957_-_Paul_Reps_-_Zen_flesh_zen_bones-A_Collection_of_Zen_and_Pre_Zen_Writings_-_Scan_by_OceanofPDF_dot_com_-_local_converter.md"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_slug "zen-flesh-zen-bones"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:paragraph_number 7 ;
    neo:text "The tea-master apologized. 'It is my mistake. Come back in and have some tea. I have your sword here covered with ashes and will clean it and give it to you.'"^^xsd:string .

ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1426 a neo:Document ;
    neo:MENTIONS ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1427,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1428 ;
    neo:h1 "ZEN FLESH, ZEN BONES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h2 "101 ZEN STORIES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h3 "55. The Tea-Master and the Assassin"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:id "e11b310ac37d126b5c476daab0386bb5"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_name "1957_-_Paul_Reps_-_Zen_flesh_zen_bones-A_Collection_of_Zen_and_Pre_Zen_Writings_-_Scan_by_OceanofPDF_dot_com_-_local_converter.md"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_slug "zen-flesh-zen-bones"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:paragraph_number 8 ;
    neo:text "In this predicament the warrior realized he could not very well kill the tea-master, so he gave up the idea."^^xsd:string .

ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1429 a neo:Document ;
    neo:MENTIONS ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1371,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1430 ;
    neo:h1 "ZEN FLESH, ZEN BONES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h2 "101 ZEN STORIES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h3 "56. The True Path"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:id "5309cfc805e0e7fbf79a1fc713b7a607"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_name "1957_-_Paul_Reps_-_Zen_flesh_zen_bones-A_Collection_of_Zen_and_Pre_Zen_Writings_-_Scan_by_OceanofPDF_dot_com_-_local_converter.md"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_slug "zen-flesh-zen-bones"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:paragraph_number 1 ;
    neo:text "Just before Ninakawa passed away the Zen master Ikkyu visited him. 'Shall I lead you on Ikkyu asked."^^xsd:string .

ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1431 a neo:Document ;
    neo:MENTIONS ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1430 ;
    neo:h1 "ZEN FLESH, ZEN BONES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h2 "101 ZEN STORIES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h3 "56. The True Path"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:id "7f5c0a59dc838aae97f0e2cac703c001"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_name "1957_-_Paul_Reps_-_Zen_flesh_zen_bones-A_Collection_of_Zen_and_Pre_Zen_Writings_-_Scan_by_OceanofPDF_dot_com_-_local_converter.md"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_slug "zen-flesh-zen-bones"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:paragraph_number 2 ;
    neo:text "Ninakawa replied: 'I came here alone and I go alone. What help could you be to me?'"^^xsd:string .

ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1432 a neo:Document ;
    neo:MENTIONS ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1371,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1433,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1434,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1435 ;
    neo:h1 "ZEN FLESH, ZEN BONES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h2 "101 ZEN STORIES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h3 "56. The True Path"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:id "a962a8f1c4e2abbaea360f3ab8ff9f81"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_name "1957_-_Paul_Reps_-_Zen_flesh_zen_bones-A_Collection_of_Zen_and_Pre_Zen_Writings_-_Scan_by_OceanofPDF_dot_com_-_local_converter.md"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_slug "zen-flesh-zen-bones"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:paragraph_number 3 ;
    neo:text "Ikkyu answered: 'If you think you really come and go, that is your delusion. Let me show you the path on which there is no coming and no going.'"^^xsd:string .

ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1436 a neo:Document ;
    neo:MENTIONS ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1371,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1430,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1437 ;
    neo:h1 "ZEN FLESH, ZEN BONES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h2 "101 ZEN STORIES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h3 "56. The True Path"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:id "a6d3f9f7f3bef4fbe24f8beb5d84716e"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_name "1957_-_Paul_Reps_-_Zen_flesh_zen_bones-A_Collection_of_Zen_and_Pre_Zen_Writings_-_Scan_by_OceanofPDF_dot_com_-_local_converter.md"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_slug "zen-flesh-zen-bones"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:paragraph_number 4 ;
    neo:text "With his words Ikkyu had revealed the path so clearly that Ninakawa smiled and passed away."^^xsd:string .

ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1438 a neo:Document ;
    neo:MENTIONS ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1381,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1439,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1440,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_266 ;
    neo:h1 "ZEN FLESH, ZEN BONES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h2 "101 ZEN STORIES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h3 "57. The Gates of Paradise"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:id "9d32d3b92c29601dfdc74d5f2f285771"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_name "1957_-_Paul_Reps_-_Zen_flesh_zen_bones-A_Collection_of_Zen_and_Pre_Zen_Writings_-_Scan_by_OceanofPDF_dot_com_-_local_converter.md"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_slug "zen-flesh-zen-bones"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:paragraph_number 1 ;
    neo:text "A soldier named Nobushige came to Hakuin, and asked: 'Is there really a paradise and a hell?'"^^xsd:string .

ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1441 a neo:Document ;
    neo:MENTIONS ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_266 ;
    neo:h1 "ZEN FLESH, ZEN BONES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h2 "101 ZEN STORIES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h3 "57. The Gates of Paradise"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:id "2e50aa3bcc23ae8ca4567f2657f921f4"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_name "1957_-_Paul_Reps_-_Zen_flesh_zen_bones-A_Collection_of_Zen_and_Pre_Zen_Writings_-_Scan_by_OceanofPDF_dot_com_-_local_converter.md"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_slug "zen-flesh-zen-bones"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:paragraph_number 2 ;
    neo:text "'Who are you? ' Inquired Hakuin."^^xsd:string .

ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1443 a neo:Document ;
    neo:MENTIONS ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1427,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1444 ;
    neo:h1 "ZEN FLESH, ZEN BONES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h2 "101 ZEN STORIES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h3 "57. The Gates of Paradise"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:id "ae50887703f9dfb5c695f547bc2114c2"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_name "1957_-_Paul_Reps_-_Zen_flesh_zen_bones-A_Collection_of_Zen_and_Pre_Zen_Writings_-_Scan_by_OceanofPDF_dot_com_-_local_converter.md"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_slug "zen-flesh-zen-bones"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:paragraph_number 3 ;
    neo:text "'I am a samurai,' the warrior replied."^^xsd:string .

ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1445 a neo:Document ;
    neo:MENTIONS ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1169,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1446,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1447,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_266 ;
    neo:h1 "ZEN FLESH, ZEN BONES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h2 "101 ZEN STORIES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h3 "57. The Gates of Paradise"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:id "6b66d5aa0fdfb75927efc45ec6bbc283"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_name "1957_-_Paul_Reps_-_Zen_flesh_zen_bones-A_Collection_of_Zen_and_Pre_Zen_Writings_-_Scan_by_OceanofPDF_dot_com_-_local_converter.md"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_slug "zen-flesh-zen-bones"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:paragraph_number 4 ;
    neo:text "'You, a soldier!' exclaimed Hakuin. 'What kind of ruler would have you as his guard? Your face looks like that of a beggar.'"^^xsd:string .

ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1448 a neo:Document ;
    neo:MENTIONS ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1178,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1439,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_266 ;
    neo:h1 "ZEN FLESH, ZEN BONES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h2 "101 ZEN STORIES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h3 "57. The Gates of Paradise"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:id "ae85b215874709b0e1e3e14719ec565d"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_name "1957_-_Paul_Reps_-_Zen_flesh_zen_bones-A_Collection_of_Zen_and_Pre_Zen_Writings_-_Scan_by_OceanofPDF_dot_com_-_local_converter.md"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_slug "zen-flesh-zen-bones"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:paragraph_number 5 ;
    neo:text "Nobushige became so angry that he began to draw his sword, but Hakuin continued: 'So you have a sword! Your weapon is probably much too dull to cut off my head.'"^^xsd:string .

ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1449 a neo:Document ;
    neo:MENTIONS ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1178,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1450,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1451,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_266 ;
    neo:h1 "ZEN FLESH, ZEN BONES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h2 "101 ZEN STORIES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h3 "57. The Gates of Paradise"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:id "d87e05ba2b9b3d04abd3bfe4fa2eb59c"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_name "1957_-_Paul_Reps_-_Zen_flesh_zen_bones-A_Collection_of_Zen_and_Pre_Zen_Writings_-_Scan_by_OceanofPDF_dot_com_-_local_converter.md"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_slug "zen-flesh-zen-bones"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:paragraph_number 6 ;
    neo:text "As Nohushige drew his sword Hakuin remarked: 'Here open the gates of hell!'"^^xsd:string .

ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1452 a neo:Document ;
    neo:MENTIONS ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1178,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1444,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1453,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_333 ;
    neo:h1 "ZEN FLESH, ZEN BONES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h2 "101 ZEN STORIES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h3 "57. The Gates of Paradise"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:id "65a92ba7168fe5ab258ee05d91514094"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_name "1957_-_Paul_Reps_-_Zen_flesh_zen_bones-A_Collection_of_Zen_and_Pre_Zen_Writings_-_Scan_by_OceanofPDF_dot_com_-_local_converter.md"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_slug "zen-flesh-zen-bones"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:paragraph_number 7 ;
    neo:text "At these words the samurai, perceiving the master's discipline, sheathed his sword and bowed."^^xsd:string .

ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1454 a neo:Document ;
    neo:MENTIONS ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1440,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_266 ;
    neo:h1 "ZEN FLESH, ZEN BONES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h2 "101 ZEN STORIES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h3 "57. The Gates of Paradise"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:id "12d1cab9a8298996cc6a08988255f1e4"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_name "1957_-_Paul_Reps_-_Zen_flesh_zen_bones-A_Collection_of_Zen_and_Pre_Zen_Writings_-_Scan_by_OceanofPDF_dot_com_-_local_converter.md"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_slug "zen-flesh-zen-bones"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:paragraph_number 8 ;
    neo:text "'Here open the gates of paradise,' said Hakuin."^^xsd:string .

ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1455 a neo:Document ;
    neo:MENTIONS ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1359,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1456,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1457,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1458,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_495 ;
    neo:h1 "ZEN FLESH, ZEN BONES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h2 "101 ZEN STORIES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h3 "58. Arresting the Stone Buddha"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:id "a70c1a304e7cc60a0edcf777a3a18e26"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_name "1957_-_Paul_Reps_-_Zen_flesh_zen_bones-A_Collection_of_Zen_and_Pre_Zen_Writings_-_Scan_by_OceanofPDF_dot_com_-_local_converter.md"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_slug "zen-flesh-zen-bones"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:paragraph_number 1 ;
    neo:text "A merchant bearing fifty rolls of cotton goods on his shoulder stopped to rest from the heat of the day beneath a shelter when a large stone Buddha was standing. Then he fell asleep, and when he awoke his goods had disappeared. He immediately reported the matter to the police."^^xsd:string .

ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1459 a neo:Document ;
    neo:MENTIONS ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1460,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1461,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1462,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1463 ;
    neo:h1 "ZEN FLESH, ZEN BONES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h2 "101 ZEN STORIES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h3 "58. Arresting the Stone Buddha"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:id "43bf173562ef1c58fe23b952380a3335"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_name "1957_-_Paul_Reps_-_Zen_flesh_zen_bones-A_Collection_of_Zen_and_Pre_Zen_Writings_-_Scan_by_OceanofPDF_dot_com_-_local_converter.md"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_slug "zen-flesh-zen-bones"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:paragraph_number 2 ;
    neo:text "A judge named O-oka opened court to investigate. 'That stone Buddha must have stolen the goods,' concluded the judge."^^xsd:string .

ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1464 a neo:Document ;
    neo:MENTIONS ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1465,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1466,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1467,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_355,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_612 ;
    neo:h1 "ZEN FLESH, ZEN BONES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h2 "101 ZEN STORIES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h3 "58. Arresting the Stone Buddha"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:id "cec7daff1d8036d0e8f49727fe8339f3"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_name "1957_-_Paul_Reps_-_Zen_flesh_zen_bones-A_Collection_of_Zen_and_Pre_Zen_Writings_-_Scan_by_OceanofPDF_dot_com_-_local_converter.md"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_slug "zen-flesh-zen-bones"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:paragraph_number 3 ;
    neo:text "'He is supposed to care for the welfare of the people but he has failed to perform his holy duty. Arrest him'"^^xsd:string .

ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1468 a neo:Document ;
    neo:MENTIONS ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1461,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1463,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1469,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1470,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_495 ;
    neo:h1 "ZEN FLESH, ZEN BONES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h2 "101 ZEN STORIES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h3 "58. Arresting the Stone Buddha"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:id "8a608370dbf57599e9a0bd96deb161ba"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_name "1957_-_Paul_Reps_-_Zen_flesh_zen_bones-A_Collection_of_Zen_and_Pre_Zen_Writings_-_Scan_by_OceanofPDF_dot_com_-_local_converter.md"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_slug "zen-flesh-zen-bones"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:paragraph_number 4 ;
    neo:text "The police arrested the stone Buddha and carried it into the court. A noisy crowd followed the statue; curious to learn what kind of a sentence the judge was about to impose."^^xsd:string .

ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1471 a neo:Document ;
    neo:MENTIONS ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1460,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1463,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1472,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1473,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1474,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1475 ;
    neo:h1 "ZEN FLESH, ZEN BONES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h2 "101 ZEN STORIES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h3 "58. Arresting the Stone Buddha"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:id "b081226dfadc287be27393c0ebf8228c"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_name "1957_-_Paul_Reps_-_Zen_flesh_zen_bones-A_Collection_of_Zen_and_Pre_Zen_Writings_-_Scan_by_OceanofPDF_dot_com_-_local_converter.md"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_slug "zen-flesh-zen-bones"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:paragraph_number 5 ;
    neo:text "When O-oka appeared on the bench he rebuked the boisterous audience. \"What right have you people to appear before the court laughing and joking in this manner? You are in contempt of court and subject to a fine and imprisonment.'"^^xsd:string .

ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1476 a neo:Document ;
    neo:MENTIONS ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1477,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1478,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1479,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1480,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_612 ;
    neo:h1 "ZEN FLESH, ZEN BONES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h2 "101 ZEN STORIES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h3 "58. Arresting the Stone Buddha"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:id "2d146d08f688bf7fb69e0277f31f601a"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_name "1957_-_Paul_Reps_-_Zen_flesh_zen_bones-A_Collection_of_Zen_and_Pre_Zen_Writings_-_Scan_by_OceanofPDF_dot_com_-_local_converter.md"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_slug "zen-flesh-zen-bones"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:paragraph_number 6 ;
    neo:text "The people hastened to apologize. \"I shall have to impose a fine on you,' said the judge,' but I will remit it provided each one of you brings one roll, of cotton goods to the court within three days. Anyone failing to do this will be arrested.'"^^xsd:string .

ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_148 a neo:Document ;
    neo:MENTIONS ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_149,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_150,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_151,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_152,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_153,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_154,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_155,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_156,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_157,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_31 ;
    neo:h1 "ZEN FLESH, ZEN BONES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h2 "101 ZEN STORIES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:id "68ba30b612892145153aa5e33b6ebd80"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_name "1957_-_Paul_Reps_-_Zen_flesh_zen_bones-A_Collection_of_Zen_and_Pre_Zen_Writings_-_Scan_by_OceanofPDF_dot_com_-_local_converter.md"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_slug "zen-flesh-zen-bones"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:paragraph_number 10 ;
    neo:text "The Noh dramas are Zen stories. Zen spirit has come to mean not only peace and understanding, but devotion to art and to work, the rich unfolding of contentment, opening the door to insight, the expression of innate beauty, the intangible charm of incompleteness. Zen carries many meanings, none of them, entirely definable. If they a defined they are not Zen."^^xsd:string .

ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1481 a neo:Document ;
    neo:MENTIONS ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1482,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1483,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_416,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_612 ;
    neo:h1 "ZEN FLESH, ZEN BONES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h2 "101 ZEN STORIES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h3 "58. Arresting the Stone Buddha"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:id "02aa3d356f2bb7697f85d965730b1122"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_name "1957_-_Paul_Reps_-_Zen_flesh_zen_bones-A_Collection_of_Zen_and_Pre_Zen_Writings_-_Scan_by_OceanofPDF_dot_com_-_local_converter.md"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_slug "zen-flesh-zen-bones"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:paragraph_number 7 ;
    neo:text "One of the rolls of cloth, which the people brought, was quickly recognized by the merchant as his own, and thus the thief was easily discovered. The merchant recovered his goods, and the cotton rolls were returned to the people."^^xsd:string .

ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1484 a neo:Document ;
    neo:MENTIONS ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1485,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1486,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1487,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1488,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_630 ;
    neo:h1 "ZEN FLESH, ZEN BONES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h2 "101 ZEN STORIES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h3 "59. Soldiers of Humanity"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:id "829c3dcc79bb61795306877b93817737"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_name "1957_-_Paul_Reps_-_Zen_flesh_zen_bones-A_Collection_of_Zen_and_Pre_Zen_Writings_-_Scan_by_OceanofPDF_dot_com_-_local_converter.md"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_slug "zen-flesh-zen-bones"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:paragraph_number 1 ;
    neo:text "Once a division of the Japanese army was engaged in I sham battle, and some of the officers found it necessary to make their headquarters in Gasan's temple."^^xsd:string .

ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1489 a neo:Document ;
    neo:MENTIONS ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1339,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1487,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1490,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_630 ;
    neo:h1 "ZEN FLESH, ZEN BONES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h2 "101 ZEN STORIES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h3 "59. Soldiers of Humanity"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:id "251d14d5da986b2e3a5daa3687564032"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_name "1957_-_Paul_Reps_-_Zen_flesh_zen_bones-A_Collection_of_Zen_and_Pre_Zen_Writings_-_Scan_by_OceanofPDF_dot_com_-_local_converter.md"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_slug "zen-flesh-zen-bones"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:paragraph_number 2 ;
    neo:text "Gasan told his cook: 'Let the officers have only the same simple fare we eat.'"^^xsd:string .

ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1491 a neo:Document ;
    neo:MENTIONS ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1082,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1492,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_630 ;
    neo:h1 "ZEN FLESH, ZEN BONES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h2 "101 ZEN STORIES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h3 "59. Soldiers of Humanity"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:id "8f97b816f765c8049dfb5b868ded04cf"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_name "1957_-_Paul_Reps_-_Zen_flesh_zen_bones-A_Collection_of_Zen_and_Pre_Zen_Writings_-_Scan_by_OceanofPDF_dot_com_-_local_converter.md"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_slug "zen-flesh-zen-bones"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:paragraph_number 3 ;
    neo:text "This made the army men angry, as they were used to very differential treatment. One came to Gasan and said: 'Who do you think we are? We are soldiers, sacrificing our lives for our country. Why don't you treat us accordingly?'"^^xsd:string .

ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1493 a neo:Document ;
    neo:MENTIONS ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1494,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_165,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_630,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_860 ;
    neo:h1 "ZEN FLESH, ZEN BONES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h2 "101 ZEN STORIES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h3 "59. Soldiers of Humanity"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:id "5dc60ed8c1bd5aa8556036c2921d0bac"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_name "1957_-_Paul_Reps_-_Zen_flesh_zen_bones-A_Collection_of_Zen_and_Pre_Zen_Writings_-_Scan_by_OceanofPDF_dot_com_-_local_converter.md"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_slug "zen-flesh-zen-bones"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:paragraph_number 4 ;
    neo:text "Gasan answered sternly: 'Who do you think we are? We are soldiers of humanity aiming to save all sentient beings.'"^^xsd:string .

ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1495 a neo:Document ;
    neo:MENTIONS ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1444,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1496,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1497,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1498,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_201 ;
    neo:h1 "ZEN FLESH, ZEN BONES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h2 "101 ZEN STORIES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h3 "60. The Tunnel"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:id "6ebf9c1adb81151e34a01f89af507a86"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_name "1957_-_Paul_Reps_-_Zen_flesh_zen_bones-A_Collection_of_Zen_and_Pre_Zen_Writings_-_Scan_by_OceanofPDF_dot_com_-_local_converter.md"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_slug "zen-flesh-zen-bones"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:paragraph_number 1 ;
    neo:text "Zenkai, the son of a samurai, journeyed to Edo and there became the retainer of a high official. He fell in love with the official's wife and was discovered. In self-defense, he slew the official. Then he ran away with the wife."^^xsd:string .

ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1499 a neo:Document ;
    neo:MENTIONS ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1496,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1500,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_213 ;
    neo:h1 "ZEN FLESH, ZEN BONES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h2 "101 ZEN STORIES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h3 "60. The Tunnel"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:id "8893dd792cb3110ad7ae31af7c93921f"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_name "1957_-_Paul_Reps_-_Zen_flesh_zen_bones-A_Collection_of_Zen_and_Pre_Zen_Writings_-_Scan_by_OceanofPDF_dot_com_-_local_converter.md"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_slug "zen-flesh-zen-bones"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:paragraph_number 2 ;
    neo:text "Both of them later became thieves. But the woman was so greedy that Zenkai grew disgusted. Finally, leaving her, he journeyed far away to the province of Buzen, where he became a wandering mendicant."^^xsd:string .

ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_15 a neo:Document ;
    neo:MENTIONS ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_12,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_16,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_17,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_18,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_19,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_20,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_21,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_22,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_7 ;
    neo:h1 "ZEN FLESH, ZEN BONES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h2 "Foreword"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:id "10e9ea4186e58f97955941e9fac7c6ca"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_name "1957_-_Paul_Reps_-_Zen_flesh_zen_bones-A_Collection_of_Zen_and_Pre_Zen_Writings_-_Scan_by_OceanofPDF_dot_com_-_local_converter.md"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_slug "zen-flesh-zen-bones"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:paragraph_number 3 ;
    neo:text "10 Bulls was first published in 1935 by DeVorss and Company, Los Angeles, and subsequently by Ralph R. Phillips, Portland, Oregon. It is a translation from the Chinese of a famous twelfth century commentary upon the stages of awareness leading to enlightenment and is here illustrated by one of Japan's best contemporary woodblock artists."^^xsd:string .

ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1501 a neo:Document ;
    neo:MENTIONS ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1263,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1496,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1502,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1503,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1504,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1505,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1506,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1507 ;
    neo:h1 "ZEN FLESH, ZEN BONES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h2 "101 ZEN STORIES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h3 "60. The Tunnel"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:id "0ecc7cb235b03fd16747fb6b944c5a86"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_name "1957_-_Paul_Reps_-_Zen_flesh_zen_bones-A_Collection_of_Zen_and_Pre_Zen_Writings_-_Scan_by_OceanofPDF_dot_com_-_local_converter.md"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_slug "zen-flesh-zen-bones"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:paragraph_number 3 ;
    neo:text "To atone for his past, Zenkai resolved to accomplish some good deed in his lifetime. Knowing of a dangerous road over a cliff that had caused the death and injury of many persons he resolved to cut a tunnel through the mountains there."^^xsd:string .

ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1508 a neo:Document ;
    neo:MENTIONS ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1496,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1504,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1509,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1510,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1511,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1512,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_587 ;
    neo:h1 "ZEN FLESH, ZEN BONES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h2 "101 ZEN STORIES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h3 "60. The Tunnel"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:id "135ca321377360c903ca077b44ac247f"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_name "1957_-_Paul_Reps_-_Zen_flesh_zen_bones-A_Collection_of_Zen_and_Pre_Zen_Writings_-_Scan_by_OceanofPDF_dot_com_-_local_converter.md"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_slug "zen-flesh-zen-bones"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:paragraph_number 4 ;
    neo:text "Begging food in the daytime, Zenkai worked at night digging his tunnel. When thirty years had gone by, the tunnel was 2,280 feet long, 20, feet high, and 30 feet wide."^^xsd:string .

ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1513 a neo:Document ;
    neo:MENTIONS ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1496,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1514,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1515,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1516 ;
    neo:h1 "ZEN FLESH, ZEN BONES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h2 "101 ZEN STORIES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h3 "60. The Tunnel"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:id "e7eeda9b655d8defe871464160572843"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_name "1957_-_Paul_Reps_-_Zen_flesh_zen_bones-A_Collection_of_Zen_and_Pre_Zen_Writings_-_Scan_by_OceanofPDF_dot_com_-_local_converter.md"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_slug "zen-flesh-zen-bones"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:paragraph_number 5 ;
    neo:text "Two years before the work was completed, the son of the official he had slain, who was a skillful swordsman found Zenkai out and came to kill him in revenge."^^xsd:string .

ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1517 a neo:Document ;
    neo:MENTIONS ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1496,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1518 ;
    neo:h1 "ZEN FLESH, ZEN BONES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h2 "101 ZEN STORIES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h3 "60. The Tunnel"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:id "904a049b598efb9a536273845e2d4296"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_name "1957_-_Paul_Reps_-_Zen_flesh_zen_bones-A_Collection_of_Zen_and_Pre_Zen_Writings_-_Scan_by_OceanofPDF_dot_com_-_local_converter.md"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_slug "zen-flesh-zen-bones"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:paragraph_number 6 ;
    neo:text "'I will give you my life willingly,' said Zenkai. 'Only let me finish this work. On the day it is completed then you may kill me.'"^^xsd:string .

ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1519 a neo:Document ;
    neo:MENTIONS ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1496,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1520,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1521,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1522 ;
    neo:h1 "ZEN FLESH, ZEN BONES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h2 "101 ZEN STORIES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h3 "60. The Tunnel"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:id "df59c8c5906e5ba413970af0848fda0d"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_name "1957_-_Paul_Reps_-_Zen_flesh_zen_bones-A_Collection_of_Zen_and_Pre_Zen_Writings_-_Scan_by_OceanofPDF_dot_com_-_local_converter.md"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_slug "zen-flesh-zen-bones"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:paragraph_number 7 ;
    neo:text "So the son awaited the day. Several months passed and Zenkai kept on digging. The son grew tired of doing nothing and began to help with the digging. After he had helped for more than a year, he came to admire Zenkai's strong will and character."^^xsd:string .

ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1523 a neo:Document ;
    neo:MENTIONS ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1504,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_591 ;
    neo:h1 "ZEN FLESH, ZEN BONES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h2 "101 ZEN STORIES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h3 "60. The Tunnel"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:id "c9e1117d6dc66ef9870f9f3f2896e653"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_name "1957_-_Paul_Reps_-_Zen_flesh_zen_bones-A_Collection_of_Zen_and_Pre_Zen_Writings_-_Scan_by_OceanofPDF_dot_com_-_local_converter.md"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_slug "zen-flesh-zen-bones"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:paragraph_number 8 ;
    neo:text "At last the tunnel was completed and the people could use it and travel in safety."^^xsd:string .

ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1524 a neo:Document ;
    neo:MENTIONS ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1496 ;
    neo:h1 "ZEN FLESH, ZEN BONES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h2 "101 ZEN STORIES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h3 "60. The Tunnel"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:id "3f7e173efddefa7ce2b4d1960c6451a3"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_name "1957_-_Paul_Reps_-_Zen_flesh_zen_bones-A_Collection_of_Zen_and_Pre_Zen_Writings_-_Scan_by_OceanofPDF_dot_com_-_local_converter.md"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_slug "zen-flesh-zen-bones"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:paragraph_number 9 ;
    neo:text "'Now cut off my head,' said Zenkai. 'My work is done.'"^^xsd:string .

ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1525 a neo:Document ;
    neo:MENTIONS ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1526,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_178 ;
    neo:h1 "ZEN FLESH, ZEN BONES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h2 "101 ZEN STORIES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h3 "60. The Tunnel"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:id "638537534a4745d9c137464eb101dee8"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_name "1957_-_Paul_Reps_-_Zen_flesh_zen_bones-A_Collection_of_Zen_and_Pre_Zen_Writings_-_Scan_by_OceanofPDF_dot_com_-_local_converter.md"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_slug "zen-flesh-zen-bones"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:paragraph_number 10 ;
    neo:text "'How can I cut off my own teacher's head?' asked the younger man with tears in his eyes."^^xsd:string .

ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1527 a neo:Document ;
    neo:MENTIONS ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1528,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_199,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_31,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_90 ;
    neo:h1 "ZEN FLESH, ZEN BONES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h2 "101 ZEN STORIES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h3 "61. Gudo and the Emperor"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:id "475b6551ceb2ae42e017d680f91296b6"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_name "1957_-_Paul_Reps_-_Zen_flesh_zen_bones-A_Collection_of_Zen_and_Pre_Zen_Writings_-_Scan_by_OceanofPDF_dot_com_-_local_converter.md"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_slug "zen-flesh-zen-bones"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:paragraph_number 1 ;
    neo:text "The emperor Goyozei was studying Zen under Gudo. He inquired: 'In Zen this very mind is Buddha. Is this correct?'"^^xsd:string .

ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1529 a neo:Document ;
    neo:MENTIONS ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_199 ;
    neo:h1 "ZEN FLESH, ZEN BONES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h2 "101 ZEN STORIES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h3 "61. Gudo and the Emperor"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:id "f137f161c8963a8f8d91f85998095329"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_name "1957_-_Paul_Reps_-_Zen_flesh_zen_bones-A_Collection_of_Zen_and_Pre_Zen_Writings_-_Scan_by_OceanofPDF_dot_com_-_local_converter.md"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_slug "zen-flesh-zen-bones"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:paragraph_number 2 ;
    neo:text "Gudo answered: 'If I say yes, you will think that you understand without understanding. If I say no, I would be contradicting a fact which many understand quite well.'"^^xsd:string .

ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1530 a neo:Document ;
    neo:MENTIONS ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1531,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_199,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_242 ;
    neo:h1 "ZEN FLESH, ZEN BONES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h2 "101 ZEN STORIES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h3 "61. Gudo and the Emperor"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:id "9af3547c8be9eed2f1825eb0f131f140"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_name "1957_-_Paul_Reps_-_Zen_flesh_zen_bones-A_Collection_of_Zen_and_Pre_Zen_Writings_-_Scan_by_OceanofPDF_dot_com_-_local_converter.md"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_slug "zen-flesh-zen-bones"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:paragraph_number 3 ;
    neo:text "On another day the emperor asked Gudo: 'Where does the enlightened man go when he dies?'"^^xsd:string .

ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1532 a neo:Document ;
    neo:MENTIONS ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_199 ;
    neo:h1 "ZEN FLESH, ZEN BONES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h2 "101 ZEN STORIES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h3 "61. Gudo and the Emperor"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:id "42a0a9cc447078911621c7ea16f0dea9"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_name "1957_-_Paul_Reps_-_Zen_flesh_zen_bones-A_Collection_of_Zen_and_Pre_Zen_Writings_-_Scan_by_OceanofPDF_dot_com_-_local_converter.md"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_slug "zen-flesh-zen-bones"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:paragraph_number 4 ;
    neo:text "Gudo answered: 'I know not.'"^^xsd:string .

ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1534 a neo:Document ;
    neo:MENTIONS ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_242 ;
    neo:h1 "ZEN FLESH, ZEN BONES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h2 "101 ZEN STORIES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h3 "61. Gudo and the Emperor"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:id "2cd43cfb40c4b5ea6b18460e88100b36"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_name "1957_-_Paul_Reps_-_Zen_flesh_zen_bones-A_Collection_of_Zen_and_Pre_Zen_Writings_-_Scan_by_OceanofPDF_dot_com_-_local_converter.md"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_slug "zen-flesh-zen-bones"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:paragraph_number 5 ;
    neo:text "'Why don't you know?' asked the emperor."^^xsd:string .

ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1535 a neo:Document ;
    neo:MENTIONS ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1536,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_199 ;
    neo:h1 "ZEN FLESH, ZEN BONES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h2 "101 ZEN STORIES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h3 "61. Gudo and the Emperor"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:id "a266fdce2d1cd4faf7acbe92ee411344"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_name "1957_-_Paul_Reps_-_Zen_flesh_zen_bones-A_Collection_of_Zen_and_Pre_Zen_Writings_-_Scan_by_OceanofPDF_dot_com_-_local_converter.md"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_slug "zen-flesh-zen-bones"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:paragraph_number 6 ;
    neo:text "'Because I have not died yet,' replied Gudo."^^xsd:string .

ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1537 a neo:Document ;
    neo:MENTIONS ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1538,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_199,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_242,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_503 ;
    neo:h1 "ZEN FLESH, ZEN BONES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h2 "101 ZEN STORIES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h3 "61. Gudo and the Emperor"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:id "14cf777f1abbbbfeefa7076eb1da07c9"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_name "1957_-_Paul_Reps_-_Zen_flesh_zen_bones-A_Collection_of_Zen_and_Pre_Zen_Writings_-_Scan_by_OceanofPDF_dot_com_-_local_converter.md"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_slug "zen-flesh-zen-bones"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:paragraph_number 7 ;
    neo:text "The emperor hesitated to inquire further about these things his mind could not grasp. So Gudo beat the floor with his hand as if to awaken him, and the emperor was enlightened!"^^xsd:string .

ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1539 a neo:Document ;
    neo:MENTIONS ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1374,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_199,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_242,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_31 ;
    neo:h1 "ZEN FLESH, ZEN BONES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h2 "101 ZEN STORIES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h3 "61. Gudo and the Emperor"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:id "5da44440b3d91e37049a9baa6519b225"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_name "1957_-_Paul_Reps_-_Zen_flesh_zen_bones-A_Collection_of_Zen_and_Pre_Zen_Writings_-_Scan_by_OceanofPDF_dot_com_-_local_converter.md"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_slug "zen-flesh-zen-bones"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:paragraph_number 8 ;
    neo:text "The emperor respected Zen and old Gudo more than ever after his enlightenment, and he even permitted Gudo to wear his hat in the palace in winter. When Gudo was over eighty he used to fall asleep in the midst of his lecture, and the emperor would quietly retire to another room so his beloved teacher might enjoy the rest his ageing body required."^^xsd:string .

ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1540 a neo:Document ;
    neo:MENTIONS ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1541,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1542,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1543 ;
    neo:h1 "ZEN FLESH, ZEN BONES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h2 "101 ZEN STORIES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h3 "62. In the Hands of Destiny"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:id "3c890d7540a9f9493b1f28d25d078e7e"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_name "1957_-_Paul_Reps_-_Zen_flesh_zen_bones-A_Collection_of_Zen_and_Pre_Zen_Writings_-_Scan_by_OceanofPDF_dot_com_-_local_converter.md"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_slug "zen-flesh-zen-bones"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:paragraph_number 1 ;
    neo:text "A great Japanese warrior named Nobunaga decided to attack the enemy although he had only one tenth the number of men the opposition commanded. He knew that he would win, but his soldiers were in doubt."^^xsd:string .

ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1544 a neo:Document ;
    neo:MENTIONS ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1545,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1546,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1547,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1548,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1549,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1550,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1551,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1552,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_355 ;
    neo:h1 "ZEN FLESH, ZEN BONES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h2 "101 ZEN STORIES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h3 "62. In the Hands of Destiny"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:id "728c1e227883e1b12da7519ff624d976"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_name "1957_-_Paul_Reps_-_Zen_flesh_zen_bones-A_Collection_of_Zen_and_Pre_Zen_Writings_-_Scan_by_OceanofPDF_dot_com_-_local_converter.md"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_slug "zen-flesh-zen-bones"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:paragraph_number 2 ;
    neo:text "On the way he stopped at a Shinto shrine and told his man, 'After I visit the shrine I will toss a coin. If head comes we will win; if tails we will loose. Destiny holds us in her hand.'"^^xsd:string .

ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1553 a neo:Document ;
    neo:MENTIONS ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1541,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1547,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1554,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1555,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1556,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1557,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_227 ;
    neo:h1 "ZEN FLESH, ZEN BONES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h2 "101 ZEN STORIES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h3 "62. In the Hands of Destiny"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:id "2fce229ecc528a5e3b2ec3eed2b74f63"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_name "1957_-_Paul_Reps_-_Zen_flesh_zen_bones-A_Collection_of_Zen_and_Pre_Zen_Writings_-_Scan_by_OceanofPDF_dot_com_-_local_converter.md"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_slug "zen-flesh-zen-bones"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:paragraph_number 3 ;
    neo:text "Nobunaga entered the shrine and offered a silent prayer. He came forth and tossed a coin. Heads appeared. His soldiers were so eager to fight that they won their battle easily."^^xsd:string .

ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1558 a neo:Document ;
    neo:MENTIONS ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1552,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1557,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_333,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_366 ;
    neo:h1 "ZEN FLESH, ZEN BONES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h2 "101 ZEN STORIES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h3 "62. In the Hands of Destiny"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:id "0b4e4c4c23389ab3094124394c74f0b9"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_name "1957_-_Paul_Reps_-_Zen_flesh_zen_bones-A_Collection_of_Zen_and_Pre_Zen_Writings_-_Scan_by_OceanofPDF_dot_com_-_local_converter.md"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_slug "zen-flesh-zen-bones"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:paragraph_number 4 ;
    neo:text "'No one can change the hand of destiny,' his attendant told him after the battle."^^xsd:string .

ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1559 a neo:Document ;
    neo:MENTIONS ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1541,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1547,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1555 ;
    neo:h1 "ZEN FLESH, ZEN BONES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h2 "101 ZEN STORIES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h3 "62. In the Hands of Destiny"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:id "e13c9536ddc2c4e8ae3bd7df12514421"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_name "1957_-_Paul_Reps_-_Zen_flesh_zen_bones-A_Collection_of_Zen_and_Pre_Zen_Writings_-_Scan_by_OceanofPDF_dot_com_-_local_converter.md"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_slug "zen-flesh-zen-bones"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:paragraph_number 5 ;
    neo:text "'Indeed not,' said Nobunaga, showing a coin, which had been doubled, with heads facing either way."^^xsd:string .

ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1561 a neo:Document ;
    neo:MENTIONS ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1005,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1562,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1563,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1564,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1565,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_174,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_305,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_480,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_503,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_630 ;
    neo:h1 "ZEN FLESH, ZEN BONES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h2 "101 ZEN STORIES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h3 "63. Killing"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:id "e3dd33aa1b7d8fbd7f9e936d9253c2a3"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_name "1957_-_Paul_Reps_-_Zen_flesh_zen_bones-A_Collection_of_Zen_and_Pre_Zen_Writings_-_Scan_by_OceanofPDF_dot_com_-_local_converter.md"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_slug "zen-flesh-zen-bones"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:paragraph_number 1 ;
    neo:text "Gasan instructed his adherents one day: 'Those who speak against killing and who desire to spare the live of all conscious beings are right. It is good to protect even animals and insects. But what about those persons who kill time, what about those who are destroying wealth and those who destroy political economy? We should not overlook them. Furthermore, what of the one who preaches without enlightenment? He is killing Buddhism.'"^^xsd:string .

ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1566 a neo:Document ;
    neo:MENTIONS ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1567,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1568,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1569,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1570,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1571,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_605 ;
    neo:h1 "ZEN FLESH, ZEN BONES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h2 "101 ZEN STORIES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h3 "64. Kasan Sweated"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:id "985604a428b4cac7c07d3be6708b52c1"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_name "1957_-_Paul_Reps_-_Zen_flesh_zen_bones-A_Collection_of_Zen_and_Pre_Zen_Writings_-_Scan_by_OceanofPDF_dot_com_-_local_converter.md"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_slug "zen-flesh-zen-bones"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:paragraph_number 1 ;
    neo:text "Kasan was asked to officiate at the funeral of a provincial lord. He had never met lords and nobler before so he was nervous."^^xsd:string .

ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1572 a neo:Document ;
    neo:MENTIONS ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1415,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1567 ;
    neo:h1 "ZEN FLESH, ZEN BONES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h2 "101 ZEN STORIES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h3 "64. Kasan Sweated"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:id "1533aa67e24eaafc5f2775504f9d89ca"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_name "1957_-_Paul_Reps_-_Zen_flesh_zen_bones-A_Collection_of_Zen_and_Pre_Zen_Writings_-_Scan_by_OceanofPDF_dot_com_-_local_converter.md"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_slug "zen-flesh-zen-bones"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:paragraph_number 2 ;
    neo:text "When the ceremony started, Kasan sweated."^^xsd:string .

ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1573 a neo:Document ;
    neo:MENTIONS ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1567,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1574,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1575,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1576,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_428 ;
    neo:h1 "ZEN FLESH, ZEN BONES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h2 "101 ZEN STORIES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h3 "64. Kasan Sweated"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:id "befe5a9d9568415a625515eab3e35e59"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_name "1957_-_Paul_Reps_-_Zen_flesh_zen_bones-A_Collection_of_Zen_and_Pre_Zen_Writings_-_Scan_by_OceanofPDF_dot_com_-_local_converter.md"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_slug "zen-flesh-zen-bones"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:paragraph_number 3 ;
    neo:text "Afterwards, when he had returned, he gathered his pupils together. Kasan confessed that he was not yet qualified to be a teacher for he lacked the sameness of bearing in the world of fame that he possessed in the secluded temple. Then Kasan resigned and became the pupil of another master. Eight years later he returned to his former pupils, enlightened."^^xsd:string .

ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1577 a neo:Document ;
    neo:MENTIONS ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1578,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1579,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_221 ;
    neo:h1 "ZEN FLESH, ZEN BONES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h2 "101 ZEN STORIES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h3 "65. The Subjugation of a Ghost"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:id "ed6b2d273bdc47af5855efc453d90cf1"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_name "1957_-_Paul_Reps_-_Zen_flesh_zen_bones-A_Collection_of_Zen_and_Pre_Zen_Writings_-_Scan_by_OceanofPDF_dot_com_-_local_converter.md"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_slug "zen-flesh-zen-bones"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:paragraph_number 1 ;
    neo:text "A young wife fell sick and was about to die. 'I love you so much,' she told her husband, 'I do not want to leave you. Do not go from me to any other woman. If you do, I will return as a ghost and cause you endless trouble.'"^^xsd:string .

ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_158 a neo:Document ;
    neo:MENTIONS ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_142,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_159,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_160,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_161,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_162,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_163,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_164,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_165,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_166,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_167,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_168,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_169,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_170,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_171,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_172,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_173,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_174,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_175,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_22,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_31,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_40 ;
    neo:h1 "ZEN FLESH, ZEN BONES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h2 "101 ZEN STORIES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:id "faddb565f43a1760ac1ed9e66f08d754"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_name "1957_-_Paul_Reps_-_Zen_flesh_zen_bones-A_Collection_of_Zen_and_Pre_Zen_Writings_-_Scan_by_OceanofPDF_dot_com_-_local_converter.md"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_slug "zen-flesh-zen-bones"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:paragraph_number 11 ;
    neo:text "It has been said that if you have Zen in your life, you have no fear, no doubt, no unnecessary craving, and no extreme emotion. Neither illiberal attitudes nor egotistical actions trouble you. You serve humanity humbly, fulfilling your presence in this world with loving-kindness and observing your passing as a petal falling from a flower. Serene you enjoy life in blissful tranquility. Such is the spirit of Zen, whose venture is thousands of temples in China and Japan, priests and monks, wealth and prestige, and often the very formalism it would itself transcend."^^xsd:string .

ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1580 a neo:Document ;
    neo:MENTIONS ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1581,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_221,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_230 ;
    neo:h1 "ZEN FLESH, ZEN BONES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h2 "101 ZEN STORIES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h3 "65. The Subjugation of a Ghost"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:id "218825b1751a6c3b1837cb1f726e8919"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_name "1957_-_Paul_Reps_-_Zen_flesh_zen_bones-A_Collection_of_Zen_and_Pre_Zen_Writings_-_Scan_by_OceanofPDF_dot_com_-_local_converter.md"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_slug "zen-flesh-zen-bones"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:paragraph_number 2 ;
    neo:text "Soon the wife passed away. The husband respected her last wish for the first three months but then he met another woman and fell in love with her. They became engaged to be married."^^xsd:string .

ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1582 a neo:Document ;
    neo:MENTIONS ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1583,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1584,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1585,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1586,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1587,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1588,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1589,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1590,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_235 ;
    neo:h1 "ZEN FLESH, ZEN BONES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h2 "101 ZEN STORIES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h3 "65. The Subjugation of a Ghost"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:id "02998c50f50b4bfaa22f26fc2df08cf7"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_name "1957_-_Paul_Reps_-_Zen_flesh_zen_bones-A_Collection_of_Zen_and_Pre_Zen_Writings_-_Scan_by_OceanofPDF_dot_com_-_local_converter.md"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_slug "zen-flesh-zen-bones"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:paragraph_number 3 ;
    neo:text "Immediately after the engagement a ghost appeared every night to the man blaming him for not keeping his promise. The ghost was clever too. She told him exactly what had transpired between himself and his new sweetheart. Whenever he gave his fiancée a present the ghost would describe it in detail She would even repeat conversations, and it so annoyed the man that he could not sleep. Someone advised him to take his problem to a Zen master who lived close to the village."^^xsd:string .

ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1591 a neo:Document ;
    neo:MENTIONS ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1592,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1593,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1594,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_76 ;
    neo:h1 "ZEN FLESH, ZEN BONES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h2 "101 ZEN STORIES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h3 "65. The Subjugation of a Ghost"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:id "456c80e88700bb5959fc1ae1f48cd5c8"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_name "1957_-_Paul_Reps_-_Zen_flesh_zen_bones-A_Collection_of_Zen_and_Pre_Zen_Writings_-_Scan_by_OceanofPDF_dot_com_-_local_converter.md"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_slug "zen-flesh-zen-bones"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:paragraph_number 4 ;
    neo:text "At length, in despair, the poor man went to him for help. 'Your former wife became a ghost and knows everything you do,' commented the master. 'Whatever you do or say, whatever you give your beloved she knows. She must be a very wise ghost. Really you should admire such a ghost. The next time she appears, bargain with her. Tell her she knows so much you can hide nothing from her, and that if she will answer you one question, you promise to break your engagement and remain single.'"^^xsd:string .

ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1595 a neo:Document ;
    neo:MENTIONS ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_235,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_329 ;
    neo:h1 "ZEN FLESH, ZEN BONES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h2 "101 ZEN STORIES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h3 "65. The Subjugation of a Ghost"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:id "8447850e00b0174935a0406c3ff20475"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_name "1957_-_Paul_Reps_-_Zen_flesh_zen_bones-A_Collection_of_Zen_and_Pre_Zen_Writings_-_Scan_by_OceanofPDF_dot_com_-_local_converter.md"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_slug "zen-flesh-zen-bones"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:paragraph_number 5 ;
    neo:text "'What is the question I must ask her?' inquired the man."^^xsd:string .

ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1596 a neo:Document ;
    neo:MENTIONS ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1597,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1598,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_261,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_329,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_76 ;
    neo:h1 "ZEN FLESH, ZEN BONES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h2 "101 ZEN STORIES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h3 "65. The Subjugation of a Ghost"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:id "50dd4c59ddc4d3092f5acb50c576c168"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_name "1957_-_Paul_Reps_-_Zen_flesh_zen_bones-A_Collection_of_Zen_and_Pre_Zen_Writings_-_Scan_by_OceanofPDF_dot_com_-_local_converter.md"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_slug "zen-flesh-zen-bones"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:paragraph_number 6 ;
    neo:text "The master replied: Take a large handful of soybeans and ask her exactly how many beans you hold in your hand. If she cannot tell you, you will know she is only figment of your imagination and will trouble you no longer.'"^^xsd:string .

ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1599 a neo:Document ;
    neo:MENTIONS ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1583,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_235,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_267 ;
    neo:h1 "ZEN FLESH, ZEN BONES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h2 "101 ZEN STORIES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h3 "65. The Subjugation of a Ghost"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:id "787f018dac9a5bf42208720993336971"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_name "1957_-_Paul_Reps_-_Zen_flesh_zen_bones-A_Collection_of_Zen_and_Pre_Zen_Writings_-_Scan_by_OceanofPDF_dot_com_-_local_converter.md"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_slug "zen-flesh-zen-bones"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:paragraph_number 7 ;
    neo:text "The next night, when the ghost appeared the man flattered her and told her that she knew everything. 'Indeed,' replied the ghost, 'and I know you went to see that Zen master today."^^xsd:string .

ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1600 a neo:Document ;
    neo:MENTIONS ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1601,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_235 ;
    neo:h1 "ZEN FLESH, ZEN BONES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h2 "101 ZEN STORIES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h3 "65. The Subjugation of a Ghost"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:id "16d57455aa20aa1d8fca48da5c30657c"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_name "1957_-_Paul_Reps_-_Zen_flesh_zen_bones-A_Collection_of_Zen_and_Pre_Zen_Writings_-_Scan_by_OceanofPDF_dot_com_-_local_converter.md"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_slug "zen-flesh-zen-bones"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:paragraph_number 8 ;
    neo:text "'And since you know so much,' demanded the man, 'tell me how many beans I hold in this hand!'"^^xsd:string .

ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1602 a neo:Document ;
    neo:MENTIONS ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1579,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1603 ;
    neo:h1 "ZEN FLESH, ZEN BONES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h2 "101 ZEN STORIES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h3 "65. The Subjugation of a Ghost"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:id "5526533788d091b43e7782af5a00302e"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_name "1957_-_Paul_Reps_-_Zen_flesh_zen_bones-A_Collection_of_Zen_and_Pre_Zen_Writings_-_Scan_by_OceanofPDF_dot_com_-_local_converter.md"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_slug "zen-flesh-zen-bones"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:paragraph_number 9 ;
    neo:text "There was no longer any ghost to answer the question."^^xsd:string .

ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1604 a neo:Document ;
    neo:MENTIONS ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1605,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1606,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_242,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_31 ;
    neo:h1 "ZEN FLESH, ZEN BONES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h2 "101 ZEN STORIES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h3 "66.Children of His Majesty"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:id "b6b811e94378f63dc69535bb4a736177"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_name "1957_-_Paul_Reps_-_Zen_flesh_zen_bones-A_Collection_of_Zen_and_Pre_Zen_Writings_-_Scan_by_OceanofPDF_dot_com_-_local_converter.md"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_slug "zen-flesh-zen-bones"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:paragraph_number 1 ;
    neo:text "Yamaoka Tesshu was a tutor of the emperor. He was also a master of fencing and a profound student of Zen."^^xsd:string .

ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1607 a neo:Document ;
    neo:MENTIONS ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1608,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1609,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1610,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_355,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_603 ;
    neo:h1 "ZEN FLESH, ZEN BONES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h2 "101 ZEN STORIES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h3 "66.Children of His Majesty"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:id "987094c806799657c00670237f89c181"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_name "1957_-_Paul_Reps_-_Zen_flesh_zen_bones-A_Collection_of_Zen_and_Pre_Zen_Writings_-_Scan_by_OceanofPDF_dot_com_-_local_converter.md"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_slug "zen-flesh-zen-bones"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:paragraph_number 2 ;
    neo:text "His home was the abode of vagabonds. He had but one suit of clothes, for they kept him always poor."^^xsd:string .

ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1611 a neo:Document ;
    neo:MENTIONS ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1612,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1613,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_225,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_242 ;
    neo:h1 "ZEN FLESH, ZEN BONES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h2 "101 ZEN STORIES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h3 "66.Children of His Majesty"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:id "24bcb87686cbcf13ad37aa2e2a28b186"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_name "1957_-_Paul_Reps_-_Zen_flesh_zen_bones-A_Collection_of_Zen_and_Pre_Zen_Writings_-_Scan_by_OceanofPDF_dot_com_-_local_converter.md"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_slug "zen-flesh-zen-bones"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:paragraph_number 3 ;
    neo:text "The emperor, observing how worn his garments were, gave Yamaoka some money to buy new ones. The next rime Yamaoka appeared he wore the same old outfit."^^xsd:string .

ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1614 a neo:Document ;
    neo:MENTIONS ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1612,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1615,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_242 ;
    neo:h1 "ZEN FLESH, ZEN BONES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h2 "101 ZEN STORIES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h3 "66.Children of His Majesty"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:id "321ceb11702b2a927741b8f612b6cce5"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_name "1957_-_Paul_Reps_-_Zen_flesh_zen_bones-A_Collection_of_Zen_and_Pre_Zen_Writings_-_Scan_by_OceanofPDF_dot_com_-_local_converter.md"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_slug "zen-flesh-zen-bones"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:paragraph_number 4 ;
    neo:text "'What became of the new clothes, Yamaoka?' asked the emperor."^^xsd:string .

ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1616 a neo:Document ;
    neo:MENTIONS ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1612,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1617,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1618,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_414 ;
    neo:h1 "ZEN FLESH, ZEN BONES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h2 "101 ZEN STORIES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h3 "66.Children of His Majesty"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:id "98c8235f49c72686b0ed17b34883fd27"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_name "1957_-_Paul_Reps_-_Zen_flesh_zen_bones-A_Collection_of_Zen_and_Pre_Zen_Writings_-_Scan_by_OceanofPDF_dot_com_-_local_converter.md"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_slug "zen-flesh-zen-bones"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:paragraph_number 5 ;
    neo:text "'I provided clothes for the children of Your Majesty,' explained Yamaoka."^^xsd:string .

ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1619 a neo:Document ;
    neo:MENTIONS ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1015,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1620,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1621,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1622,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1623,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1624,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_251,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_31,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_333,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_463,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_47,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_899 ;
    neo:h1 "ZEN FLESH, ZEN BONES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h2 "101 ZEN STORIES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h3 "67. What Are You Doing! What Are You Saying!"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:id "9e43d64ea6a199ee5f0a39e402836b98"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_name "1957_-_Paul_Reps_-_Zen_flesh_zen_bones-A_Collection_of_Zen_and_Pre_Zen_Writings_-_Scan_by_OceanofPDF_dot_com_-_local_converter.md"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_slug "zen-flesh-zen-bones"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:paragraph_number 1 ;
    neo:text "In modern times a great deal of nonsense is talked about masters and disciples, and about the inheritance of a master's teaching by favorite pupils, entitling them to pass the truth on to their adherents. Of course Zen should be imparted in this way, from heart to heart, and in the past it was really accomplished. Silence and humility reigned rather than profession and assertion. The one who received such a teaching kept the matter hidden even after twenty years. Not until another discovered through his own need that a real master was at hand was it learned that the teaching had been imparted, and even then the occasion arose quite naturally and the teaching made its way in its own right. Under no circumstance did the teacher ever claim 'I am the successor of So-and-so.' Such a claim would prove quite the contrary"^^xsd:string .

ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1625 a neo:Document ;
    neo:MENTIONS ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1078,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1626,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1627,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_263,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_31 ;
    neo:h1 "ZEN FLESH, ZEN BONES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h2 "101 ZEN STORIES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h3 "67. What Are You Doing! What Are You Saying!"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:id "e393b11611d6ca7639d036fdac077f1e"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_name "1957_-_Paul_Reps_-_Zen_flesh_zen_bones-A_Collection_of_Zen_and_Pre_Zen_Writings_-_Scan_by_OceanofPDF_dot_com_-_local_converter.md"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_slug "zen-flesh-zen-bones"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:paragraph_number 2 ;
    neo:text "The Zen master Mu-nan had only one successor. His name was Shoju. After Shoju had completed his study of Zen. Mu- nan called him into his room. 'I am getting old,' he said, 'and as far as I know Shoju, you are the only one who will carry out this teaching. Here is a book. It has been passed down from master to master for seven generations. I also have added many points according to my understanding. The book is very valuable and I am giving it to you to represent your successor ship.'"^^xsd:string .

ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1628 a neo:Document ;
    neo:MENTIONS ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1078,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1626,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_31 ;
    neo:h1 "ZEN FLESH, ZEN BONES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h2 "101 ZEN STORIES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h3 "67. What Are You Doing! What Are You Saying!"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:id "182ed0d53f4fb57607aa3ccf42ea6dc5"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_name "1957_-_Paul_Reps_-_Zen_flesh_zen_bones-A_Collection_of_Zen_and_Pre_Zen_Writings_-_Scan_by_OceanofPDF_dot_com_-_local_converter.md"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_slug "zen-flesh-zen-bones"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:paragraph_number 3 ;
    neo:text "'If the book is such an important thing, you had better keep it,' Shoju replied.' I received your Zen without writing and am satisfied with it as it is.'"^^xsd:string .

ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1629 a neo:Document ;
    neo:MENTIONS ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1630,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_251,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_263,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_333 ;
    neo:h1 "ZEN FLESH, ZEN BONES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h2 "101 ZEN STORIES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h3 "67. What Are You Doing! What Are You Saying!"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:id "7d1d1788daa6f652b1f9e756ae802f63"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_name "1957_-_Paul_Reps_-_Zen_flesh_zen_bones-A_Collection_of_Zen_and_Pre_Zen_Writings_-_Scan_by_OceanofPDF_dot_com_-_local_converter.md"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_slug "zen-flesh-zen-bones"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:paragraph_number 4 ;
    neo:text "'I know that,' said Mu-nan. 'Even so, this work has been carried from master to master for seven generations, so you may keep it as a symbol of having received the teaching. Here.'"^^xsd:string .

ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1631 a neo:Document ;
    neo:MENTIONS ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1078,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1626,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1632,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1633,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1634 ;
    neo:h1 "ZEN FLESH, ZEN BONES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h2 "101 ZEN STORIES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h3 "67. What Are You Doing! What Are You Saying!"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:id "2ed5ec86b8591dd8933404dd913a1897"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_name "1957_-_Paul_Reps_-_Zen_flesh_zen_bones-A_Collection_of_Zen_and_Pre_Zen_Writings_-_Scan_by_OceanofPDF_dot_com_-_local_converter.md"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_slug "zen-flesh-zen-bones"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:paragraph_number 5 ;
    neo:text "The two happened to be talking before a brazier. The instant Shoju felt the book in his hands he thrust it into the flaming coals. He had no lust for possessions."^^xsd:string .

ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1635 a neo:Document ;
    neo:MENTIONS ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_263 ;
    neo:h1 "ZEN FLESH, ZEN BONES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h2 "101 ZEN STORIES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h3 "67. What Are You Doing! What Are You Saying!"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:id "cf0f7ef6d5b1032f8961b40e04159d70"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_name "1957_-_Paul_Reps_-_Zen_flesh_zen_bones-A_Collection_of_Zen_and_Pre_Zen_Writings_-_Scan_by_OceanofPDF_dot_com_-_local_converter.md"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_slug "zen-flesh-zen-bones"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:paragraph_number 6 ;
    neo:text "Mu-nan who never had been angry before yelled: 'What are you doing!'"^^xsd:string .

ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1637 a neo:Document ;
    neo:MENTIONS ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1626 ;
    neo:h1 "ZEN FLESH, ZEN BONES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h2 "101 ZEN STORIES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h3 "67. What Are You Doing! What Are You Saying!"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:id "4379289f8e8c56f3a32005ec9d31a2a4"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_name "1957_-_Paul_Reps_-_Zen_flesh_zen_bones-A_Collection_of_Zen_and_Pre_Zen_Writings_-_Scan_by_OceanofPDF_dot_com_-_local_converter.md"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_slug "zen-flesh-zen-bones"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:paragraph_number 7 ;
    neo:text "Shoju shouted back: 'What are you saying!'"^^xsd:string .

ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1638 a neo:Document ;
    neo:MENTIONS ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1639,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_22,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_242,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_31,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_40 ;
    neo:h1 "ZEN FLESH, ZEN BONES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h2 "101 ZEN STORIES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h3 "68. One Note of Zen"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:id "9c933fe00927ca6bf1c0889d8cd599b2"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_name "1957_-_Paul_Reps_-_Zen_flesh_zen_bones-A_Collection_of_Zen_and_Pre_Zen_Writings_-_Scan_by_OceanofPDF_dot_com_-_local_converter.md"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_slug "zen-flesh-zen-bones"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:paragraph_number 1 ;
    neo:text "After Kakua visited the emperor he disappeared and no one knew what became of him. He was the first Japanese to study Zen in China, but since he showed nothing of it, save one note, he is not remembered for having brought Zen into his country."^^xsd:string .

ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1640 a neo:Document ;
    neo:MENTIONS ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1639,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1641,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_40,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_410 ;
    neo:h1 "ZEN FLESH, ZEN BONES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h2 "101 ZEN STORIES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h3 "68. One Note of Zen"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:id "c0cc784642d9bcc885fb613fb1685696"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_name "1957_-_Paul_Reps_-_Zen_flesh_zen_bones-A_Collection_of_Zen_and_Pre_Zen_Writings_-_Scan_by_OceanofPDF_dot_com_-_local_converter.md"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_slug "zen-flesh-zen-bones"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:paragraph_number 2 ;
    neo:text "Kakua visited China and accepted the true teaching. He did not travel while he was there. Meditating constantly, he lived on a remote part of a mountain. Whenever people found him and asked him to preach he would say a few words and then move to another part of the mountain where he could be found less easily."^^xsd:string .

ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1642 a neo:Document ;
    neo:MENTIONS ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1639,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_22,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_242,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_31 ;
    neo:h1 "ZEN FLESH, ZEN BONES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h2 "101 ZEN STORIES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h3 "68. One Note of Zen"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:id "a359d4c5877007e0bae85361baa4febd"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_name "1957_-_Paul_Reps_-_Zen_flesh_zen_bones-A_Collection_of_Zen_and_Pre_Zen_Writings_-_Scan_by_OceanofPDF_dot_com_-_local_converter.md"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_slug "zen-flesh-zen-bones"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:paragraph_number 3 ;
    neo:text "The emperor heard about Kakua when he returned to Japan and asked him to preach Zen for his edification and that of his subjects."^^xsd:string .

ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1643 a neo:Document ;
    neo:MENTIONS ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1031,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1639,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1644,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1645,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_200 ;
    neo:h1 "ZEN FLESH, ZEN BONES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h2 "101 ZEN STORIES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h3 "68. One Note of Zen"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:id "9fb27f20ff2d9f1a4d75a28bb46d75ac"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_name "1957_-_Paul_Reps_-_Zen_flesh_zen_bones-A_Collection_of_Zen_and_Pre_Zen_Writings_-_Scan_by_OceanofPDF_dot_com_-_local_converter.md"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_slug "zen-flesh-zen-bones"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:paragraph_number 4 ;
    neo:text "Kakua stood before the emperor in silence. He then produced a flute from the folds of his robe and blew one short note."^^xsd:string .

ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1646 a neo:Document ;
    neo:MENTIONS ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1647,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1648,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_355 ;
    neo:h1 "ZEN FLESH, ZEN BONES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h2 "101 ZEN STORIES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h3 "68. One Note of Zen"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:id "c2454447843aabeb9f5ef774567b3b36"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_name "1957_-_Paul_Reps_-_Zen_flesh_zen_bones-A_Collection_of_Zen_and_Pre_Zen_Writings_-_Scan_by_OceanofPDF_dot_com_-_local_converter.md"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_slug "zen-flesh-zen-bones"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:paragraph_number 5 ;
    neo:text "Bowing politely, he disappeared."^^xsd:string .

ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1649 a neo:Document ;
    neo:MENTIONS ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1339,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1650,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1651,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1652,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1653,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1654,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1655,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1656,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1657,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_267 ;
    neo:h1 "ZEN FLESH, ZEN BONES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h2 "101 ZEN STORIES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h3 "69. Eating the Blame"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:id "9255bd8bb1fa6cec00676dbda2f9dbef"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_name "1957_-_Paul_Reps_-_Zen_flesh_zen_bones-A_Collection_of_Zen_and_Pre_Zen_Writings_-_Scan_by_OceanofPDF_dot_com_-_local_converter.md"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_slug "zen-flesh-zen-bones"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:paragraph_number 1 ;
    neo:text "Circumstances arose one day which delayed preparation of the dinner of a Sate Zen master, Fugai, and his followers. In haste the cook went to the garden with his curved knife and cut off the tops of green vegetables, chopped them together, and made soup, unaware that in his haste he had included a part of a snake in the vegetables."^^xsd:string .

ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1658 a neo:Document ;
    neo:MENTIONS ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1032,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1140,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1339,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1650,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1653,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1659 ;
    neo:h1 "ZEN FLESH, ZEN BONES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h2 "101 ZEN STORIES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h3 "69. Eating the Blame"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:id "bffa9165b1902d4311fb8a214dd4c33f"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_name "1957_-_Paul_Reps_-_Zen_flesh_zen_bones-A_Collection_of_Zen_and_Pre_Zen_Writings_-_Scan_by_OceanofPDF_dot_com_-_local_converter.md"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_slug "zen-flesh-zen-bones"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:paragraph_number 2 ;
    neo:text "The followers of Fugai thought they never had tasted such good soup. But when the master himself found the snake's head in his bowl, he summoned the cook, 'What is this?' he demanded, holding up the head of the snake."^^xsd:string .

ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1660 a neo:Document ;
    neo:MENTIONS ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1661,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1662,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_333 ;
    neo:h1 "ZEN FLESH, ZEN BONES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h2 "101 ZEN STORIES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h3 "69. Eating the Blame"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:id "4311e49a041b16203a379ae59abd4694"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_name "1957_-_Paul_Reps_-_Zen_flesh_zen_bones-A_Collection_of_Zen_and_Pre_Zen_Writings_-_Scan_by_OceanofPDF_dot_com_-_local_converter.md"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_slug "zen-flesh-zen-bones"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:paragraph_number 3 ;
    neo:text "'Oh, thank you, master,' replied the cook, taking the morsel and eating it quickly.'"^^xsd:string .

ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1663 a neo:Document ;
    neo:MENTIONS ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1664,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1665,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_267,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_633,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_7 ;
    neo:h1 "ZEN FLESH, ZEN BONES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h2 "101 ZEN STORIES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h3 "70. The Most Valuable Thing in the World"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:id "fcce99d42b6f6ab269266a1ea47e26c6"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_name "1957_-_Paul_Reps_-_Zen_flesh_zen_bones-A_Collection_of_Zen_and_Pre_Zen_Writings_-_Scan_by_OceanofPDF_dot_com_-_local_converter.md"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_slug "zen-flesh-zen-bones"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:paragraph_number 1 ;
    neo:text "Sozan, a Chinese Zen master, was asked by a student: 'What is the most valuable thing in the world?'"^^xsd:string .

ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1666 a neo:Document ;
    neo:MENTIONS ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1667,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1668,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_76 ;
    neo:h1 "ZEN FLESH, ZEN BONES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h2 "101 ZEN STORIES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h3 "70. The Most Valuable Thing in the World"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:id "ad891a8517e8783b730b25823d058c94"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_name "1957_-_Paul_Reps_-_Zen_flesh_zen_bones-A_Collection_of_Zen_and_Pre_Zen_Writings_-_Scan_by_OceanofPDF_dot_com_-_local_converter.md"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_slug "zen-flesh-zen-bones"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:paragraph_number 2 ;
    neo:text "The master replied: The head of a dead cat.'"^^xsd:string .

ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1669 a neo:Document ;
    neo:MENTIONS ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1668,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1670,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_641 ;
    neo:h1 "ZEN FLESH, ZEN BONES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h2 "101 ZEN STORIES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h3 "70. The Most Valuable Thing in the World"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:id "0f8dca31601cf4ab967245c64f02f83d"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_name "1957_-_Paul_Reps_-_Zen_flesh_zen_bones-A_Collection_of_Zen_and_Pre_Zen_Writings_-_Scan_by_OceanofPDF_dot_com_-_local_converter.md"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_slug "zen-flesh-zen-bones"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:paragraph_number 3 ;
    neo:text "'Why is the head of a dead cat the most valuable thing in the world?' inquired the student."^^xsd:string .

ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1671 a neo:Document ;
    neo:MENTIONS ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1664,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1672 ;
    neo:h1 "ZEN FLESH, ZEN BONES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h2 "101 ZEN STORIES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h3 "70. The Most Valuable Thing in the World"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:id "68cbfe186c5677dafb9fb1544200b2fa"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_name "1957_-_Paul_Reps_-_Zen_flesh_zen_bones-A_Collection_of_Zen_and_Pre_Zen_Writings_-_Scan_by_OceanofPDF_dot_com_-_local_converter.md"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_slug "zen-flesh-zen-bones"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:paragraph_number 4 ;
    neo:text "Sozan replied: 'Because no one can name its price.'"^^xsd:string .

ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1673 a neo:Document ;
    neo:MENTIONS ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_139,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1674,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1675,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1676,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1677,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_22,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_31 ;
    neo:h1 "ZEN FLESH, ZEN BONES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h2 "101 ZEN STORIES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h3 "71. Learning to be Silent"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:id "654ec0886bdb5c14a9bdd0f971d68eaf"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_name "1957_-_Paul_Reps_-_Zen_flesh_zen_bones-A_Collection_of_Zen_and_Pre_Zen_Writings_-_Scan_by_OceanofPDF_dot_com_-_local_converter.md"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_slug "zen-flesh-zen-bones"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:paragraph_number 1 ;
    neo:text "The pupils of the Tendai School used to study meditation before Zen entered Japan. Four of them who were intimate friends promised one another to observe seven days of silence."^^xsd:string .

ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1678 a neo:Document ;
    neo:MENTIONS ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_139,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1679,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1680,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1681,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_399,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_872 ;
    neo:h1 "ZEN FLESH, ZEN BONES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h2 "101 ZEN STORIES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h3 "71. Learning to be Silent"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:id "6eafa3dfb3d6c6960d9e1939bf75b492"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_name "1957_-_Paul_Reps_-_Zen_flesh_zen_bones-A_Collection_of_Zen_and_Pre_Zen_Writings_-_Scan_by_OceanofPDF_dot_com_-_local_converter.md"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_slug "zen-flesh-zen-bones"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:paragraph_number 2 ;
    neo:text "On the first day all were silent Their meditation had begun auspiciously, but when night came and the oil-lamps were growing dim one of the pupils could not help exclaiming to a servant: 'Fix those lamps.'"^^xsd:string .

ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1682 a neo:Document ;
    neo:MENTIONS ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1683,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1684,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1685 ;
    neo:h1 "ZEN FLESH, ZEN BONES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h2 "101 ZEN STORIES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h3 "71. Learning to be Silent"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:id "997d73a60b95cbdfbb08e0871a376b5c"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_name "1957_-_Paul_Reps_-_Zen_flesh_zen_bones-A_Collection_of_Zen_and_Pre_Zen_Writings_-_Scan_by_OceanofPDF_dot_com_-_local_converter.md"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_slug "zen-flesh-zen-bones"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:paragraph_number 3 ;
    neo:text "The second pupil was surprised to hear the first one talk. 'We are not supposed to say a word,' he remarked."^^xsd:string .

ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1686 a neo:Document ;
    neo:MENTIONS ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1687,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1688 ;
    neo:h1 "ZEN FLESH, ZEN BONES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h2 "101 ZEN STORIES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h3 "71. Learning to be Silent"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:id "a3852612928215c9fbe18f0447bb43a8"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_name "1957_-_Paul_Reps_-_Zen_flesh_zen_bones-A_Collection_of_Zen_and_Pre_Zen_Writings_-_Scan_by_OceanofPDF_dot_com_-_local_converter.md"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_slug "zen-flesh-zen-bones"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:paragraph_number 4 ;
    neo:text "'You two are stupid. Why did you talk?' asked the third."^^xsd:string .

ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1689 a neo:Document ;
    neo:MENTIONS ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1690 ;
    neo:h1 "ZEN FLESH, ZEN BONES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h2 "101 ZEN STORIES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h3 "71. Learning to be Silent"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:id "58a70bf6bd13d2b06bb8f550cf261daf"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_name "1957_-_Paul_Reps_-_Zen_flesh_zen_bones-A_Collection_of_Zen_and_Pre_Zen_Writings_-_Scan_by_OceanofPDF_dot_com_-_local_converter.md"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_slug "zen-flesh-zen-bones"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:paragraph_number 5 ;
    neo:text "'I am the only one who has not talked,' muttered the fourth pupil."^^xsd:string .

ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1692 a neo:Document ;
    neo:MENTIONS ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1693,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1694,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_199,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_31 ;
    neo:h1 "ZEN FLESH, ZEN BONES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h2 "101 ZEN STORIES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h3 "72. The Blockhead Lord"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:id "46682e621532a13797b18c43b0ab63e2"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_name "1957_-_Paul_Reps_-_Zen_flesh_zen_bones-A_Collection_of_Zen_and_Pre_Zen_Writings_-_Scan_by_OceanofPDF_dot_com_-_local_converter.md"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_slug "zen-flesh-zen-bones"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:paragraph_number 1 ;
    neo:text "Two Zen teachers Daigu and Gudo, were invited to visit a lord. Upon arriving, Gudo said to the lord: 'You are wise by nature and have an inborn ability to learn Zen.'"^^xsd:string .

ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1695 a neo:Document ;
    neo:MENTIONS ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1693,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1694,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_31 ;
    neo:h1 "ZEN FLESH, ZEN BONES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h2 "101 ZEN STORIES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h3 "72. The Blockhead Lord"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:id "a27b5cb0cfc53e6fd79ef7a9537a9d73"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_name "1957_-_Paul_Reps_-_Zen_flesh_zen_bones-A_Collection_of_Zen_and_Pre_Zen_Writings_-_Scan_by_OceanofPDF_dot_com_-_local_converter.md"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_slug "zen-flesh-zen-bones"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:paragraph_number 2 ;
    neo:text "'Nonsense,' said Daigu 'Why do you flatter this blockheads? He may be a lord, but he doesn't know anything of Zen.'"^^xsd:string .

ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1696 a neo:Document ;
    neo:MENTIONS ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1693,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1697,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_199,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_31,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_391 ;
    neo:h1 "ZEN FLESH, ZEN BONES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h2 "101 ZEN STORIES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h3 "72. The Blockhead Lord"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:id "41b46186e1cbc404f1d763d5f77c259c"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_name "1957_-_Paul_Reps_-_Zen_flesh_zen_bones-A_Collection_of_Zen_and_Pre_Zen_Writings_-_Scan_by_OceanofPDF_dot_com_-_local_converter.md"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_slug "zen-flesh-zen-bones"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:paragraph_number 3 ;
    neo:text "So, instead of building a temple for Gudo the lord built it for Daigu and studied Zen with him."^^xsd:string .

ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1698 a neo:Document ;
    neo:MENTIONS ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1699,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1700,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1701,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1702,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1703,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1704,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1705,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_178,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_31,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_561,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_764 ;
    neo:h1 "ZEN FLESH, ZEN BONES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h2 "101 ZEN STORIES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h3 "73. Ten Successors"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:id "c373cc904e4d031116ba63110262a594"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_name "1957_-_Paul_Reps_-_Zen_flesh_zen_bones-A_Collection_of_Zen_and_Pre_Zen_Writings_-_Scan_by_OceanofPDF_dot_com_-_local_converter.md"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_slug "zen-flesh-zen-bones"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:paragraph_number 1 ;
    neo:text "Zen pupils take a vow that even if they are killed by their teacher, they intend to learn Zen. Usually they cut a finger and seal their resolution with blood. In time the vow has become a men formality, and for this reason the pupil who died by the hand of Ekido was made to appear a martyr. Ekido had become a severe teacher. His pupils feared him. One of them on duty, striking the gong to tell the time of day, missed his beats when his eye was attracted by a beautiful girl passing the temple gate."^^xsd:string .

ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1706 a neo:Document ;
    neo:MENTIONS ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1707,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1708,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_220,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_561 ;
    neo:h1 "ZEN FLESH, ZEN BONES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h2 "101 ZEN STORIES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h3 "73. Ten Successors"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:id "37ce3beda68d1f88275f556ece3523e0"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_name "1957_-_Paul_Reps_-_Zen_flesh_zen_bones-A_Collection_of_Zen_and_Pre_Zen_Writings_-_Scan_by_OceanofPDF_dot_com_-_local_converter.md"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_slug "zen-flesh-zen-bones"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:paragraph_number 2 ;
    neo:text "At that moment Ekido, who was directly behind him, hit him with a stick and the shock happened to kill him."^^xsd:string .

ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1709 a neo:Document ;
    neo:MENTIONS ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1710,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1711,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_561,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_872 ;
    neo:h1 "ZEN FLESH, ZEN BONES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h2 "101 ZEN STORIES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h3 "73. Ten Successors"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:id "97cb2327615b0fe3ea51ceb454414cb0"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_name "1957_-_Paul_Reps_-_Zen_flesh_zen_bones-A_Collection_of_Zen_and_Pre_Zen_Writings_-_Scan_by_OceanofPDF_dot_com_-_local_converter.md"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_slug "zen-flesh-zen-bones"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:paragraph_number 3 ;
    neo:text "The pupil's guardian, hearing of the accident went directly to Ekido. Knowing that he was not to blame he praised the master for his severe teaching. Ekido's attitude was just the same as if the pupil were still alive."^^xsd:string .

ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1712 a neo:Document ;
    neo:MENTIONS ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1713,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_355 ;
    neo:h1 "ZEN FLESH, ZEN BONES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h2 "101 ZEN STORIES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h3 "73. Ten Successors"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:id "63506df761d704f458beae0923d3b0ec"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_name "1957_-_Paul_Reps_-_Zen_flesh_zen_bones-A_Collection_of_Zen_and_Pre_Zen_Writings_-_Scan_by_OceanofPDF_dot_com_-_local_converter.md"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_slug "zen-flesh-zen-bones"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:paragraph_number 4 ;
    neo:text "After this took place, he was able to produce under his guidance more than ten enlightened successors, a very unusual number."^^xsd:string .

ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1714 a neo:Document ;
    neo:MENTIONS ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1715,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1716,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1717,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_31,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_409,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_504 ;
    neo:h1 "ZEN FLESH, ZEN BONES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h2 "101 ZEN STORIES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h3 "74. True Reformation"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:id "82c09ffcbd73348d0ca528f36411ff74"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_name "1957_-_Paul_Reps_-_Zen_flesh_zen_bones-A_Collection_of_Zen_and_Pre_Zen_Writings_-_Scan_by_OceanofPDF_dot_com_-_local_converter.md"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_slug "zen-flesh-zen-bones"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:paragraph_number 1 ;
    neo:text "Ryokan devoted his life to the study of Zen. One day he heard that his nephew, despite the admonitions of relatives, was spending his money on a courtesan. Inasmuch as the nephew had taken Ryokan's place in managing the family estate and the property was in danger of being dissipated, the relatives asked Ryokan to do something about it."^^xsd:string .

ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1718 a neo:Document ;
    neo:MENTIONS ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1715,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_409 ;
    neo:h1 "ZEN FLESH, ZEN BONES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h2 "101 ZEN STORIES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h3 "74. True Reformation"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:id "21b2e4f3c3024c77f59b731c5131a585"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_name "1957_-_Paul_Reps_-_Zen_flesh_zen_bones-A_Collection_of_Zen_and_Pre_Zen_Writings_-_Scan_by_OceanofPDF_dot_com_-_local_converter.md"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_slug "zen-flesh-zen-bones"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:paragraph_number 2 ;
    neo:text "Ryokan had to travel a long way to visit his nephew, whom he had not seen for many years. The nephew seemed pleased to meet his uncle again and invited him to remain overnight."^^xsd:string .

ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1719 a neo:Document ;
    neo:MENTIONS ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_139,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1720,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1721,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_286,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_409 ;
    neo:h1 "ZEN FLESH, ZEN BONES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h2 "101 ZEN STORIES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h3 "74. True Reformation"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:id "c0df4ad25bae35d0957bbe63c49d1886"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_name "1957_-_Paul_Reps_-_Zen_flesh_zen_bones-A_Collection_of_Zen_and_Pre_Zen_Writings_-_Scan_by_OceanofPDF_dot_com_-_local_converter.md"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_slug "zen-flesh-zen-bones"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:paragraph_number 3 ;
    neo:text "All night Ryokan sat in meditation. As he was departing in the morning he said to the young man: 'I must be getting old, my hand shakes so. Will you help me tie the string of my straw sandal?'"^^xsd:string .

ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1722 a neo:Document ;
    neo:MENTIONS ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1715,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_409 ;
    neo:h1 "ZEN FLESH, ZEN BONES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h2 "101 ZEN STORIES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h3 "74. True Reformation"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:id "65febc33d5e35c1bb689bb1d3253c4f1"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_name "1957_-_Paul_Reps_-_Zen_flesh_zen_bones-A_Collection_of_Zen_and_Pre_Zen_Writings_-_Scan_by_OceanofPDF_dot_com_-_local_converter.md"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_slug "zen-flesh-zen-bones"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:paragraph_number 4 ;
    neo:text "The nephew helped him willingly. 'Thank you,' finished Ryokan, 'you see, a man becomes older and feebler day by day."^^xsd:string .

ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1723 a neo:Document ;
    neo:MENTIONS ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1724,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1725,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1726,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1727,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_409 ;
    neo:h1 "ZEN FLESH, ZEN BONES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h2 "101 ZEN STORIES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h3 "74. True Reformation"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:id "a5c0dbb0eeaeaa425365c986baa79f05"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_name "1957_-_Paul_Reps_-_Zen_flesh_zen_bones-A_Collection_of_Zen_and_Pre_Zen_Writings_-_Scan_by_OceanofPDF_dot_com_-_local_converter.md"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_slug "zen-flesh-zen-bones"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:paragraph_number 5 ;
    neo:text "Take good care of yourself.' Then Ryokan left, never mentioning a word about the courtesan or the complaints of the relatives. But, from that morning on, the dissipations of the nephew ended."^^xsd:string .

ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1728 a neo:Document ;
    neo:MENTIONS ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1729,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1730,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_294 ;
    neo:h1 "ZEN FLESH, ZEN BONES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h2 "101 ZEN STORIES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h3 "75. Temper"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:id "5929345b963650bcafeb5076a72fedb6"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_name "1957_-_Paul_Reps_-_Zen_flesh_zen_bones-A_Collection_of_Zen_and_Pre_Zen_Writings_-_Scan_by_OceanofPDF_dot_com_-_local_converter.md"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_slug "zen-flesh-zen-bones"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:paragraph_number 1 ;
    neo:text "A Zen student came to Bankei and complained: 'Master, I have an ungovernable temper. How can I cure it?'"^^xsd:string .

ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1731 a neo:Document ;
    neo:MENTIONS ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_294 ;
    neo:h1 "ZEN FLESH, ZEN BONES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h2 "101 ZEN STORIES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h3 "75. Temper"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:id "231149a80297ead5d08046241d9d295e"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_name "1957_-_Paul_Reps_-_Zen_flesh_zen_bones-A_Collection_of_Zen_and_Pre_Zen_Writings_-_Scan_by_OceanofPDF_dot_com_-_local_converter.md"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_slug "zen-flesh-zen-bones"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:paragraph_number 2 ;
    neo:text "'You have something very strange,' replied Bankei. 'Let me see what you have.'"^^xsd:string .

ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1732 a neo:Document ;
    neo:MENTIONS ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1733,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_370,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_537 ;
    neo:h1 "ZEN FLESH, ZEN BONES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h2 "101 ZEN STORIES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h3 "75. Temper"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:id "ee6c5a273c89017d2a42f73a46b3f89d"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_name "1957_-_Paul_Reps_-_Zen_flesh_zen_bones-A_Collection_of_Zen_and_Pre_Zen_Writings_-_Scan_by_OceanofPDF_dot_com_-_local_converter.md"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_slug "zen-flesh-zen-bones"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:paragraph_number 3 ;
    neo:text "'Just now I cannot show it to you,' replied the other."^^xsd:string .

ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1734 a neo:Document ;
    neo:MENTIONS ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_294 ;
    neo:h1 "ZEN FLESH, ZEN BONES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h2 "101 ZEN STORIES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h3 "75. Temper"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:id "e7bef391c4eddbc9c48545a583fa0a7f"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_name "1957_-_Paul_Reps_-_Zen_flesh_zen_bones-A_Collection_of_Zen_and_Pre_Zen_Writings_-_Scan_by_OceanofPDF_dot_com_-_local_converter.md"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_slug "zen-flesh-zen-bones"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:paragraph_number 4 ;
    neo:text "'When can you show it to me?' asked Bankei."^^xsd:string .

ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1735 a neo:Document ;
    neo:MENTIONS ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_641 ;
    neo:h1 "ZEN FLESH, ZEN BONES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h2 "101 ZEN STORIES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h3 "75. Temper"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:id "71f59359208e406e09de280c1a84eccb"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_name "1957_-_Paul_Reps_-_Zen_flesh_zen_bones-A_Collection_of_Zen_and_Pre_Zen_Writings_-_Scan_by_OceanofPDF_dot_com_-_local_converter.md"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_slug "zen-flesh-zen-bones"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:paragraph_number 5 ;
    neo:text "'It arises unexpectedly,' replied the student."^^xsd:string .

ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1736 a neo:Document ;
    neo:MENTIONS ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1737,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1738,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_177,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_294 ;
    neo:h1 "ZEN FLESH, ZEN BONES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h2 "101 ZEN STORIES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h3 "75. Temper"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:id "421178a95a2ee49961b1b3e7e6c10bbf"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_name "1957_-_Paul_Reps_-_Zen_flesh_zen_bones-A_Collection_of_Zen_and_Pre_Zen_Writings_-_Scan_by_OceanofPDF_dot_com_-_local_converter.md"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_slug "zen-flesh-zen-bones"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:paragraph_number 6 ;
    neo:text "'Then,' concluded Bankei, 'it must not be your own nature. If it were, you could show it to me at any time. When you were born you did not have if and your parents did not give it to you. Think that over.'"^^xsd:string .

ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1739 a neo:Document ;
    neo:MENTIONS ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1740,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1741,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1742,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_844 ;
    neo:h1 "ZEN FLESH, ZEN BONES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h2 "101 ZEN STORIES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h3 "76. The Stone Mind"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:id "fd4430b011a3edce918ed7c2767125bb"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_name "1957_-_Paul_Reps_-_Zen_flesh_zen_bones-A_Collection_of_Zen_and_Pre_Zen_Writings_-_Scan_by_OceanofPDF_dot_com_-_local_converter.md"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_slug "zen-flesh-zen-bones"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:paragraph_number 1 ;
    neo:text "Hogen, a Chinese Zen teacher, lived alone in a small temple in the country. One day four traveling monks appeared and asked if they might make a fire in his yard to warm themselves."^^xsd:string .

ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1743 a neo:Document ;
    neo:MENTIONS ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1052,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1053,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1740,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1744,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1745,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_97 ;
    neo:h1 "ZEN FLESH, ZEN BONES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h2 "101 ZEN STORIES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h3 "76. The Stone Mind"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:id "c9166ccf012dca22bfa893080a7fe346"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_name "1957_-_Paul_Reps_-_Zen_flesh_zen_bones-A_Collection_of_Zen_and_Pre_Zen_Writings_-_Scan_by_OceanofPDF_dot_com_-_local_converter.md"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_slug "zen-flesh-zen-bones"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:paragraph_number 2 ;
    neo:text "While they were building the fire, Hogen heard them arguing about subjectivity and objectivity. He joined them and said: There is a big stone. Do you consider it to be inside or outside your mind?'"^^xsd:string .

ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1746 a neo:Document ;
    neo:MENTIONS ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1747,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1748,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_340,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_548,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_97 ;
    neo:h1 "ZEN FLESH, ZEN BONES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h2 "101 ZEN STORIES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h3 "76. The Stone Mind"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:id "f2d9e32583cc9eb5b99f69face5b7e52"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_name "1957_-_Paul_Reps_-_Zen_flesh_zen_bones-A_Collection_of_Zen_and_Pre_Zen_Writings_-_Scan_by_OceanofPDF_dot_com_-_local_converter.md"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_slug "zen-flesh-zen-bones"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:paragraph_number 3 ;
    neo:text "One of the monks replied: 'From the Buddhist viewpoint everything is an objectification of mind, so I would say that the stone is inside my mind.'"^^xsd:string .

ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1749 a neo:Document ;
    neo:MENTIONS ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1548,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1740,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1747,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_97 ;
    neo:h1 "ZEN FLESH, ZEN BONES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h2 "101 ZEN STORIES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h3 "76. The Stone Mind"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:id "5336af29467c934490bb963bcc1214ec"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_name "1957_-_Paul_Reps_-_Zen_flesh_zen_bones-A_Collection_of_Zen_and_Pre_Zen_Writings_-_Scan_by_OceanofPDF_dot_com_-_local_converter.md"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_slug "zen-flesh-zen-bones"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:paragraph_number 4 ;
    neo:text "'Your head must feel very heavy', observed Hogen. 'if you are carrying around a stone like that in your mind.'"^^xsd:string .

ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1750 a neo:Document ;
    neo:MENTIONS ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1751,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_40,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_520 ;
    neo:h1 "ZEN FLESH, ZEN BONES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h2 "101 ZEN STORIES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h3 "77. No Attachment to Dust"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:id "6149b296375c188f13d135c4aa702637"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_name "1957_-_Paul_Reps_-_Zen_flesh_zen_bones-A_Collection_of_Zen_and_Pre_Zen_Writings_-_Scan_by_OceanofPDF_dot_com_-_local_converter.md"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_slug "zen-flesh-zen-bones"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:paragraph_number 1 ;
    neo:text "Zengetsu, a Chinese master of the T'ang dynasty, wrote the following advice for his pupils:"^^xsd:string .

ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1752 a neo:Document ;
    neo:MENTIONS ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1670,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1729,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1753,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1754,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1755,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1756 ;
    neo:h1 "ZEN FLESH, ZEN BONES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h2 "101 ZEN STORIES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h3 "77. No Attachment to Dust"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:id "e9bd3696980939b440aa16f90bdf65e4"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_name "1957_-_Paul_Reps_-_Zen_flesh_zen_bones-A_Collection_of_Zen_and_Pre_Zen_Writings_-_Scan_by_OceanofPDF_dot_com_-_local_converter.md"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_slug "zen-flesh-zen-bones"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:paragraph_number 2 ;
    neo:text "Living in the world yet not forming attachments to the dust of the world is the way of a true Zen student."^^xsd:string .

ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1757 a neo:Document ;
    neo:MENTIONS ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1758,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1759,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1760,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1761 ;
    neo:h1 "ZEN FLESH, ZEN BONES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h2 "101 ZEN STORIES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h3 "77. No Attachment to Dust"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:id "4a41683c580ed2146b0cabb6e59a1d71"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_name "1957_-_Paul_Reps_-_Zen_flesh_zen_bones-A_Collection_of_Zen_and_Pre_Zen_Writings_-_Scan_by_OceanofPDF_dot_com_-_local_converter.md"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_slug "zen-flesh-zen-bones"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:paragraph_number 3 ;
    neo:text "When witnessing the good action of another encourage yourself to follow his example. Hearing of the mistaken action of another, advise yourself not to emulate it."^^xsd:string .

ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_176 a neo:Document ;
    neo:MENTIONS ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_177,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_178,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_179,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_180,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_181,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_182,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_31 ;
    neo:h1 "ZEN FLESH, ZEN BONES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h2 "101 ZEN STORIES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:id "aab8ffb53a2bca23f967f069d5cbd636"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_name "1957_-_Paul_Reps_-_Zen_flesh_zen_bones-A_Collection_of_Zen_and_Pre_Zen_Writings_-_Scan_by_OceanofPDF_dot_com_-_local_converter.md"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_slug "zen-flesh-zen-bones"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:paragraph_number 12 ;
    neo:text "To study Zen, the flowering of one's nature, is no easy task in any age or civilization. Many teachers, true and false, have purposed to assist others in this accomplishment. It is from innumerable and actual adventures in Zen that these stories have evolved. May the reader in turn realize them in living experience today."^^xsd:string .

ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1762 a neo:Document ;
    neo:MENTIONS ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_141,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1763,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1764,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1765,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1766 ;
    neo:h1 "ZEN FLESH, ZEN BONES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h2 "101 ZEN STORIES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h3 "77. No Attachment to Dust"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:id "8aacd5da8c173815f93e2051b58c4eea"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_name "1957_-_Paul_Reps_-_Zen_flesh_zen_bones-A_Collection_of_Zen_and_Pre_Zen_Writings_-_Scan_by_OceanofPDF_dot_com_-_local_converter.md"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_slug "zen-flesh-zen-bones"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:paragraph_number 4 ;
    neo:text "Even though alone in a dark room, be as if you were facing a noble guest. Express your feelings, but become no more expressive than your true nature."^^xsd:string .

ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1767 a neo:Document ;
    neo:MENTIONS ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1768,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1769,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1770 ;
    neo:h1 "ZEN FLESH, ZEN BONES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h2 "101 ZEN STORIES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h3 "77. No Attachment to Dust"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:id "86f52a01a543c9e3aeeb476e290e09aa"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_name "1957_-_Paul_Reps_-_Zen_flesh_zen_bones-A_Collection_of_Zen_and_Pre_Zen_Writings_-_Scan_by_OceanofPDF_dot_com_-_local_converter.md"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_slug "zen-flesh-zen-bones"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:paragraph_number 5 ;
    neo:text "Poverty is your treasure. Never exchange it for an easy life."^^xsd:string .

ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1771 a neo:Document ;
    neo:MENTIONS ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1772,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1773,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1774 ;
    neo:h1 "ZEN FLESH, ZEN BONES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h2 "101 ZEN STORIES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h3 "77. No Attachment to Dust"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:id "3396392746365fa2589458fa47e9a3a0"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_name "1957_-_Paul_Reps_-_Zen_flesh_zen_bones-A_Collection_of_Zen_and_Pre_Zen_Writings_-_Scan_by_OceanofPDF_dot_com_-_local_converter.md"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_slug "zen-flesh-zen-bones"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:paragraph_number 6 ;
    neo:text "A person may appear a fool and yet not be one. He may only be guarding his wisdom carefully."^^xsd:string .

ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1775 a neo:Document ;
    neo:MENTIONS ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_143,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1776,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1777,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_233,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_433 ;
    neo:h1 "ZEN FLESH, ZEN BONES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h2 "101 ZEN STORIES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h3 "77. No Attachment to Dust"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:id "da882f3fa2d1910af39914ea82c9eb34"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_name "1957_-_Paul_Reps_-_Zen_flesh_zen_bones-A_Collection_of_Zen_and_Pre_Zen_Writings_-_Scan_by_OceanofPDF_dot_com_-_local_converter.md"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_slug "zen-flesh-zen-bones"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:paragraph_number 7 ;
    neo:text "Virtues are the fruit of self-discipline and do not drop from heaven of themselves as does rain or snow."^^xsd:string .

ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1778 a neo:Document ;
    neo:MENTIONS ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1772,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1776,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1779,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_268 ;
    neo:h1 "ZEN FLESH, ZEN BONES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h2 "101 ZEN STORIES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h3 "77. No Attachment to Dust"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:id "0120c998a265e5341d49a961bf609e40"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_name "1957_-_Paul_Reps_-_Zen_flesh_zen_bones-A_Collection_of_Zen_and_Pre_Zen_Writings_-_Scan_by_OceanofPDF_dot_com_-_local_converter.md"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_slug "zen-flesh-zen-bones"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:paragraph_number 8 ;
    neo:text "Modesty is the foundation of all virtues. Let your neighbors discover you before you make yourself known to them."^^xsd:string .

ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1780 a neo:Document ;
    neo:MENTIONS ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1781,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1782,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1783,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1784,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1785,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_87 ;
    neo:h1 "ZEN FLESH, ZEN BONES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h2 "101 ZEN STORIES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h3 "77. No Attachment to Dust"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:id "24e39776833eeb56cf67704c3827f445"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_name "1957_-_Paul_Reps_-_Zen_flesh_zen_bones-A_Collection_of_Zen_and_Pre_Zen_Writings_-_Scan_by_OceanofPDF_dot_com_-_local_converter.md"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_slug "zen-flesh-zen-bones"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:paragraph_number 9 ;
    neo:text "A noble heart never forces itself forward. Its words are a rare gems seldom displayed and of great value."^^xsd:string .

ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1786 a neo:Document ;
    neo:MENTIONS ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1005,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1787,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1788,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1789,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_745 ;
    neo:h1 "ZEN FLESH, ZEN BONES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h2 "101 ZEN STORIES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h3 "77. No Attachment to Dust"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:id "ec9f1376a2f217b9481081ebd0411077"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_name "1957_-_Paul_Reps_-_Zen_flesh_zen_bones-A_Collection_of_Zen_and_Pre_Zen_Writings_-_Scan_by_OceanofPDF_dot_com_-_local_converter.md"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_slug "zen-flesh-zen-bones"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:paragraph_number 10 ;
    neo:text "To a sincere student, every day is a fortunate day. Time passes but he never lags behind. Neither glory nor shame can move him."^^xsd:string .

ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1790 a neo:Document ;
    neo:MENTIONS ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1760,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1791,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1792,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1793,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1794,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1795 ;
    neo:h1 "ZEN FLESH, ZEN BONES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h2 "101 ZEN STORIES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h3 "77. No Attachment to Dust"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:id "30d0e8639a88e3c87c2ed545564b036e"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_name "1957_-_Paul_Reps_-_Zen_flesh_zen_bones-A_Collection_of_Zen_and_Pre_Zen_Writings_-_Scan_by_OceanofPDF_dot_com_-_local_converter.md"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_slug "zen-flesh-zen-bones"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:paragraph_number 11 ;
    neo:text "Censure yourself, never another. Do not discuss right and wrong."^^xsd:string .

ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1796 a neo:Document ;
    neo:MENTIONS ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1793,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1794,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1797,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1798,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1799,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1800,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1801,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1802 ;
    neo:h1 "ZEN FLESH, ZEN BONES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h2 "101 ZEN STORIES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h3 "77. No Attachment to Dust"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:id "adbc896197178211c32bd15483044ca8"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_name "1957_-_Paul_Reps_-_Zen_flesh_zen_bones-A_Collection_of_Zen_and_Pre_Zen_Writings_-_Scan_by_OceanofPDF_dot_com_-_local_converter.md"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_slug "zen-flesh-zen-bones"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:paragraph_number 12 ;
    neo:text "Some things though right, were considered wrong for generations. Since the value of righteousness may be recognized after centuries, there is no need to crave an immediate appreciation."^^xsd:string .

ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1803 a neo:Document ;
    neo:MENTIONS ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_135,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1804,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1805,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1806,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1807,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1808 ;
    neo:h1 "ZEN FLESH, ZEN BONES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h2 "101 ZEN STORIES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h3 "77. No Attachment to Dust"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:id "64e394f9ad0c9d9238b6b45ee3ccde5f"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_name "1957_-_Paul_Reps_-_Zen_flesh_zen_bones-A_Collection_of_Zen_and_Pre_Zen_Writings_-_Scan_by_OceanofPDF_dot_com_-_local_converter.md"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_slug "zen-flesh-zen-bones"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:paragraph_number 13 ;
    neo:text "Live with cause and leave results to the great law of the universe. Pass each day in peaceful contemplation."^^xsd:string .

ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1809 a neo:Document ;
    neo:MENTIONS ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1810,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1811 ;
    neo:h1 "ZEN FLESH, ZEN BONES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h2 "101 ZEN STORIES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h3 "78. Real Prosperity"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:id "74091690cd29e88b554f34c7387d1142"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_name "1957_-_Paul_Reps_-_Zen_flesh_zen_bones-A_Collection_of_Zen_and_Pre_Zen_Writings_-_Scan_by_OceanofPDF_dot_com_-_local_converter.md"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_slug "zen-flesh-zen-bones"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:paragraph_number 1 ;
    neo:text "A rich man asked Sengai to write something for the continued prosperity of his family so that it might be treasured from generation to generation."^^xsd:string .

ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1812 a neo:Document ;
    neo:MENTIONS ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1811,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1813,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1814,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_290,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_610 ;
    neo:h1 "ZEN FLESH, ZEN BONES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h2 "101 ZEN STORIES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h3 "78. Real Prosperity"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:id "3dbcb0f0283659551dcd595f5adb06d5"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_name "1957_-_Paul_Reps_-_Zen_flesh_zen_bones-A_Collection_of_Zen_and_Pre_Zen_Writings_-_Scan_by_OceanofPDF_dot_com_-_local_converter.md"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_slug "zen-flesh-zen-bones"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:paragraph_number 2 ;
    neo:text "Sengai obtained a large sheet of paper and wrote: 'Father dies, son dies, grandson dies.'"^^xsd:string .

ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1815 a neo:Document ;
    neo:MENTIONS ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1810,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_247 ;
    neo:h1 "ZEN FLESH, ZEN BONES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h2 "101 ZEN STORIES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h3 "78. Real Prosperity"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:id "fe75d6ce6fa2cc558183825fc2edffe7"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_name "1957_-_Paul_Reps_-_Zen_flesh_zen_bones-A_Collection_of_Zen_and_Pre_Zen_Writings_-_Scan_by_OceanofPDF_dot_com_-_local_converter.md"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_slug "zen-flesh-zen-bones"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:paragraph_number 3 ;
    neo:text "The rich man became angry. I asked you to write something for the happiness of my family! Why do you make such a joke as this?'"^^xsd:string .

ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1816 a neo:Document ;
    neo:MENTIONS ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1811,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1817,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1818,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1819,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1820,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1821,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_261 ;
    neo:h1 "ZEN FLESH, ZEN BONES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h2 "101 ZEN STORIES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h3 "78. Real Prosperity"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:id "896056f4add9b3ddc950e0103d289ae0"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_name "1957_-_Paul_Reps_-_Zen_flesh_zen_bones-A_Collection_of_Zen_and_Pre_Zen_Writings_-_Scan_by_OceanofPDF_dot_com_-_local_converter.md"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_slug "zen-flesh-zen-bones"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:paragraph_number 4 ;
    neo:text "'No joke is intended,' explained Sengai. 'If before you yourself die your son should die, this would grieve you greatly. If your grandson should pass away before your son, both of you would be broken hearted. If your family, generation after generation, passes away in the order I have named, it will be the natural course of life. I call this real prosperity.'"^^xsd:string .

ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1822 a neo:Document ;
    neo:MENTIONS ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1823,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1824,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1825,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1826,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1827,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1828,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_22 ;
    neo:h1 "ZEN FLESH, ZEN BONES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h2 "101 ZEN STORIES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h3 "79. Incense Burner"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:id "e240860b16a004294a69bf60078bf9e3"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_name "1957_-_Paul_Reps_-_Zen_flesh_zen_bones-A_Collection_of_Zen_and_Pre_Zen_Writings_-_Scan_by_OceanofPDF_dot_com_-_local_converter.md"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_slug "zen-flesh-zen-bones"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:paragraph_number 1 ;
    neo:text "A woman of Nagasaki named Kame was one of the few makers of incense burners in Japan. Such a burner is a work of art to be used only in a tea room or before a family shrine."^^xsd:string .

ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1829 a neo:Document ;
    neo:MENTIONS ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1823,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1830,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1831,
