        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_305,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_31 ;
    neo:h1 "ZEN FLESH, ZEN BONES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h2 "101 ZEN STORIES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h3 "4. Obedience"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:id "ac9cd6c7054732937d0af141c461a609"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_name "1957_-_Paul_Reps_-_Zen_flesh_zen_bones-A_Collection_of_Zen_and_Pre_Zen_Writings_-_Scan_by_OceanofPDF_dot_com_-_local_converter.md"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_slug "zen-flesh-zen-bones"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:paragraph_number 2 ;
    neo:text "His large audiences angered a priest of the Nichiren sect because the adherents had left to hear about Zen. The self-centered Nichiren priest came to the temple determined to debate with Bankei."^^xsd:string .

ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_3016 a neo:Document ;
    neo:MENTIONS ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1548,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_2753,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_2783,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_2985,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_3017,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_3018,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_3019,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_3020,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_3021,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_788 ;
    neo:h1 "ZEN FLESH, ZEN BONES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h2 "10 BULLS"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h3 "3. Perceiving the Bull"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:id "e7a0c9823ffece19207e289f63dfdfca"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_name "1957_-_Paul_Reps_-_Zen_flesh_zen_bones-A_Collection_of_Zen_and_Pre_Zen_Writings_-_Scan_by_OceanofPDF_dot_com_-_local_converter.md"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_slug "zen-flesh-zen-bones"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:paragraph_number 1 ;
    neo:text "I hear the song of the nightingale. The sun is warm, the wind is mild, willows are green along the shore, Here no bull can hide! What artist can draw that massive head, those majestic horns?"^^xsd:string .

ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_3022 a neo:Document ;
    neo:MENTIONS ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1791,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_2771,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_3015,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_3023,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_3024,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_3025,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_3026,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_3027,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_3028 ;
    neo:h1 "ZEN FLESH, ZEN BONES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h2 "10 BULLS"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h3 "3. Perceiving the Bull"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:id "5d3566b31079a83f593448505098a453"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_name "1957_-_Paul_Reps_-_Zen_flesh_zen_bones-A_Collection_of_Zen_and_Pre_Zen_Writings_-_Scan_by_OceanofPDF_dot_com_-_local_converter.md"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_slug "zen-flesh-zen-bones"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:paragraph_number 2 ;
    neo:text "Comment: When one hears the voice, one can sense its source. As soon as the six senses merge, the gate is entered. Wherever one enters one sees the head of the bull! This unity is like salt in water, like color in dyestuff. The slightest thing is not apart from self."^^xsd:string .

ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_3029 a neo:Document ;
    neo:MENTIONS ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_220,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_2641,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_3030,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_3031,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_3032,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_3033,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_3034,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_370 ;
    neo:h1 "ZEN FLESH, ZEN BONES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h2 "10 BULLS"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h3 "4. Catching the Bull"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:id "9e40d721ba6f3be193f4c7c6d2371ba4"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_name "1957_-_Paul_Reps_-_Zen_flesh_zen_bones-A_Collection_of_Zen_and_Pre_Zen_Writings_-_Scan_by_OceanofPDF_dot_com_-_local_converter.md"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_slug "zen-flesh-zen-bones"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:paragraph_number 1 ;
    neo:text "I seize him with a terrific struggle. His great will and power are inexhaustible. He charges to the high plateau far above the cloud-mists, Or in an impenetrable ravine he stands."^^xsd:string .

ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_3035 a neo:Document ;
    neo:MENTIONS ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_1219,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_2993,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_3036,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_3037,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_355,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_370 ;
    neo:h1 "ZEN FLESH, ZEN BONES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h2 "10 BULLS"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h3 "4. Catching the Bull"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:id "9538920a4259f8369b16893bc81aa52d"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_name "1957_-_Paul_Reps_-_Zen_flesh_zen_bones-A_Collection_of_Zen_and_Pre_Zen_Writings_-_Scan_by_OceanofPDF_dot_com_-_local_converter.md"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_slug "zen-flesh-zen-bones"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:paragraph_number 2 ;
    neo:text "Comment: He dwelt in the forest a long time, but I caught him today! Infatuation for scenery interferes with his direction. Longing for sweeter grass, he wanders away. His mind still is stubborn and unbridled. If I wish him to submit, I must raise my whip."^^xsd:string .

ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_3038 a neo:Document ;
    neo:MENTIONS ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_3037,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_3039,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_3040,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_333,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_355 ;
    neo:h1 "ZEN FLESH, ZEN BONES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h2 "10 BULLS"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h3 "5. Taming the Bull"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:id "90566946a89393f49fe721f93aff06bf"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_name "1957_-_Paul_Reps_-_Zen_flesh_zen_bones-A_Collection_of_Zen_and_Pre_Zen_Writings_-_Scan_by_OceanofPDF_dot_com_-_local_converter.md"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_slug "zen-flesh-zen-bones"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:paragraph_number 1 ;
    neo:text "The whip and rope are necessary, Else he might stray off down some dusty road. Being well trained, he becomes naturally gentle. Then, unfettered, he obeys his master."^^xsd:string .

