    neo:h2 "Foreword"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:id "1f48bc2f177c493501432a679755ee3d"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_name "1957_-_Paul_Reps_-_Zen_flesh_zen_bones-A_Collection_of_Zen_and_Pre_Zen_Writings_-_Scan_by_OceanofPDF_dot_com_-_local_converter.md"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_slug "zen-flesh-zen-bones"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:paragraph_number 17 ;
    neo:text "The directness of Zen has led many to believe it stemmed from sources before the time of Buddha, 500 BC. The reader may judge for himself, for he has here for the first time in one book the experiences of Zen, the mind problems, the stages of awareness and a similar teaching predating Zen by centuries."^^xsd:string .

ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_894 a neo:Document ;
    neo:MENTIONS ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_884,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_895,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_896,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_897,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_898,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_899 ;
    neo:h1 "ZEN FLESH, ZEN BONES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h2 "101 ZEN STORIES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h3 "26. Trading Dialogue for Lodging"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:id "de0478c902e0d4762b1c7190cf9e251b"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_name "1957_-_Paul_Reps_-_Zen_flesh_zen_bones-A_Collection_of_Zen_and_Pre_Zen_Writings_-_Scan_by_OceanofPDF_dot_com_-_local_converter.md"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_slug "zen-flesh-zen-bones"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:paragraph_number 3 ;
    neo:text "A wandering monk came and asked for lodging properly challenging them to a debate about the sublime teaching. The elder brother, tired that day from much studying, told the younger one to take his place. 'Go and request the dialogue in silence,' he cautioned."^^xsd:string .

ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_9 a neo:Document ;
    neo:MENTIONS ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_10,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_11,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_12,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_13,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_14,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_6 ;
    neo:h1 "ZEN FLESH, ZEN BONES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h2 "Foreword"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:id "c6001b80456953e4a3258709bd400e9b"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_name "1957_-_Paul_Reps_-_Zen_flesh_zen_bones-A_Collection_of_Zen_and_Pre_Zen_Writings_-_Scan_by_OceanofPDF_dot_com_-_local_converter.md"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_slug "zen-flesh-zen-bones"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:paragraph_number 2 ;
    neo:text "The Gateless Gate was first published in 1934 by John Murray, Los Angeles. It is a collection of problems, called koan that Zen teachers use in guiding their students toward release, first recorded by a Chinese master in the year 1228."^^xsd:string .

ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_900 a neo:Document ;
    neo:MENTIONS ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_227,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_895,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_901,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_902 ;
    neo:h1 "ZEN FLESH, ZEN BONES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h2 "101 ZEN STORIES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h3 "26. Trading Dialogue for Lodging"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:id "c6cac4f80b49f06c05e4c4e9f90b5f54"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_name "1957_-_Paul_Reps_-_Zen_flesh_zen_bones-A_Collection_of_Zen_and_Pre_Zen_Writings_-_Scan_by_OceanofPDF_dot_com_-_local_converter.md"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_slug "zen-flesh-zen-bones"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:paragraph_number 4 ;
    neo:text "So the young monk and the strange went to the shrine and sat down. Shortly afterwards the traveler rose and went in to the elder brother and said: 'Your young brother is a wonderful fellow. He defeated me.'"^^xsd:string .

ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_903 a neo:Document ;
    neo:MENTIONS ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_904,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_905 ;
    neo:h1 "ZEN FLESH, ZEN BONES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h2 "101 ZEN STORIES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h3 "26. Trading Dialogue for Lodging"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:id "35cefd5752234b135f8ef0639e763db1"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_name "1957_-_Paul_Reps_-_Zen_flesh_zen_bones-A_Collection_of_Zen_and_Pre_Zen_Writings_-_Scan_by_OceanofPDF_dot_com_-_local_converter.md"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_slug "zen-flesh-zen-bones"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:paragraph_number 5 ;
    neo:text "'Relate the dialogue to me,' said the elder one."^^xsd:string .

ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_906 a neo:Document ;
    neo:MENTIONS ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_90,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_907,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_908,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_909,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_910,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_911,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_912 ;
    neo:h1 "ZEN FLESH, ZEN BONES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h2 "101 ZEN STORIES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h3 "26. Trading Dialogue for Lodging"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:id "9b4dbefb282691eda7ed3a1ffffc609b"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_name "1957_-_Paul_Reps_-_Zen_flesh_zen_bones-A_Collection_of_Zen_and_Pre_Zen_Writings_-_Scan_by_OceanofPDF_dot_com_-_local_converter.md"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_slug "zen-flesh-zen-bones"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:paragraph_number 6 ;
    neo:text "'Well,' explained the traveler,' first I held up one finger, representing Buddha, the enlightened one. So he held up two fingers, signifying Buddha and his teaching. I held up three fingers representing Buddha, his teaching, and his followers living the harmonious life. Then he shook his clenched fist in my face, indicating that all three come from one realization."^^xsd:string .

ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_913 a neo:Document ;
    neo:MENTIONS ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_355,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_902 ;
    neo:h1 "ZEN FLESH, ZEN BONES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h2 "101 ZEN STORIES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h3 "26. Trading Dialogue for Lodging"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:id "6dde2c4d1778ced979e31c4d70f2ab87"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_name "1957_-_Paul_Reps_-_Zen_flesh_zen_bones-A_Collection_of_Zen_and_Pre_Zen_Writings_-_Scan_by_OceanofPDF_dot_com_-_local_converter.md"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_slug "zen-flesh-zen-bones"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:paragraph_number 7 ;
    neo:text "Thus he won and so I have no right to remain here.' With this, the traveler left."^^xsd:string .

ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_914 a neo:Document ;
    neo:MENTIONS ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_358,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_915,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_916 ;
    neo:h1 "ZEN FLESH, ZEN BONES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h2 "101 ZEN STORIES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h3 "26. Trading Dialogue for Lodging"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:id "7843499d9c9624bc9445e0d6973b8e91"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_name "1957_-_Paul_Reps_-_Zen_flesh_zen_bones-A_Collection_of_Zen_and_Pre_Zen_Writings_-_Scan_by_OceanofPDF_dot_com_-_local_converter.md"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_slug "zen-flesh-zen-bones"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:paragraph_number 8 ;
    neo:text "'Where is that fellow?' asked the younger one, running in to his elder brother."^^xsd:string .

ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_917 a neo:Document ;
    neo:MENTIONS ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_261,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_370,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_918 ;
    neo:h1 "ZEN FLESH, ZEN BONES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h2 "101 ZEN STORIES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h3 "26. Trading Dialogue for Lodging"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:id "c559374de2e5b0bef68e6cdc714e81da"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_name "1957_-_Paul_Reps_-_Zen_flesh_zen_bones-A_Collection_of_Zen_and_Pre_Zen_Writings_-_Scan_by_OceanofPDF_dot_com_-_local_converter.md"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_slug "zen-flesh-zen-bones"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:paragraph_number 9 ;
    neo:text "'I understand you won the debate.'"^^xsd:string .

ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_919 a neo:Document ;
    neo:MENTIONS ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_220,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_370 ;
    neo:h1 "ZEN FLESH, ZEN BONES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h2 "101 ZEN STORIES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h3 "26. Trading Dialogue for Lodging"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:id "a2f4ae9af43ed644c1bd225c8f75f00b"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_name "1957_-_Paul_Reps_-_Zen_flesh_zen_bones-A_Collection_of_Zen_and_Pre_Zen_Writings_-_Scan_by_OceanofPDF_dot_com_-_local_converter.md"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_slug "zen-flesh-zen-bones"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:paragraph_number 10 ;
    neo:text "'Won nothing. I'm going to beat him up.'"^^xsd:string .

ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_920 a neo:Document ;
    neo:MENTIONS ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_904,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_918 ;
    neo:h1 "ZEN FLESH, ZEN BONES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h2 "101 ZEN STORIES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h3 "26. Trading Dialogue for Lodging"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:id "562da738073e9758f74875b4f3688f81"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_name "1957_-_Paul_Reps_-_Zen_flesh_zen_bones-A_Collection_of_Zen_and_Pre_Zen_Writings_-_Scan_by_OceanofPDF_dot_com_-_local_converter.md"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_slug "zen-flesh-zen-bones"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:paragraph_number 11 ;
    neo:text "'Tell me the subject of the debate,' asked the elder one."^^xsd:string .

ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_921 a neo:Document ;
    neo:MENTIONS ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_922,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_923 ;
    neo:h1 "ZEN FLESH, ZEN BONES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h2 "101 ZEN STORIES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h3 "26. Trading Dialogue for Lodging"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:id "792d1216bbeaa725914f330fba267c6b"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_name "1957_-_Paul_Reps_-_Zen_flesh_zen_bones-A_Collection_of_Zen_and_Pre_Zen_Writings_-_Scan_by_OceanofPDF_dot_com_-_local_converter.md"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_slug "zen-flesh-zen-bones"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:paragraph_number 12 ;
    neo:text "'Why, the minute he saw me he held up one finger, insulting me by insinuating that I have only one eye. Since he was a stranger I thought I would be polite to him, so I held up two fingers congratulating him that he her two eyes. Then the impolite wretch held up three fingers, suggesting that between us we only have three eyes. So I got mad and started to punch him, but he ran out and that ended it.'"^^xsd:string .

ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_924 a neo:Document ;
    neo:MENTIONS ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_294,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_925,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_926,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_927,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_928,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_929 ;
    neo:h1 "ZEN FLESH, ZEN BONES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h2 "101 ZEN STORIES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h3 "27. The Voice of Happiness"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:id "9eaa2044f4b83683adb19f08c2c0b396"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_name "1957_-_Paul_Reps_-_Zen_flesh_zen_bones-A_Collection_of_Zen_and_Pre_Zen_Writings_-_Scan_by_OceanofPDF_dot_com_-_local_converter.md"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_slug "zen-flesh-zen-bones"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:paragraph_number 1 ;
    neo:text "After Bankei had passed away, a blind man who lived near the master's temple told a friend: 'Since I am blind, I cannot watch a person's face, so I must judge his character by the sound of his voice. Ordinarily when I hear someone congratulate another upon his happiness or success, I also hear a secret tone of envy. When condolence is expressed for the misfortune of another. I hear pleasure and satisfaction as if the one condoling was really glad there was something left to gain in his own world."^^xsd:string .

ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_930 a neo:Document ;
    neo:MENTIONS ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_294,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_928,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_931,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_932,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_933 ;
    neo:h1 "ZEN FLESH, ZEN BONES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h2 "101 ZEN STORIES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h3 "27. The Voice of Happiness"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:id "0a41517cc25b2caf2efcda4b6c9a841a"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_name "1957_-_Paul_Reps_-_Zen_flesh_zen_bones-A_Collection_of_Zen_and_Pre_Zen_Writings_-_Scan_by_OceanofPDF_dot_com_-_local_converter.md"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_slug "zen-flesh-zen-bones"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:paragraph_number 2 ;
    neo:text "'In all my experience however, Bankei's voice was always sincere. Whenever he expressed happiness, I heard nothing but happiness, and whenever he expressed sorrow, sorrow was all I heard.'"^^xsd:string .

ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_934 a neo:Document ;
    neo:MENTIONS ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_40,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_935,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_936 ;
    neo:h1 "ZEN FLESH, ZEN BONES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h2 "101 ZEN STORIES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h3 "28. Open Your Own Treasure House"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:id "b163c61abe847207c8083d46de5695b0"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_name "1957_-_Paul_Reps_-_Zen_flesh_zen_bones-A_Collection_of_Zen_and_Pre_Zen_Writings_-_Scan_by_OceanofPDF_dot_com_-_local_converter.md"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_slug "zen-flesh-zen-bones"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:paragraph_number 1 ;
    neo:text "Daiju visited the master Baso in China. Baso asked: 'What do you seek?'"^^xsd:string .

ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_937 a neo:Document ;
    neo:MENTIONS ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_503,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_935 ;
    neo:h1 "ZEN FLESH, ZEN BONES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h2 "101 ZEN STORIES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h3 "28. Open Your Own Treasure House"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:id "eaf0d181db33d3d24b9fdb2e63cafe48"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_name "1957_-_Paul_Reps_-_Zen_flesh_zen_bones-A_Collection_of_Zen_and_Pre_Zen_Writings_-_Scan_by_OceanofPDF_dot_com_-_local_converter.md"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_slug "zen-flesh-zen-bones"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:paragraph_number 2 ;
    neo:text "'Enlightenment,' replied Daiju."^^xsd:string .

ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_938 a neo:Document ;
    neo:MENTIONS ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_261,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_936 ;
    neo:h1 "ZEN FLESH, ZEN BONES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h2 "101 ZEN STORIES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h3 "28. Open Your Own Treasure House"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:id "238dfaa30ece56cd9beb32d3560f200c"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_name "1957_-_Paul_Reps_-_Zen_flesh_zen_bones-A_Collection_of_Zen_and_Pre_Zen_Writings_-_Scan_by_OceanofPDF_dot_com_-_local_converter.md"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_slug "zen-flesh-zen-bones"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:paragraph_number 3 ;
    neo:text "'You have your own treasure house. Why do you search outside?' Baso asked."^^xsd:string .

ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_939 a neo:Document ;
    neo:MENTIONS ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_935,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_940 ;
    neo:h1 "ZEN FLESH, ZEN BONES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h2 "101 ZEN STORIES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h3 "28. Open Your Own Treasure House"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:id "1cb5a6d75931bbf8c6e91885acc03a26"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_name "1957_-_Paul_Reps_-_Zen_flesh_zen_bones-A_Collection_of_Zen_and_Pre_Zen_Writings_-_Scan_by_OceanofPDF_dot_com_-_local_converter.md"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_slug "zen-flesh-zen-bones"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:paragraph_number 4 ;
    neo:text "Daiju inquired : 'Where is my treasure house?'"^^xsd:string .

ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_941 a neo:Document ;
    neo:MENTIONS ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_936,
        ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_940 ;
    neo:h1 "ZEN FLESH, ZEN BONES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h2 "101 ZEN STORIES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h3 "28. Open Your Own Treasure House"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:id "084a595c193737df95b30df4c14380a6"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_name "1957_-_Paul_Reps_-_Zen_flesh_zen_bones-A_Collection_of_Zen_and_Pre_Zen_Writings_-_Scan_by_OceanofPDF_dot_com_-_local_converter.md"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_slug "zen-flesh-zen-bones"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:paragraph_number 5 ;
    neo:text "Baso answered: 'What you me asking me is your treasure house.'"^^xsd:string .

ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_942 a neo:Document ;
    neo:MENTIONS ex:node_4_151b43f1_567f_4578_b41f_d18c5e861cad_604,
